Page 1 abacino: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|abbacinō}}

===Etymology===
Possibly formed from {{affix|la|ab-|bacīnum|gloss2=basin}} or {{m|la|bacīnus}}, from {{m|la|baccus||container, vessel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|abacinō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|abacinō}}

# to [[make]] [[blind]], blind, [[remove]] the [[power]] of [[sight]], especially by using a [[red-hot]] iron rod or basin
#* {{quote-text|la|year=1741|author=w:Ludovico Antonio Muratori|title=Antiquitates italicæ medii ævi|volume=4|page=985
|passage=Filios Tancredi abacinavit; filias vero liberas dimiſit.}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+|abacinō}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|make blind}} {{l|la|excaecō}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|en|abacinate}}
* {{desc|it|abbacinare}}

[[Category:la:Vision]]

-------- end text --------
