Page 8 abalieno: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|ab-|t1=from, away from|aliēnō|t2=alienate, estrange}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|abaliēnō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+.p3inf|abaliēnō}}

# to [[make]] [[alien]] from someone, [[alienate]] (from), [[estrange]], make [[hostile]], [[remove]], [[separate]]
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Miles Gloriosus|4|8|11|quote=istuc crucior a viro me tali '''abalienarier'''|trans=I am distracted at this, that I am '''estranged''' from such a man.}}
# {{lb|la|by extension|in general}} to [[dispose]], [[detach]], [[abstract]], separate, remove
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Curculio|1|3|18|quote=nec prohibere quit / nec prohibebit nisi mors meum animum aps te '''abalienaverit'''|trans=He neither can restrain me, nor will he restrain me, unless death should '''separate''' my soul from you.}}
# {{lb|la|legal}} to [[sell]], [[alienate]], [[dispose]] of, [[give up]] [[possession]] of, [[transfer]] by [[sale]]
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|De lege agraria|2|24|64|quote={{...}} idemque agros vectigalis populi Romani '''abalienaret'''|trans={{...}} and also to have power to '''alienate''' the lands of the Roman people from which their revenues are derived;}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+.p3inf|abaliēnō}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|alienate}} {{l|la|abscindō}}, {{l|la|aliēnō}}, {{l|la|dīvellō}}
* {{sense|separate, remove}} {{l|la|abiungō}}, {{l|la|abscindō}}, {{l|la|disiungō}}, {{l|la|dīvellō}}, {{l|la|dīvidō}}, {{l|la|sēgregō}}
* {{sense|transfer by sale}} {{l|la|aliēnō}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|alienate}} {{l|la|faveō}}
* {{sense|separate, remove}} {{l|la|cōnectō}}, {{l|la|iungō}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|la|abaliēnātiō}}
* {{l|la|abaliēnātus}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|la|aliēnō}}
* {{l|la|aliēnus}}
* {{l|la|alius}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|en|abalienate|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fr|abaliéner|bor=1}}
* {{desc|de|abalienieren|bor=1}}
* {{desc|it|abalienare|bor=1}}
* {{desc|pt|abalienar|bor=1}}

