Page 23 abdo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-}}
From {{af|la|ab-|*dere|t2=put/give}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|abdō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|abdō|abdid|abdit}}

# to [[hide]], [[conceal]], [[keep]] [[secret]], [[cover]], [[suppress]], [[sheathe]]
# to [[remove]], [[put away]], [[set]] aside; [[banish]]
# {{lb|la|often with se}} to [[betake]] oneself, [[go away]], go and [[hide]]
#* {{Q|la|Julius Caesar|Bello Gallico|1|12|quote=Eos impeditos et inopinantes adgressus magnam partem eorum concidit; reliqui sese fugae mandarunt atque in proximas silvas '''abdiderunt'''.|trans=Attacking them encumbered with baggage, and not expecting him, he cut to pieces a great part of them; the rest betook themselves to flight, and '''concealed themselves''' in the nearest woods.}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|abdō|abdid|abdit}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|banish}} {{l|la|ablēgō}}, {{l|la|dēpellō}}, {{l|la|eximō}}, {{l|la|expellō}}, {{l|la|exterminō}}, {{l|la|pellō}}, {{l|la|prōiciō}}, {{l|la|relēgō}}, {{l|la|submoveō}}
