Page 24 abduco: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*abdoukō}}. Equivalent to {{affix|la|ab-|gloss1=from, away from|dūcō|gloss2=to lead, conduct, draw, bring forward}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|abdūcō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg|abdūcō}}

# {{lb|la|literally}}
## {{q|in general}} to [[lead]] away or aside, [[take away]], [[bring]] away, [[carry off]]; [[detach]], [[remove]]
##: {{syn|la|abdō|āmandō|āmōlior|āmoveō|aspellō|auferō|dēmoveō|dētrahō|exhauriō|eximō|relēgō|legō|removeō|submoveō|sperno|āvertō|eximō|dēmō}}
##: {{ant|la|addō}}
## {{q|in particular}}:
### to [[take]] (with one) to [[dine]]
### to [[take]] [[aside]]
### to [[carry off]] or [[carry away|away]] [[forcibly]]; [[rob]], [[ravish]]
#: {{syn|la|rapiō|dīripiō|ēripiō|adimō|rapiō|corripiō|auferō|āmoveō|āvertō|tollō|praedor|agō}}
#:# {{lb|la|law}} [[take away]], [[drive away]]
# {{lb|la|figurative}}
## {{q|in general}} to [[lead]] away, [[separate]], [[distinguish]]
## {{q|in particular}}:
### to [[seduce]], [[charm]], [[attract]] or [[entice]] away, [[pervert]]; [[alienate]] from [[fidelity]] or [[allegiance]]
###: {{syn|la|allicefaciō|corrumpō|pelliciō|sēdūcō}}
### to [[withdraw]], [[draw off]], [[hinder]] (from a [[study]], [[pursuit]], [[duty]], etc.)
###: {{syn|la|recēdō}}
### to [[cause]] to [[withdraw]], be [[separated]], [[fall off]] or [[drop out]]; [[divert]]
###: {{syn|la|redūcō}}
### to [[bring down]], [[reduce]], [[degrade]], [[lower]]
###: {{syn|la|attenuō}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|irreg|abdūcō}}

