Page 25 abeo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|la|habeō||pcl|vul|proscribed}}

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|ab-|gloss1=from, away|eō|gloss2=go}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|abeō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg.pass-impers|abeō}}

# to [[depart]], [[go away]], [[go off]], [[exit]]
#: {{syn|la|dīgredior|dēcēdō|facessō|dēficiō|discēdō|cēdō|ēgredior|exeō|ēvādō|eiciō}}
#: {{ant|la|adeō|ingredior|aggredior|adorior|prōcēdō|prōdeō|ineo|intrō|introeō|accēdō|immigrō}}
#* {{Q|la|Gnaeus Naevius|Bellum Punicum|5|thru=7|quote=Ambōrum uxōrēs<br>noctū Troiād exībant capitibus opertīs,<br>flentēs ambae '''abeuntēs''' lacrimīs cum multīs.|t=The wives of both<br>were leaving Troy at night with covered heads,<br>both weeping while '''departing''' with many tears.}}
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Amphitryon|1|3|45|thru=46|quote=MERCURIUS. Eāmus, Amphitruō. Lūcēscit hoc iam. IUPPITER. '''Abī''' prae, Sōsiā;<br>iam egō sequar.|t=MERCURY. Let's go, Amphitryo. Day's breaking already. JUPITER. '''Go''' ahead, Sosia;<br>I'll follow in a moment.}}
#* '''353 {{CE|nodots=yes}} – 431 {{CE|nodots=yes}}''', [[w:Paulinus of Nola|Paulinus of Nola]], ''Poems'' 13.1 in [[w:Corpus Scriptorum Ecclesiasticorum Latinorum|Corpus Scriptorum Ecclesiasticorum Latinorum]] (volume 30), [[w:Wilhelm von Hartel|Wilhelm von Hartel]] (editor), [[w:Vienna|Vienna]] 1866, [https://archive.org/stream/corpusscriptoru25wiengoog#page/n117/mode/1up page 67]:
#*: Tempora temporibus subeunt, '''abit''' et venit aetās.
#*:: Times give way to times, age comes and '''goes'''.
## {{lb|la|with qualifiers}} to [[pass away]]
##* {{Q|la|Cicero|Tusculanae Disputationes|1|30|74|quote=Catō autem sīc '''abiit''' ē vītā, ut causam moriendī nactum sē esse gaudēret.|t=But Cato did '''pass away''' such that he was happy to have found a reason to die.}}
## to [[retire]] from office
##* {{Q|la|Aulus Gellius|Noctes Atticae|7|7|4|quote=Praeterea sī quadrāgintā annōs nāta sacerdōtiō '''abīre''' ac nūbere voluisset, iūs eī potestāsque exaugurandī atque nūbendī facta est mūnificentiae et beneficiī grātiā, quod campum Tiberīnum sīve Mārtium populō condōnāsset.|t=Then, if at the age of forty she wishes to '''retire''' from the [‌[[w:Vestal virgin|Vestal]]] priesthood and marry, the right and power to withdraw is given to her for the sake of the kindness and service of presenting the ''Campus Tiberinus'' or ''[[w:Campus Martius|Campus Martius]]'' to the people.}}
## {{lb|la|astronomy}} to [[set]]
##* '''4 {{CE|nodots=yes}}''', [[w:Germanicus|Germanicus]] (translator), ''Phaenomena'' [[s:la:Aratea (Germanicus)|667-668]] (original author: [[w:Aratus|Aratus]]):
##*: Illa '''abit''' Ōceanō, tōtīus serta Corōnae<br>in caelum redeunt, {{...}}
##*:: She ([[w:Cassiopeia (constellation)|Cassiopeia]]) '''sets''' in the Ocean, the wreaths of the entire [[w:Corona Borealis|Corona]]<br>return to the heavens, {{...}}
# {{lb|la|with {{m|la|in}}}} to [[change]] one's [[nature]]
#* {{Q|la|Livy|Ab urbe condita libri|1|32|2|quote=Inde et cīvibus ōtiī cupidīs et fīnītimīs cīvitātibus facta spēs in avī mōrēs atque īnstitūta rēgem '''abitūrum'''.|t=Hence to the citizens eager for peace and to the neighbouring cities came hope that the king may '''change''' to the character and institutions of his grandfather.}}
## {{lb|la|poetic}} to be [[transform]]ed, [[metamorphose]]d
##* {{Q|la|Ovid|Metamorphoses|1|236|thru=237|quote=In villōs '''abeunt''' vestēs, in crūra lacertī.|t=Clothes '''turn''' to fur, arms to legs.}}
# {{lb|la|Late Latin|Grecism}} {{synonym of|la|eō}} {{defdate|''[[circa|c.]]'' 230 {{CE|nodots=yes}}}}
#* '''''[[circa|c.]]'' 250 {{CE|nodots=yes}}''', [[w:Commodian|Commodian]], ''Carmen Apologeticum'' 1053–1055 in ''[[w:Corpus Scriptorum Ecclesiasticorum Latinorum|Corpus Scriptorum Ecclesiasticorum Latinorum]]'' (volume 15), Bernhard Dombard (editor), [[w:Vienna|Vienna]] 1887, [https://archive.org/stream/corpusscriptoru22wiengoog#page/n221/mode/1up page 187]:
#*: Et sī nōn crēdiderint, in umbrā mortis '''abībunt'''.
#*:: And should they not believe, they shall '''walk''' in the shadow of death.
#* '''4th C. {{CE|nodots=yes}}''', [[w:Saint Jerome|Saint Jerome]], ''[[w:Vulgate|Vulgate]]'', [[w:Psalms|Psalms]] 1:1:
#*: {{quote|la|Beātus vir quī nōn '''abiit''' in cōnsiliō impiōrum, et in viā peccātōrum nōn stetit, et in cathedrā pestilentiae nōn sēdit.
|translation=Blessed is the man who hath not '''walked''' in the counsel of the ungodly, nor stood in the way of sinners, nor sat in the chair of pestilence.}}

====Conjugation====
Irregular conjugation, but similar to [[Appendix:Latin fourth conjugation|fourth conjugation]]. The third principal part is, unlike other derivates of {{m|la|eō}}, never found as **''abīvī''. In forms where the letter I appears consecutively, the syllable is often contracted to a long Ī in every period of the Latin language.
{{la-conj|irreg.pass-impers|abeō}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|la|ē mediō abeō}}

