Page 203 adeo: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|adeō}}

===Etymology 1===
{{affix|la|ad-|gloss1=to, towards|eō|gloss2=there; so much}}

====Adverb====
{{la-adv|adeō|-}}

# [[so]], [[thus]], [[so much]]
#: {{syn|la|tam}}
#* {{Q|la|Publius Terentius Afer|Andria|1|1|92|quote=et voltū, Sōsia, '''adeō''' modestō, '''adeō''' venustō ut nīl suprā.}}
#* {{Q|la|Horace|Epistulae|1|1|39|quote=nēmō '''adeō''' ferus est, ut nōn mītēscere possit, sī modo cultūrae patientem commodet aurem.}}
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|Pro Rabirio perduellionis reo|10|28|quote='''adeō'''ne hospes hujus urbis, '''adeō'''ne ignārus es disciplīnae consvētūdinisque nostrae, ut haec nesciās?}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Eclogae|2|25|quote=nec sum '''adeō''' īnformis: [...]}}
#* {{Q|la|Livy|Ab urbe condita|21|11|1|quote=cum Hannō perōrāsset, nēminī omnium cum eō certare necesse fuit: '''adeō''' prope omnis senātus Hannibalis erat:}}
# {{lb|la|postpositive}} [[just]], [[indeed]], [[precisely]]
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Curculio|5|3|1|quote=argentāriīs male crēdī quī ajunt, nūgās praedicant: nam et bene et male crēdī dīcō; id '''adeo''' hodiē ego expertus sum.}}
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|Pro Caecina|30|87|quote= id '''adeo''', sī placet, consīderāte}}

=====Usage notes=====
The sense "just, indeed, precisely" fulfils a similar role to {{m+|grc|γε}}.

===Etymology 2===
{{affix|la|ad-|gloss1=to, towards|eō|gloss2=go}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|irreg.p3inf|adeō}}
# to [[approach]], [[go]] to
#: {{syn|la|vādō|ambulō|deambulō|cammīnō|obeō|pergō|baetō|eō|gradior|subeō|cēdō|īnferō|aggredior|adorior|ēvehō|incēdō}}
#: {{ant|la|facessō|dēcēdō|discēdō|cēdō|dēficiō|concēdō|inclīnō|recēdō|recipiō|referō}}
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Caesar|Caesar]]|[[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]]|VII, 25|quote=Quod [...] nec facile '''adire''' apertos ad auxiliandum animadvertebant|t=Because [...] they perceived that [our soldiers] being militarily undefended could not easily '''go to''' give assistance}}
# to [[attend]] (a performance)
# to [[undertake]], [[undergo]]
#: {{syn|la|ineō|obeō|sūmō|assūmō}}
# to [[assail]], [[attack]]
#: {{syn|la|invādō|incurrō|impetō|aggredior|īnstō|oppugnō|excurrō|concurrō|occurrō|petō|accēdō|intrō|incēdō|irrumpō|adorior|opprimō|inruō|incidō|accurrō|appetō|arripiō|assiliō|invehō|incessō|lacessō}}
#: {{ant|la|repugnō|resistō|adversor|obversor|obstō|sistō}}
# {{lb|la|reflexive}} to [[present]] (oneself)
# {{lb|la|of inheritance}} to take possession of
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Pliny the Younger|Pliny the Younger]]|[[w:Epistulae (Pliny)|Epistles]]|II|4|quote=''Si pluribus pater tuus vel uni cuilibet alii quam mihi debuisset, fuisset fortasse dubitandum an '''adires''' hereditatem etiam viro gravem.''|trans=If your father had been indebted to more than one person or even to one person other than me, it might be doubtful whether '''you would enter into''' the inheritance, which would be burdensome even for a man.}}

=====Conjugation=====
Irregular, but similar to [[Appendix:Latin fourth conjugation|fourth conjugation]]. The third principal part is most often contracted to {{m|la|adiī}}, but occasionally appears as {{m|la|adīvī}}.
{{la-conj|irreg.p3inf|adeō}}

=====Descendants=====
