Page 249 adhibeo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|la|adibeō|athibeō||in manuscripts}}

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|ad-|habeō|gloss2=have}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|adhibeō|eccl=yes}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2+|adhibeō}}

# {{sense|to extend something toward another}} to [[extend]], [[hold out]]
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Poenulus|5|5|38|thru=39|quote=Quīn '''adhibuistī''', dum istaec loquēre, tympanum?<br>nam tē cinaedum esse arbitror magis quam virum.|trans=Why didn't you '''hold out''' a tambourine while saying this?<br>'cause I think you're more of a catamite than a man.}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Georgicon|3|452|thru=456|quote=Nōn tamen ūlla magis praesēns fortūna labōrum est,<br>quam sī quis ferrō potuit rescindere summum<br>ulceris ōs: alitur vitium vīvitque tegendō,<br>dum medicās '''adhibēre''' manūs ad vulnera pāstor<br>abnegat, et meliōra deōs sedet ōmina poscēns.|trans=However there isn't any success of the efforts more present<br>than if someone could cut with iron the top<br>opening of the ulcer: the problem is nourished and lives by concealment,<br>while the shepherd doesn't allow medical hands to '''hold out'''<br>to the wound, and sits asking the gods for better omens.}}
# {{sense|to apply one's self or devote attention to something}} to [[attend]] (to), [[handle]], [[look after]]
# to [[apply]], [[adopt]], [[employ]]
#: {{syn|la|adoptō|assūmō|sūmō|ūtor|suscipiō|vēscor|ūsūrpō|accipiō|indūcō|ineō|aggredior}}
# to [[summon]], [[call]] upon, [[invite]]
#: {{syn|la|arcesso|invito|accio|excio}}
#* {{Q|la|Juvenal|Satires|2|132|thru=135|quote={{...}}'Officium crās<br>prīmō sōle mihī peragendum in valle Quirīnī.'<br>'Quae causa officiī?' 'Quid quaeris? nūbit amīcus,<br>nec multōs '''adhibet'''.{{...}}|trans={{...}}'A ceremony tomorrow<br>I must attend in the valley of Quirinus at sunrise.'<br>'What's the ceremony for?' 'Why do you want to know? A friend's getting married to a man,<br>and he doesn't '''invite''' too many.'{{...}}}}
# to [[add]]

