Page 257 adimpero: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{af|la|ad-|imperō}}.

Attested in various early documents from the Occitan and Catalan zone.<ref>{{R:FEW|24|142|*adimperare}}</ref> Perhaps the earliest attestation, albeit indirectly via the derived noun {{m|la||adimperamentum}}, dates to 887 CE.<ref>Balari y Jovany, Jose. [1899] 1964. Orígenes históricos de Cataluña. San Cugat del Vallés: Instituto internacional de cultura románica. Page 508.</ref> Appears to have left no descendants outside of the aforementioned region.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Proto-Gallo-Romance}} {{IPA|la|/aˈðempɾo/}}

===Verb===
