Page 483 aestimo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|aestumō}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|itc-ola|aestumāre}}, from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*aistomāō}}, whose origin is {{unc|la|nocap=1}}. Usually explained as {{affix|la|aes|gloss1=copper, bronze|*temos|gloss2=cut}}, so “one who cuts copper”, meaning one in the Roman Republic who mints money. The second element is then from {{der|la|ine-pro|*temh₁-||to cut}}.

However, De Vaan finds this improbable and instead proposes a connection with {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₂eys-||to seek}}, found in {{m|la|aeruscō||to beg}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|aestimō}}

===Verb===
