Page 487 aestuo: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|la|2014|December|15}}

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|aestus|t1=undulating, waving; heat|-ō|id2=denominative}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|aestuō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|aestuō}}

# to be in [[agitation]] or [[violent]] [[commotion]], [[move]] [[to and fro]], [[writhe]], [[rage]], [[toss]], [[boil]] up, [[heave]]
#* {{Q|la|Lucretius|De rerum natura|5|1097|quote=et ramosa tamen cum ventis pulsa vacillans / '''aestuat''' in ramos incumbens arboris arbor|trans=Yet also when a many-branched tree,'' / ''beaten by winds, '''writhes''' swaying to and fro, pressing 'gainst branches of a neighbour tree}}
# {{lb|la|of fire}} to [[burn]], [[blaze]], rage
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Georgicon|4|263|quote={{...}} '''aestuat''' ut clausis rapidus fornacibus ignis|trans={{...}} as the rapacious fire '''blazes''' in a sealed furnace}}
# {{lb|la|of the effect of fire}} to be [[warm]] or [[hot]], [[swelter]], [[glow]], [[burn]]
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Georgicon|1|107|quote={{...}} et cum exustus ager morientibus '''aestuat''' herbis / ecce {{...}}|trans={{...}} and see, when the scorched land '''burns''' with the grasses withering {{...}}}}
# {{lb|la|of water}} to [[rise]] in [[waves]] or [[billows]], [[surge]], [[whirl]], [[seethe]]
#* {{Q|la|Horace|Odes|2|6|4|quote={{...}} ubi Maura semper / '''aestuat''' unda|trans={{...}} and Moorish wave / that '''whirls''' the sand.}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively|of emotions}} to burn with [[desire]], be [[agitated]] or [[excited]], be [[inflamed]], [[fret]]
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|In Verrem|2|2|55|quote=quod ubi auditum est '''aestuare''' illi qui pecuniam dederant|trans=And when this was known, they began to '''fret''' who had paid the money.}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively|of emotions}} to [[vacillate]], [[hesitate]], be in [[doubt]] or [[undecided]]
#* {{Q|la|Quintilian|Institutio Oratoria|10|7|33|quote=sic anceps inter utrumque animus '''aestuat''' {{...}}|trans=''Consequently, the mind will '''waver in doubt''' between the two alternatives'' {{...}}}}

