Page 655 anticipo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*keh₂p-}}
The conjugation suggests this is a denominal verb in {{m|la|-ō|-ō, -āre|id=denominative}} built on some unattested noun or adjective derived from {{prefix|la|ante-|t1=before, in front of}} the verb {{m|la|capiō|t=take}}<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=capiō|page=90}}</ref>, e.g. {{m|la||*anticeps}}; compare {{m|la|mancipō|t=to transfer or sell}} from {{m|la|manceps|t=purchaser, renter; owner}} and {{m|la|participō|t=to partake of, share, participate}} from {{m|la|particeps|t=sharing, partaking}}. Alternatively, it may have been formed directly on the analogy of the preceding verbs without {{m|la||*anticeps}} ever existing as a precursor.<ref>{{cite-journal|author=J. N. Madvig|authorlink=Johan Nicolai Madvig|title=En Sprogbemærkning|journal=Maanedskrift for Litteratur|location=Copenhagen|date=1838|volume=20|pages=409-410|url=https://www.google.com/books/edition/Maanedsskrift_for_litteratur/lUH6PH8ejFAC?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PT38&printsec=frontcover
}}</ref>. 

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|anticipō}}

