===Etymology===
{{word|la|ine|h₂epó}}{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₂wer-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro||*apwerjō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₂epó||off, from}} (whence {{m|la|ab}}) + {{m|ine-pro|*h₂wer-||to cover, shut}} {{suf|ine-pro||*-yeti|alt2=*-ye-|nocat=1}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=aperiō, -īre|page=46}}</ref> Related to {{m|la|operiō||to cover}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|aperiō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|4|aperiō|aperu|apert}}

# {{lb|la|literal}} to [[uncover]], make or [[lay]] [[bare]], [[reveal]], [[clear]]
#: {{syn|la|adaperiō}}
#: {{ant|la|vēlō|dissimulō|occultō|indūcō|operiō|obnūbō|occulō|condō|recondō|verrō|obruō|adoperiō|nūbō|tegō|abdō|abscondō|cooperiō|premō|opprimō|mergō}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|1|681|quote=cum serimus, caelum ventīs '''aperīte''' serēnīs|trans=''When we are sowing, '''you (pl.) clear*''' the sky with fair winds.''<br/>*(In this quotation, the imperative plural '''aperīte''' is invoking the goddesses {{w|Terra}} and {{w|Ceres}}.)}}
# {{lb|la|figurative}} to make [[visible]], [[discover]], [[show]], [[reveal]], [[lay]] [[open]]
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Proverbs|13|16|quote=Astūtus omnia agit cum cōnsiliō: quī autem fatuus est '''aperit''' stultitiam.|trans=''The prudent man doth all things with counsel: but he that is a fool, '''layeth open''' his folly.''<br/>(Douay-Rheims trans., Challoner rev.: '''1752''' CE)}}
# {{lb|la|metaphor}}
## to [[unclose]], [[open]], [[break open]]
##: {{syn|la|adaperiō|patefaciō}}
##: {{ant|la|interclūdō|claudō|inclūdō|arceō|obserō|operiō}}
