Page 717 arceo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₂erk-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*arkeō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₂erk-}}. Cognates include {{cog|xcl|արգել||obstacle}} and {{cog|grc|ἀρκέω}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|arceō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2+|arceō}}

# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[keep off]], [[keep away]], [[ward off]], [[reject]], [[repel]]
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|6|481-482|quote=Quae dea sit? Quārē famulās ā līmine templī<br/>'''arceat''' ('''arcet''' enim) lībaque tosta petat?|trans=Which goddess is she? Why does '''she keep away''' handmaids from the threshold of her temple (indeed '''she keeps''' [them] '''away'''), and asks for toasted cakes?<br/>(''See'': {{w|Mater Matuta}}.)}} 
#* {{Q|la|Juan Luis Vives|De Disciplinis Libri XII|De tradendis disciplinis liber III|year=early 16th century|quote=Ante omnia '''arcendus''' puer ab authore, qui vitium poteſt fovere ac nutrire, quo is laboret : ut libidinoſus ab Ovidio, ſcurrilis a Martiale, maledicus & ſubſanator a Luciano, pronus ad impietatem a Lucretio, & pleriſque philoſophorum, Epicureis potiſſimum. Glorioſulo non multum conferet Cicero, niſi oſtendas {{...}}|t=Above all, a boy '''should be kept off''' from an author that may foster and nourish his vice, as he does his work: and so the lecherous should be kept away from Ovid, the wisecracker from Martial, the slanderous from Lucian, the prone to impiety from Lucretius and most philosophers, especially Epicureans. Cicero does not bring much to the braggart, unless you [go out of your way to] show him {{...}}}}
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[prevent]], [[hinder]]
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[confine]], [[keep]] [[close]]
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[shut up]], [[enclose]]
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[defend]], [[protect]] (from)
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[keep away]], [[take off]], [[move away]], [[alienate]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|2+|arceō}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|ward off}} {{l|la|dīvertō}}, {{l|la|dēviō}}, {{l|la|prōpulsō}}, {{l|la|āvertō}}, {{l|la|dēclīnō}}, {{l|la|dēflectō}}, {{l|la|flectō}}, {{l|la|āspernor}}, {{l|la|dēmoveō}}
* {{sense|prevent}} {{l|la|retineō}}, {{l|la|dētineō}}, {{l|la|prohibeō}}, {{l|la|impediō}}, {{l|la|sistō}}, {{l|la|resistō}}, {{l|la|exclūdō}}, {{l|la|supprimō}}, {{l|la|moror}}, {{l|la|refrēnō}}, {{l|la|cohibeō}}, {{l|la|cū̆nctor}}, {{l|la|obstō}}, {{l|la|saepiō}}, {{l|la|comprimō}}, {{l|la|intersaepiō}}, {{l|la|interclūdō}}, {{l|la|perimō}}, {{l|la|obstruō}}, {{l|la|obstō}}, {{l|la|officiō}}, {{l|la|reprimō}}, {{l|la|premō}}
* {{sense|shut up}} {{l|la|inclūdō}}, {{l|la|claudō}}, {{l|la|obserō}}
