Page 732 arguo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₂erǵ-}}
Often taken to be a denominative verb 'to make bright, enlighten' to {{der|la|itc-pro|*argu-||bright}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₂érǵus||white}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₂erǵ-}}. Thus cognate with Ancient Greek {{m|grc|ἄργυρος}} and {{cog|hit||tr=ḫarki-||bright, white}}. If so, compare {{cog|en|declare|lit=to make clear}} for the sense development.

Duchesne-Guillemin, Laroche and Melchert reject the above etymology and instead compare ''arguo'' with the semantically better-fitting Hittite {{m|hit||tr=arkuwā(i)-||state one's case, make a plea}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|arguō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|arguō|argu|argūt}}

# {{sense|to make clear to the mind}} to [[clarify]], to [[make]] [[plain]]; to [[assert]], [[declare]], [[prove]], [[show]]
#: {{syn|la|affirmō|firmō|contendō|aiō|fīgō}}
# to [[reprove]], [[accuse]], [[charge]] with
#: {{syn|la|accūsō|condemnō|crīminor|compellō|obloquor|obiectō|corripiō|arripiō|pulsō|incūsō|arcessō}}
#* ''[[w:Vulgate|Vulgate]]''; ''[[w:Book of Proverbs|Prōverbia]]'', 9:8
#*: Nōlī '''arguere''' dērīsōrem nē ōderit tē '''argue''' sapientem et dīliget tē.
#*:: ''Translation from American Standard Version:''
#*::: '''Reprove''' not a scoffer, lest he hate thee: '''Reprove''' a wise man, and he will love thee.
# to [[blame]], [[censure]]
#: {{syn|la|obiūrgō|castīgō|perstringō|īnsector|corripiō|exprobrō|accūsō|incūsō|damnō|obloquor|acclāmō|inclāmō|increpō|animadvertō|reprehendō|compellō}}
# to [[denounce]] as false

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|arguō|argu|argūt}}

