Page 841 audeo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{af|la|avidus|t1=greedy|-eō|pos2=stative suffix}}, hence originally meaning {{m-g|to be greedy}}, as also evidenced by the form {{m|la|sōdēs|t=if you please}} < *{{m|la|[[sī]] [[audēs]]|lit=if you want very much}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|audeō|pages=60–61}}</ref> For the supine {{m|la|ausum}} compare also {{m|la|ārdeō}} : {{m|la|ārsum}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|audeō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2.opt-semi-depon|audeō|aus|aus}}

# to [[dare]], [[venture]], [[risk]]
#: {{syn|la|perīclitor}}
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|Catiline|Oratio in Catilinam Prima in Senatu Habita|1|quote=Quam diū quisquam erit quī tē dēfendēre '''audeat''', vīvēs, et vīvēs ita ut nunc vīvis, multīs meīs et firmīs praesidiīs obsessus nē commōvēre tē contrā rem pūblicam possīs. Multōrum tē etiam oculī et aurēs nōn sentientem, sīcut adhūc fēcērunt, speculābuntur atque custōdient.|trans=As long as one person exists who can '''dare''' to defend you, you shall live; but you shall live as you do now, surrounded by my many and trusty guards, so that you shall not be able to stir one finger against the republic: many eyes and ears shall still observe and watch you, as they have hitherto done, though you shall not perceive them.}}
#* {{Q|la|Horace|Epistles|1|40|quote=Sapere '''audē'''.|trans='''Dare''' to be wise.}}
# {{lb|la|poetic}} to be [[eager]] for [[battle]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|2.opt-semi-depon.sigm|audeō|aus|aus|aus}}

