===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*bʰer-|*telh₂-|id2=bear}}
From {{affix|la|ab-|gloss1=from, away, off|ferō|gloss2=to bear, carry, bring}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|auferō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg|auferō|abs|ab}}

# {{lb|la|literally}} to [[take away]], [[take off]], [[bear away]], [[bear off]], [[carry off]], [[remove]], [[withdraw]]
## {{lb|la|usually|poetic}} {{q|of [[body|bodies]]}} to [[bear away|bear]] or [[carry away]], [[sweep away]] by [[wing]]s, the [[wind]]s, [[wave]]s, or any other [[quick]] [[motion]]; [[waft]] away, sweep away
## {{lb|la|figurative}} to [[carry away]], [[mislead]], [[deceive]]
# {{q|especially}}:
## to [[take away|take]] or [[snatch]] away; [[take]] by [[force]], [[remove]], take away [[violently]], [[abduct]], [[rob]], [[steal]], [[snatch]], [[confiscate]]
##: {{syn|la|rapiō|abdūcō|dīripiō|ēripiō|adimō|exhauriō|fraudō|corripiō|āvertō|tollō|āmoveō|praedor|eximō|legō|agō}}
##: {{uxi|la|'''auferre''' {{l|la|aliquid}} {{l|la|ab}} {{l|la|aliquo}}|t=to '''steal''' something from someone}}
##: {{uxi|la|{{l|la|alicui}} {{l|la|caput}} '''auferre'''|t=to behead someone}}
### {{lb|la|poetic}} to [[take off]] or [[take away|away]], [[destroy]], [[kill]], [[slay]], [[consume]]
### to [[separate]], [[sever]], [[divide]] {{q|of [[place]]s}}
## to [[lay aside]] (some [[action]], [[manner]] of [[speaking]], etc.); [[cease]] from, [[desist]] from, [[leave off]]
##: {{uxi|la|{{l|la|coeptos}} '''auferte''' {{l|la|labores}}|t='''lay aside''' the works that have been started}}
## {{lb|la|metonymic}} {{q|[[effect]] for [[cause]]}} to [[carry off]] (as the [[fruit]] or [[result]] of one's [[labor]], [[exertion]]s, [[error]]s, etc.); [[obtain]], [[gain]], [[get]], [[receive]], [[acquire]]
### {{lb|la|figurative}} to [[carry away]] (the [[knowledge]] of a thing); [[learn]], [[understand]]
# to [[banish]], [[dispel]]
#: {{syn|la|expellō|exsulō|āmoveō|exportō|ēiciō|ablēgō|eximō|fugō|pellō}}

