===Etymology===
{{unk|la}}. Perhaps from {{bor|la|cel-gau|-}} or {{bor|la|gem}}, ultimately either from {{der|la|ine-pro|*bʰedʰ-||to stab, dig}}, or a separate root {{m|ine-pro|*bʰat-||to hit}}; ultimately {{onomatopoeic|la|nocap=1}}.  Compare {{cog|cy|bathu|t=beat}}; {{cog|ang|beadu|t=battle}}. {{dbt|la|battō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|battuō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|battuō|battu}}

# {{lb|la|very rare}} to [[beat]], [[hit]], [[pound]], [[beat up]], [[strike]]
#* {{Q|la|Plaut.|Cas.|2|8|60}}
#* {{Q|la|Marc. Emp.|Medic.|36}}
#* {{Q|la||Apic.|4|2|108}}
# to [[fence]], play [[fencing]]; to [[fight]]
#* {{Q|la|Suet.||Calig|54}}
#* {{Q|la|Cic.|Fam.|9|22|4}}
# to [[bang]] {{gloss|[[have sex]] with}}
#* {{rfq|la}}

====Inflection====
{{la-conj|3|battuō|battu}}

====Derived terms====
