===Etymology 1===
{{onomatopoeic|la}}, compare {{cog|grc|βύας}}, {{cog|bg|буч}}, {{cog|xcl|բու}}, {{cog|fa|بوم|tr=bum}}, {{cog|ar|بُوم}}, {{cog|syc|ܒܐܘܐ|tr=baʾwāʾ}} and Caucasian languages such as {{cog|oge|ბუვი}}, {{cog|ce|бухӏа}}, and {{cog|agx|бу́гьу}}, all meaning owls.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|la|būfus||Late Latin}}
* {{alter|la|*gūfus||Vulgar Latin}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|būbō}}

====Noun====
{{la-noun|būbō<3>|g=m}}

# [[owl]], especially the [[Eurasian eagle owl]], ''[[Bubo bubo]]''

=====Usage notes=====
Nearly always masculine, but used once as a feminine noun by [[w:Virgil|Virgil]] in ''[[s:la:Aeneis|Aeneis]]'' IV:462:
: hinc exaudiri voces et verba vocantis
: visa viri, nox cum terras obscura teneret,
: solaque culminibus ferali carmine bubo
: saepe queri et longas in fletum ducere voces;

=====Declension=====
{{la-ndecl|būbō<3>}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|la|būbulō}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|mul|''{{ll|mul|Bubo}}''}}

