Page 968 caligo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Formation from an earlier adjective is possible, similarly to several similar nouns in {{m|la|-īgō}}, examples at {{m|la|rōbīgō||}}, with the verb deriving from the noun, as {{affix|la|cālīgō|-ō|pos1=noun|id2=denominative}}. A possible reading in [[:w:Pacuvius|Pacuvius]] suggests earlier verb semantics as “I make dark”, consistent with this construction. Possibly from {{der|la|ine-pro|*kel-|t=dark spot}}, suggested to be connected to {{m|la|columba|t=dove, pigeon}}, {{cog|sa|कलङ्क|t=dark blemish}}, {{cog|sh|kal|kâl}} / {{m|sh|ка̑л|tr="mud, dirt"|sc=Cyrl}}.<ref>{{R:es:Roberts:2014}}</ref><ref>{{R:ine:IEW|547-548}}</ref><ref>{{R:cel:EDPC|head=kalyo|pages=186}}</ref> Various further Indo-European cognates have been suggested, such as {{cog|grc|κελαινός||dark, black}}, {{cog|grc|κηλίς||spot, stain}} and the rare adjective {{cog|la|cā̆lidus||having a white spot on the forehead}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|cālīgō}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|cālīgō<3>|g=f}}

# [[fog]], [[mist]], [[vapor]]
# [[darkness]], [[gloom]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} inability to [[perceive]] mentally

====Declension====
{{la-ndecl|cālīgō<3>}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|fog, mist}} {{l|la|nebula}}

