{{la-verb|1+|canōnizō}} {{tlb|la|Medieval Latin|Ecclesiastical Latin}}

# to [[canonize]] {{gloss|recognize as a [[saint]]}}
#* {{quote-book|la|year=13th century|author=Anonymous|chapter=Cronica Minor Minoritae Erphordensis|year_published=1899|title=Monumenta Erphesfurtensia Saec. XII. XIII. XIV.|page=648|url=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=IKRLAQAAMAAJ&dq=%22quod%20nullus%20novus%20sanctus%20in%20veneratione%22&pg=RA1-PA648#v=onepage&f=false|text=Hic papa Innocentius {{...}} statuit {{...}} quod nullus novus sanctus in veneratione habeatur nisi auctoritate sedis apostolice, ita quod '''canonizetur''' a papa.|translation=This Pope Innnocent [III] decreed {{...}} that no new saint should be held in veneration without the authority of the apostolic see, that they therefore are to be '''canonized''' by the pope.}}
# to [[ratify]], [[declare]] something [[official]] or [[authoritative]], e.g. as part of the [[biblical]] [[canon]] or the [[liturgy]]
#* {{quote-book|la|year=1074|author=w:Pope Gregory VII|chapter=Epistola {{...}} ad Ottonem Constantiensem Episcopum {{...}}|year_published=1644|title=Conciliorum omnium generalium et provincialium collectio regia|volume=26|page=527|url=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=R8JiAAAAcAAJ&lpg=PA527&ots=5tQcUZAet9&dq=%22Sic%20enim%20legati%20sedis%22&pg=PA527#v=onepage|text=Sic enim legati sedis apostolicae eorumdem principalium Conciliorum sanctiones primaria subscriptione apostolica vice '''canonizabant'''.|translation=For the legates of the apostolic see '''used to ratify''' the decrees of the same Councils in this way in place of the principal apostolic signature.}}
# to [[justify]] in [[canon law]]
# to make someone a [[canon]] {{gloss|member of a [[cathedral]] [[chapter]]}}

