Page 1004 carpo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*karpō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*kerp-}}.

Compare Greek {{m|grc|καρπός||fruit}} and {{m|grc|κείρω||to cut off}}, English {{m|en|harvest}}, {{m|en|sharp}}, {{m|en|shear}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|carpō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|carpō|carps|carpt}}

# {{lb|la|literally}} to [[pluck]], [[pick]], [[harvest]]
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Metamorphoses|9|380|thru=381|quote=Stāgna tamen timeat, nec '''carpat''' ab arbore flōrēs,<br>et fruticēs omnēs corpus putet esse deārum.|trans=May he fear the ponds, and may he not '''pick''' flowers from the trees,<br>and may he think all trees to be bodies of goddesses.}}
# to [[tear off]], [[tear out]], [[rend]], [[separate]] a [[whole]] into [[single]] [[parts]], to [[cut]] to [[pieces]], [[divide]]
#: {{syn|la|discindō|scindō|findō|discerpō|distineō|discīdō|incīdō|intercīdō|distrahō}}
#: {{ant|la|cōgō|congerō|coniungō|contrahō}}
#* {{Q|la|Valerius Flaccus|Argonautica|8|7|thru=8|quote={{...}}crīnemque genāsque<br>aegra per antīquī '''carpsit''' vestīgia somnī.|t={{...}}and she '''tore off''' her hair and her cheeks,<br>sorrowful, amid the traces of her previous sleep.}}
#* '''''[[circa|c.]]'' 400 {{CE|nodots=yes}}''', [[w:Prudentius|Prudentius]], ''Liber Peristephanon'' [[s:la:Liber Peristephanon/10|10.694–695]]:
#*: Oculī parentis pūnientur ācrius<br>quam sī cruentae membra '''carpant''' ungulae.
#*:: The parent's eyes are more intensely punished<br>than if bloody nails were to '''tear''' at her limbs.
# {{lb|la|textiles}} to [[spin]]
#* {{Q|la|Vergil|Georgicon|4|334|thru=335|quote={{...}}Mīlēsia vellera nymphae<br>'''carpēbant'''{{...}}|t={{...}}the nymphs '''were spinning'''<br>Milesian wool{{...}}}}
# to make good [[use]] of, [[enjoy]] something (usually a period of time)
#* {{Q|la|Horace|Odes|1|11|6|thru=8|quote=Sapiās, vīna liquēs, et spatiō brevī<br>spem longam resecēs. Dum loquimur, fūgerit invida<br>aetās: '''carpe''' diem, quam minimum crēdula posterō.|t=Be wise, make wine, and in a short time,<br>lose any great hope. As we speak, time is cruelly fleeing away.<br>'''Enjoy''' the day, believing the least in the future.}}
#* {{Q|la|Vergil|Aeneid|7|413|thru=414|quote=Tēctīs hīc Turnus in altīs<br>iam mediam nigrā '''carpēbat''' nocte quiētem.|t=Here and now, in a high floor, Turnus<br>'''was enjoying''' his rest in the middle of the dark night.}}
#* {{Q|la|Valerius Flaccus|Argonautica|5|48|quote='''Carpere''' sēcūrās quis iam iubet Aesona noctēs?|t=Who is now telling Aeson '''to enjoy''' his peaceful nights?}}
# to [[revile]], [[criticize]], [[slander]], [[carp]] at
#* {{Q|la|Catullus|Carmina|62|quote=At lubet innūptīs fīctō tē '''carpere''' questū.<br>Quid tum, sī '''carpunt''', tacitā quem mente requīrunt?|t=But maidens like to '''chide''' you with feigned complaint.<br>What then, if they '''chide''' him whom in their secret heart they desire?}}
#* {{Q|la|Livy|Ab urbe condita libri|45|35|5|quote=Paulum, cui ipsī quoque sē conparāre ērubuissent, obtrectātiō '''carpsit'''.|t=Criticism '''reviled''' Paulus, a man that people would have blushed to compare themselves to.}}
#* '''3rd''' or '''4th C. {{CE}}''', Pseudo-Cato, ''[[w:Distichs of Cato|Disticha Catonis|]]'' [[s:la:Disticha Catonis#Liber III|3.7]]:
#*: {{quote|la|Alterius dictum aut factum nē '''carpseris''' umquam,<br>exemplō similī nē tē dērīdeat alter.
|translation=Don't ever '''criticize''' what someone says or does,<br>lest another laugh at you when you do something similar.}}
# {{lb|la|military}} to [[weaken]], [[harass]] an enemy
#* {{Q|la|Julius Caesar|Commentarii de Bello Civili|1|63|quote=Relinquēbātur Caesarī nihil, nisi utī equitātū agmen adversāriōrum male habēret et '''carperet'''.|t=No option remained to Cesar, other than annoying and '''harassing''' the enemy army with the cavalry.}}

