Page 1006 carro: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*karzō}}, from the Proto-Indo-European root {{m|ine-pro|*(s)kers-||to comb wool}}, extended from {{m|ine-pro|*(s)ker-||to cut}}. Compare Lithuanian {{m|lt|kar̃šti||combs, cards}}, Latvian {{m|lv|kā̀rst||combs, cards}}, Old High German {{m|goh|scerran||to scratch}}. Varro falsely connects this with {{m|la|careō}}, possibly because the word had already gone extinct in his time, with the only reminiscence being {{m|la|carmen||card for flax or wool}} which was the evident derivational base of the rather common {{m|la|carminō||I card}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|la|carō|carriō}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|carrō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|3|carrō}}

