Page 1025 caveo: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Dom_dramaturga.jpg|thumb|right|'''''Cave''' canem''<br/>'''Beware''' of the dog]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*kawēō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*(s)kewh₁-||to perceive, pay attention}}.

Cognate with {{cog|grc|κοέω}}, {{cog|sa|कवि|tr=kaví||wise, poet, seer, sage}}, {{cog|lt|kavoti||safeguard, tend}}, {{cog|xcl|ցուցանեմ||I show}}, {{cog|en|show}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|caveō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2.poet-sync-perf|caveō|cāv|caut}}

# to take [[precautions]], [[beware]], take [[care]]; to [[guard against]], [[attend]] to a thing for a person, [[provide]]
#: {{syn|la|cūrō|accūrō|servō|videō|cōnsulō|prōcūrō|colō|cōnsultō}}
#: {{ux|la|'''Caveat''' emptor.|t=Buyer '''beware'''.}}
## {{lb|la|with accusative}} to [[beware]] of, [[keep away]] from, [[avoid]]
##* {{Q|la|Petronius|Satyricon|29|quote='''Cave''' canem.|trans='''Beware''' of the dog.}}
# {{lb|la|with ablative|with dative|with ab|with cum|with nē|with ut}} to [[guard against]], to be on one's [[guard]] [[against]], to [[take care]] that (not)
## {{lb|la|imperative}} [[beware]] not to!, [[refrain]] from!, [[make sure]] that not, [[mind]] that you [[don't]]!
##: {{ux|la|'''Cave''' sīs tē videam!|t='''Make sure''' I don't see you again!}}
##* {{Q|la|Catullus|Carmina|50|13-14|quote=Nunc audāx '''cave''' sīs, precēsque nostrās/ōrāmus, '''cave''' dēspuās, ocelle!|t=Beware of being haughty now, I beg you, and don't reject my desperate request, my jewel!}}
# {{lb|la|with dative}} to [[look out]] in the [[interest]]s of
# {{lb|la|legal}} to make legal [[provision]]s {{qual|for or against}}, to [[order]], [[decree]], [[stipulate]]
# {{lb|la|legal}} to give [[surety]] or [[guarantees]], to [[secure]] [[bail]]; to [[pledge]], [[certify]]
## {{lb|la|with ab}} to [[procure]] [[bail]] or [[surety]] from

====Usage notes====
The primary sense ("beware") may either govern a noun in the accusative or a subjunctive clause joined with {{m|la|nē}}, with the meaning "beware not to, make sure that you don't". However, the latter use became idiomatic early on with the particle '''nē''' omitted. In either case, the semantically-weakened '''cavĕ''' regularly has a short final vowel through iambic shortening. C.f. the parallel positive {{m|la|video|vidĕ|see that, make sure to}}.

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|2.poet-sync-perf|caveō|cāv|caut}}

====Derived terms====
