Cognate with {{cog|grc|κρίνω}}, {{cog|en|ridder}}, {{m|en|riddle|t=sieve}}, and possibly {{cog|en|rinse}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|cernō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3.poet-sync-perf|cernō|crēv|crēt}}

# to [[distinguish]], [[divide]], [[separate]], [[sift]]
#: {{syn|la|aufero|eripio|diripio|excludo|distraho|tollo}}
# to [[perceive]], [[see]]
#: {{syn|la|percipiō|sentiō|audiō|videō|cōnspicor}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|2|671-672|quote=nunc quoque, sē suprā nē quid nisi sīdera '''cernat''',<br/>exiguum templī tēcta forāmen habent.|trans=''Even now, '''so that he may see''' nothing except the stars above him,<br/>the roof of the temple has a tiny opening.''<br/>(The ancient Romans believed that {{w|Terminus (god)}}, protector of boundary stones, had refused to yield the ground of his own shrine – located inconveniently on the site where the {{w|Temple of Jupiter Optimus Maximus}} was to be built. And that is why Jupiter's great temple honored the immovable will of Terminus by way of a sacred stone or altar with a clear sightline to the stars.)}}
# to (intellectually) [[comprehend]], [[discern]], [[regard]], [[understand]]
#: {{syn|la|agnōscō|cognōscō|inveniō|sentiō|cōnsciō|sapiō|sciō|nōscō|scīscō|intellegō|percipiō|discernō|inveniō|tongeō|audiō}}
#: {{ant|la|ignōrō|nesciō}}
# to [[decide]]
#: {{syn|la|statuō|dēcernō|parō|cōnstituō|placeō}}

