Page 1155 clamo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*kelh₁-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*klāmāō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*kelh₁-||to shout}}. Probably reflecting unattested ''*clāma'' ("a shout") + {{m|la|-ō|id=denominative}} (confer {{m|la|fāma}}). See also Latin {{m|la|calō}}, {{m|la|clārus}}, {{m|la|classis}}, {{m|la|concilium}}.

Cognate with {{cog|grc|καλέω}}, {{m|grc|κληδών||report, fame}}, {{m|grc|κλήση||to call}}, {{m|grc|κέλαδος||noise}}, {{cog|lt|kalba||language}}, {{cog|ang|hlowan||to low, make a noise like a cow}}, {{cog|goh|halan||to call}}, {{cog|mga|cailech||cock}}, {{cog|sa|उषःकल||cock, ''literally'' dawn-calling}}, {{cog|pl|kłamać||lie}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|clāmō}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-clamo.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|clāmō}}

# to [[cry out]], [[clamor]], [[shout]], [[yell]], [[exclaim]]
#: {{syn|la|conclāmō|vōcificō|vōciferor|clāmitō|tonō|succlāmō|acclāmō|exclāmō|inclāmō}}
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin}} to [[call]], to [[call to]]
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin}} to [[address]] as, [[call]] by name

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+|clāmō}}

