===Etymology 1===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*(s)kleh₂w-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*klaudō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*(s)kleh₂w-|*kleh₂u-|key, hook, nail}}. Cognate with {{cog|grc|κλείς|t=bar, bolt, key}}, {{cog|goh|sliozan|t=to close, conclude, lock}}, {{cog|osx|slūtan|t=to close, conclude, lock}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|la|clūdō}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|claudō|eccl=1}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|3|claudō|claus|claus}}

# to [[shut up]], [[close]], [[lock]]
#: {{syn|la|retineō|intersaepiō|interclūdō|inclūdō|operiō|premō|obserō}}
#: {{ant|la|adaperiō|aperiō|patefaciō}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|232-233|quote=“quid Trōēs potuēre, quibus, tot fūnera passīs,<br/>cūnctus ob Ītaliam terrārum '''clauditur''' orbis?”|trans=''“What have the Trojans done, for whom, having suffered so many losses, the whole circle of the lands '''has been closed'''. [And all] for the sake of Italy.”''<br/>(Venus, speaking to Jupiter, laments the plight of the Trojans as they wander the Mediterranean shores.)}}
# to [[imprison]], [[confine]]
#: {{syn|la|comprehendo|retineo|intersaepio|includo|intercludo|arceo|impedio|urgeō|coerceō|prohibeo}}
# to [[encompass]], [[surround]]
#: {{syn|la|complector|amplector|stīpō|circumdō|circumveniō}}
# to [[besiege]], [[blockade]]
#: {{syn|la|circumveniō|circumeō|circumsistō|circumdō|obsideō|assideō|circumsaepiō|saepiō|obstruō}}
# to [[limit]], [[restrict]]
#: {{syn|la|delīmitō|līmitō|inclūdō|fīniō|coerceō|minuō|moderor}}
# to [[terminate]], [[finish]], [[complete]]
#: {{syn|la|perficiō|dēfungor|cōnficiō|agō|cumulō|absolvō|nāvō|perpetrō|inclūdō|expleō|fungor|efficiō|patrō|conclūdō|condō|peragō|trānsigō|exsequor|gerō|impleō|exhauriō}}

