Page 1199 coepio: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|con-|alt1=co-|apō|t2=lit. to lay hold of something on different sides, to lay hold of; hence of an action, to begin}}. The present stem is a {{back-form|la||nocap=1}} from the perfect stem {{m|la|coepī}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|coepiō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|coepiō|coep|coept}}

# {{lb|la|ante-classical lemma|_|and|_|post-classical|ambitransitive}} to [[begin]], [[commence]], [[initiate]]
#: {{syn|la|incohō|exōrdior|occipiō|incipiō|ōrdior|initiō|ineō|ingredior|aggredior|sūmō|moveō|committō|mōlior|exorior}}
#: {{ant|la|dēsistō|subsistō|cessō}}

====Usage notes====
In classical times, only the perfect tenses were in use; the present, imperfect and future indicative and the present and imperfect subjunctive, were supplied by {{m|la|incipiō}}.  This is similar to {{m|la|odiō}}.

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|coepiō|coep|coept}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|la|coepī}}
* {{l|la|coeptō}}

===References===
* {{R:L&S}}
* {{R:Elementary Lewis}}
* {{R:Gaffiot}}
-------- end text --------
