Page 1202 coest: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{af|la|con-|sort=est}} + {{m|la||est}} (see {{m|la|sum}})

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg.impers|consum|3s_pres_actv_indc=coest|pres_actv_inf=coesse}}

# {{lb|la|archaic|rare}} to [[happen]], to be [[accomplish]]ed
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Miles Gloriosus|3|3|66|thru=68|notes=lines 939–941|quote=''Acr.'' Datne ab se mulier operam? <br> ''Per.'' Lepidissume et compsissume. <br> ''Acr.'' Confido '''confuturum'''.<br>ubi facta erit conlatio nostrarum malitiarum,<br>haud vereor ne nos subdola perfidia pervincamur.|transauthor=Paul Nixon|trans=Is the girl herself helping us? <br>Oh, delightfully, toutafaitly!<br>I trust '''things will turn out well'''. <br>When we've lumped together our talents for mischief, <br>I have no fear of our being beaten at artful wiles.}}
#* {{Q|la|Terence|Andria|1|1|138|thru=140|quote=sin eveniat quod volo,<br>in Pamphilo ut nil sit morae, restat Chremes,<br>qui mi exorandus est: et spero '''confore'''.|transauthor=Henry Thomas Riley|trans=If it should turn out, as I wish, <br>that there is no delay on the part of Pamphilus, Chremes remains<br> to be prevailed upon by me; and I do hope that '''all will go well'''.}}
# {{lb|la|Late Latin|Medieval Latin}} to [[occur]] at the same time, to [[coexist]]
#* {{Q|la|{{w|William of Saint Thierry}}|Meditativae orationes|1|7|52|quote=Est autem praescientia tua, Deus, ipsa sapientia tua, quae ab aeterno tibi aeternaliter '''coest''', (etiam si nulla esset creatura){{...}}|trans=Moreover, Thy foreknowledge, O my God, is one thing with Thy wisdom, which '''is with''' Thee from and to all eternity, and so would it have been with Thee, had never a creature existed.}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|irreg.impers|consum|3s_pres_actv_indc=coest|3s_impf_actv_indc=coerat|3s_futr_actv_indc=coerit|3s_futr_actv_impr=-|3s_impf_actv_subj=coesset/cōnforet|pres_actv_inf=coesse}}

===References===
* {{R:L&S|consum|consum}}
* {{R:Elementary Lewis|confore|confore}}
* {{R:Gaffiot|confuit|confuit}}
* {{R:du Cange|coesse|coesse}}
