Page 1207 cogo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|la|coagō}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₂eǵ-}}
From {{affix|la|con-|alt1=co-|agō|t2=lead, drive, impel, push}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|cōgō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|cōgō|coēg|coāct}}

# to [[collect]], [[assemble]], [[gather]] together
#I [[restrict]] or [[confine]] in space
#: {{syn|la|contrahō|cōnferō|congerō|coniungō|concieō|cōnserō|convehō|cōnstruō|glomerō|concitō|colligō|reficiō}}
#* Thomas of Celano, ''Dies Irae'':
#*: {{quote|la|Tuba mirum spargens sonum, per sepulchra regionum, '''coget''' omnes ante Thronum.|t=The trumpet, scattering its awesome sound across the sepulchres of the lands, '''shall assemble''' all people before the Throne.}}
# to [[force]], [[compel]], [[urge]], [[encourage]], [[finagle]]
#: {{syn|la|impingō|perpellō|compellō|impellō|subigō}}
#* Saint Jerome, ''Preface to the Vulgata'':
#*: {{quote|la|Novum opus facere me '''cogis''' ex veteri, ut post exemplaria scripturarum toto orbe dispersa quasi quidam arbiter sedeam (...).|t= You '''order''' me to make a new work out of the old one, so that after the copies of the Scriptures dispersed across the globe I preside as some kind of arbitrator (...).}}
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Caesar|Caesar]]|[[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]]|VII, 15|quote=ne pulcherrimam prope totius Galliae urbem, quae praesidio et ornamento sit civitati, suis manibus succendere '''cogerentur'''|t=lest they should '''be compelled''' to set fire with their own hands to the fairest city of almost the whole of Gaul, which is a protection and  ornament to the state}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|cōgō|coēg|coāct}}

