{{la-verb|3|colligō|collēg|collēct}}

# to [[gather]], [[draw]], [[bring]] or [[collect]] (together), [[assemble]], [[pick]] up; [[contract]], [[draw up]], [[compress]], [[concentrate]]; [[harvest]]
#: {{syn|la|cōgō|stīpō|glomerō|compellō|congerō|cōnserō|contrahō|cōnstruō|coniungō|cōnferō}}
#* {{Q|la|Terence|Adelphoe|5|3|59|thru=63|quote=DĒMEA. Ego istuc vīderō,<br>atque ibi favīllae plēna, fūmī ac pollinis<br>coquendō sit faxō et molendō. Praeter haec<br>merīdiē ipsō faciam ut stipulam '''colligat'''.<br>Tam excoctam reddam atque ātram quam carbō est.|trans=DEMEA. I'll see to that,<br>and full of soot, smoke and flour<br>from the cooking and grinding I'll make her. And, besides that,<br>I'll make her '''collect''' the straw at noon.<br>I'll render her as burnt and black as coal.}}
#* {{Q|la|Julius Caesar|Commentarii de Bello Gallico|3|18|quote=Quā rē concessā laetī ut explōrātā victōriā sarmentīs virgultisquī '''collēctīs''', quibus fossās Rōmānōrum compleant, ad castra pergunt.|trans=With that concession, as if with victory assured, they go on their way to the camps with twigs and brushwood '''gathered''', to fill the Roman trenches with.}}
# to [[make]] [[thick]], [[thicken]]; [[bind]] or [[mass]] together
#: {{syn|la|cumulō|struō|accumulō}}
# to [[get]], [[gain]], [[acquire]], [[produce]], collect
#: {{syn|la|acquīrō|adipīscor|cōnsequor|parō|pariō|impetrō|mereō|sūmō|emō|comparō|potior|apīscor|obtineō|conciliō|nancīscor|alliciō|possideō}}
