Page 1330 comprehendo: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|la|2014|November|1}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|la|comprēndō|conprehendō}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*gʰed-}}
From {{affix|la|con-|prehendō|gloss2=catch, grasp}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|comprehendō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|comprehendō|comprehend|comprehēns}}

# to [[lay]] [[hold]] of something on all sides; [[take hold|take]] or [[catch]] hold of, [[grasp]], [[grip]]
#: {{syn|la|capiō|tangō|apprehendō|dēprehendō|prehēnsō|potior|temptō|teneō|capessō|prehēndō|arripiō}}
# to seize upon in a [[hostile]] manner, lay hold of; [[occupy]], [[capture]] {{qualifier|of a place}}; [[arrest]], [[detain]], [[apprehend]], [[catch]]; to [[intercept]] (a letter)
#: {{syn|la|expugnō|claudō|capiō|teneō|occupō|obtineō|compleō|apprehendō|opprimō|inclūdō|possideō|obsideō|retineō}}
# {{lb|la|to a crime or deed}} to [[discover]], [[detect]], [[come upon]], [[reveal]]
# {{lb|la|of space}} to [[contain]], [[comprise]], to [[enclose]], to [[include]], to [[comprehend]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively|Late Latin}} to [[shut]] in, to [[include]]
# ''to conjoin, to fuse with the thing that has come close''
## {{lb|la|of plants}} to [[take root]], to take hold
## {{lb|la|of a woman}} to become [[pregnant]], to [[conceive]]
## {{lb|la|with ignem}} to [[catch fire|catch]] (fire)
## {{lb|la|Late Latin|of medicines}} to [[combine]], [[unite]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} ''to be connected to a structure serving cognition as follows''
## to comprehend by sense of sight, [[perceive]], [[observe]], [[see]]
## to comprehend something by the [[mind]], [[understand]], [[perceive]], grasp
#: {{syn|la|apprehendō|dēprehendō|accipiō|cognōscō|concipiō|teneō|apīscor|capiō|complector|excipiō|exaudiō|cōnsequor}}
#: {{ant|la|nesciō|ignōrō}}
## to [[include]] or comprehend in words, [[comprise]] in discourse, [[express]], [[describe]], [[recount]], [[narrate]]
## {{lb|la|of|law}} to [[provide]], to [[establish]], to [[determine]]
##* {{w|Digest (Roman law)|Dig.}} XLV.I.19 ''{{w|Sextus Pomponius|Pomponius}} libro quinto decimo ad Sabinum''
##*: {{quote|la|Si stipulatio facta fuerit: «si culpa tua divortium factum fuerti, dari?», nulla obligatio est, quia contenti esse debemus poenis legum '''comprehensis''': nisi si et stipulatio tantundem habeat poenae, quanta lege sit '''comprehensa'''.|If a stipulation has been made that “it is to be given if by your fault divorce befalls”, then this stipulation is void, because we have to be content with the penalties '''provided for''' by the laws: except if the stipulation has a penalty of the same height as is '''provided for''' by law.}}
## to [[number]], [[enumerate]], [[reckon]]
## to comprehend someone in [[affection]], [[embrace]] with [[kindness]], to [[bind]] or put under [[obligation]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|comprehendō|comprehend|comprehēns}}

