|trans=''Don’t '''yield''' anything to a neighbor [who’s] asking you [to].''<br/>(The protector of boundary stones, {{w|Terminus (god)}}, had a divine duty to guard property, and ought not defer to human requests. As Ovid invokes Terminus, the poet's use of the imperative ''concēde'' also has a more direct intent: ''Don't let them move the boundary stone!'')}}

