Page 1581 conspicio: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|con-|speciō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|cōnspiciō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|cōnspiciō|cōnspex|cōnspect}}

# to [[see]], [[watch]], [[observe]], [[perceive]], [[catch]] [[sight]] of, [[look at]] with [[admiration]] or [[close]] [[attention]], [[gaze]] [[upon]], [[contemplate]], [[behold]]
#: {{syn|la|observō|servō|spectō|cōnspicor|cū̆stōdiō|intueor|animadvertō}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|151-152|quote=tum, pietāte gravem ac meritīs sī forte virum quem<br/>'''cōnspexēre''', silent, arrēctīsque auribus adstant.|trans=''Then, if by chance [the disorderly people] '''catch sight of''' some man, venerable in [his] piety and service, they [fall] silent, and stand straight with [attentive] ears.''<br/>(Here, “conspexere” is a syncopated form of the third person plural perfect “conspexerunt.” Understand “quem” along with its prefix: “[[aliquem]].”)}}
# to [[examine]], [[consider]]
#: {{syn|la|aspiciō|lūstrō|perlūstrō|recēnseō|circumspiciō|obeō|īnspiciō|arbitror|cōnsīderō|reputō|exsequor}}
# (Passive with reflexive value) to attract [[attention]], to be [[conspicuous]], to be [[visible]]
# to [[comprehend]], [[realize]], [[notice]]
#: {{syn|la|cognosco|nosco|apiscor|teneo|comprehendo|accipio|concipio}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|cōnspiciō|cōnspex|cōnspect}}

