===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*komstaēō}}. Equivalent to {{affix|la|con-|gloss1=together|stō|gloss2=stand}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|cōnstō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1.nopass|cōnstō|cōnstit|cōnstāt}}

# to [[stand]] together
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Caesar|Caesar]]|[[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]]|VII, 28|quote=In foro ac locis patentioribus [...] '''constiterunt'''|t=They '''stood together''' in the marketplace and the more open places}}
# to stand still; to remain the same; stand [[firm]]
#: {{syn|la|sistō|persistō|remaneō|maneō|stō|haereō}}
# to [[agree]], [[correspond]], [[fit]]
#: {{syn|la|concordō|condīcō|conveniō|cōnsentiō|assentiō|concurrō|congruō|pangō}}
#: {{ant|la|dissentiō|dissideō|discordō|variō|abhorreō}}
