Page 1600 consulo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{affix|la|con-|sort=solo}} + a derivation of {{der|la|ine-pro|*selh₁-||to take, grab}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=consulo|page=131}}</ref> Compare with {{m|la|cōnsul}} and {{m|la|cōnsilium}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|sell}}, {{m|en|sale}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|cōnsulō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|cōnsulō|cōnsulu|cōnsult}}

# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[consult]], seek [[counsel]] from, take counsel from
#: {{syn|la|cōnsultō|dēlīberō}}
#* {{Q|la|Livy|Ab Urbe Condita|26|1|quote=Cn. Fuluius Centumalus P. Sulpicius Galba consules cum idibus Martiis magistratum inissent, senatu in Capitolium uocato, de re publica, de administratione belli, de prouinciis exercitibusque patres '''consuluerunt'''.|year=27-25 BCE|trans=When the consuls Gnaeus Fulvius Centumalus and Publius Sulpicius Galba took up the magistracy on the Ides of March, they summoned the senate to the Capitoline Hill and '''consulted''' the senators on issues regarding the state, the handling of the war, the provinces and the armies.}}
# to [[deliberate]]
# {{lb|la|ambitransitive|followed by the accusative or with {{l|la|de}}}} to [[reflect upon]], deliberate over, think (something) over
#: {{syn|la|reflectō|ponderō|dēlīberō|putō|pendō|cōnsīderō|reputō|replicō|dubitō|cōnsultō|circumspiciō|videō|versō}}
# to give thought to, have [[regard]] for
# {{lb|la|transitive|followed by the dative}} to [[look after]] the [[interest]]s of, [[take care]] of (someone)
#: {{syn|la|cūrō|accūrō|prōcūrō|cū̆stōdiō|servō|videō|respiciō|colō|cōnsultō|caveō|serviō}}
#: {{uxi|la|Legati ad eum venissent oratum ut sibi ignosceret suaeque vitae '''consuleret'''|Ambassadors came to him to beg that he would pardon them and '''take care of''' their lives}} ([[w:Caesar|Caesar]], [[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]], VII, 12)
#: {{uxi|la|ut suis fortunis '''consulat'''|in order that he might '''take care of''' their properties}} ([[w:Caesar|Caesar]], [[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]], VII, 8)
# {{lb|la|transitive|followed by the dative}} to be [[mindful]] of, pay [[attention]] to (someone's safety, life; dignity, reputation, etc.)

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|cōnsulō|cōnsulu|cōnsult}}

====Derived terms====
{{der3|la|cōnsultor|cōnsultō|cōnsultus}}

