{{la-verb|3|contingō|contig|contāct}}

# to [[touch]] on all sides, [[take]] [[hold]] of, come into [[contact]] with
#: {{syn|la|tempto|tango}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|2|238-239|quote=“[...] Puerī circum innūptaeque puellae<br/>sacra canunt, fūnemque manū '''contingere''' gaudent.”|trans=''“Around [the wooden horse], boys and unwedded girls chant hymns, and delight '''to touch''' a rope by hand.”''<br/>(The Trojans pull the wooden horse using heavy ropes while their children celebrate it as a sacred effigy.)}}
# to [[reach]] (by moving), [[attain]] to, [[come]] to, [[arrive]] at, [[meet]] with
# to touch, [[extend]] to, [[border]] upon, [[reach]]; to be [[near]], [[neighbouring]] or [[contiguous]] to
#: {{syn|la|subsum|immineo|astō|insto}}
#: {{ant|la|dissideō|distō}}
