#: {{syn|la|percutio|accido|verbero|cello|discutio|ico|percello|affligo}}
# to touch, [[affect]], [[seize]] upon, [[move]]
# {{lb|la|usually in passive}} to touch with [[pollution]], [[pollute]], [[stain]], [[defile]], [[contaminate]]
#: {{syn|la|polluō|inquinō|maculō|scelerō}}
#: {{ant|la|tergeō|abstergeō|pūrgō|luō|putō|effingō}}
# {{lb|la|with dative}} to [[fall]] to one's [[lot]], [[obtain]]
# to [[happen]], [[turn out]], come to [[pass]]
#: {{syn|la|interveniō|ēveniō|obveniō|expetō|obtingō|incurrō|accēdō|intercidō|incidō|accidō|fīō}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|94-96|quote=[...] “Ō terque quaterque beātī,<br/>quīs ante ōra patrum Troiae sub moenibus altīs<br/>'''contigit''' oppetere! [...].”|trans=''“Oh [those] three and four times blessed, to whom – before [your] fathers’ faces, beneath the high walls of Troy – '''it happened''' [for you] to meet [death]!”''<br/>(Aeneas speaks in [[apostrophe]] to absent warriors; in other words, those heroes who died on the battlefield of Troy, as witnessed by their fathers from atop the city walls. Note: Here “quis” is “[[quibus]],” a plural dative of interest.)}}

