Page 1645 contribuo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|con-|tribuō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|contribuō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|contribuō|contribu|contribūt}}

# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[put together]], [[combine]], [[join]] in one, [[unite]]
#: {{syn|la|committō|addō|adiciō|adalligō|colligō|applicō|illigō|implicō}}
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[attach]] {{lb|la|a township, state, ruler, etc.}} for political or administrative purposes
## {{lb|la|in general}} to allot, assign
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[bring in]] one's [[share]]; to [[contribute]], [[give]]
#: {{syn|la|intribuō}}
#* {{Q|la|Seneca the Younger|De brevitate vitae|15|quote=Horum te mori nemo coget, omnes docebunt; horum nemo annos tuos conteret, suos tibi '''contribuet'''; nullius ex his sermo periculosus erit, nullius amicitia capitalis, nullius sumptuosa obseruatio.|trans=No one of these will force you to die, but all will teach you how to die; no one of these will wear out your years, but each will add his own years to yours; conversations with no one of these will bring you peril, the friendship of none will endanger your life, the courting of none will tax your purse.}}
# to [[incorporate]], [[impart]]
#: {{syn|la|participō}}
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin|intransitive|absolute|with {{m|la|ad}}|with {{m|la|in}}}} to [[pay]] {{lb|la|a share}}, [[contribute]]
#* [episcopi et archidiaconi] dicunt quod '''contribuere''' non debent, [..] quia contributio fieret contra eum qui contraxit cum principe suo.

====Usage notes====
Unlike its Romance descendants or {{m|la|confero|cōnferre}}, classically always transitive.

