Page 1715 credo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*ḱerd-|*dʰeh₁-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*krezðō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*ḱréddʰh₁eti|*ḱred dʰeh₁-|to place one's heart, i.e. to trust, believe}}, compound phrase of oblique case form of {{m|ine-pro|*ḱḗr||heart}} (whence also {{cog|la|cor}}) and {{m|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-||to put, place, set}} (whence {{m|la|*dere||put/give}}).<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=crēdō|pages=141-142}}</ref>

Cognates include {{cog|sa|श्रद्दधाति||tr=śrad-√dhā|to trust, believe}} and {{cog|sga|creitid||believes|pos=v}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|crēdō}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-credo.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|crēdō|crēdid|crēdit}}

# {{lb|la|with accusative or dative}} to [[believe]], to [[trust]] in, to give [[credence]] to
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Captivi|url=http://www.ihaystack.com/authors/m/plautus_titus_maccius/00016564_amphitryo_asinaria_aulularia_bacchides_captivi_amphi/00016564_englishlatin_utf8_p043.htm|quote=Tune huic '''credis'''?|trans=Do you '''believe''' him?}}
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Captivi|url=http://www.ihaystack.com/authors/m/plautus_titus_maccius/00016564_amphitryo_asinaria_aulularia_bacchides_captivi_amphi/00016564_englishlatin_utf8_p043.htm|quote=Aristophontes: Quid tu autem? Etiam huic '''credis'''?<br>Hegio: Quid ego '''credam''' huic?<br>Aristophontes: Insanum esse me?|trans=Aristophontes: How’s this? You, too? Do you actually '''believe''' him?<br>Hegio: '''Believe''' him in what?<br>Aristophontes: That I’m insane?}}
# to [[confide]] in, have [[confidence]] in
#: {{syn|la|confido|fido}}
#: {{ant|la|diffīdō|suspiciō}}
# to [[think]], [[imagine]], [[suppose]], [[assume]]
#: {{syn|la|censeo|iūdicō|puto|cōgitō|sentio|existimo|arbitror|opinor|reor}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|1|518|quote=quis tantum fātī '''crēdat''' habēre locum?|trans=''Who could '''imagine''' the place to have so great a destiny?''}}
# to [[commit]] or [[consign]] something to one for [[preservation]], [[protection]], etc., to [[entrust]] to one
# to [[lend]], to [[loan]]

====Usage notes====
* ''Crēdō'' often governs the dative with persons believed in, but the accusative with things or concepts believed in. The accusative may be accompanied by a preposition: ''Crēdō in ūnum Deum'' = "I believe in one God".

====Conjugation====
