Page 1720 cresco: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{inh+|la|ine-pro|*ḱreh₁[[-sḱéti]]}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*ḱer-|t=to grow, become bigger}}, whence also {{m+|la|creō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|crēscō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3.nopass|crēscō|crēv|crēt}}

# to [[rise]], [[grow]], [[grow up]]; [[prosper]], [[thrive]]; [[increase]], [[multiply]], [[augment]]
#: {{syn|la|adolēscō|accrēscō|excrēscō|olēscō|glīscō}}
#: {{ant|la|dēcrēscō}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|4|913-914|quote=‘tū sata sīderibus caelī nūtrīta secundīs<br/>'''crēscere''', dum fīant falcibus apta, sinās.’|trans=''“May you allow the crops – having been nourished by the stars of favorable heaven – '''to thrive''', until they become ready for the sickles.”''<br/>(A prayer spoken by the {{w|Flamen Quirinalis}} during the {{w|Robigalia}} to propitiate the deity Robigo or Robigus and prevent agricultural diseases.)}}
# to [[come]] to be
# to become [[visible]], [[spring]] from, [[arise]], [[come forth]]
#: {{syn|la|appāreō|obversor|prōcēdō|exorior|orior|coorior}}
#: {{ant|la|cēdō|concēdō|decēdō|excēdō|discēdō|pereō|intereō}}

====Conjugation====
* The only attested passive forms are those from {{m|la|crētus}}, which is used in an active sense.
