Page 1725 criso: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|la|crissō}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*(s)kreyt-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(s)ker-|t=twist, turn, bend}}. Cognates include {{cog|de|schreiten}}, {{cog|en|shrithe}} and {{cog|mga|crith}}, {{cog|br|skrija|t=tremble with fear}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|crīsō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|crīsō}}

# {{lb|la|vulgar}} to [[grind]] (rhythmically move the haunches during sex)
#* [[w:en:Marcus Valerius Martialis|Martial]], ''Epigrammaton'', 14:203:
#*: ''Tam tremulum '''crisat''', tam blandum prurit, ut ipsum / Masturbatorem fecerit Hippolytum.''
#*:: So tremulously she '''shakes her behind''', so alluringly she arouses, / that she would make Hippolytus himself a masturbator.
#* [[w:Juvenal|Juvenal]], ''Satire VI'', 322:
#*: ''[...] / ipsa Medullinae fluctum '''crisantis''' adorat: / [...]''
#*:: [...] then she in turn worships Medullina's '''undulating''' surges [...]

====Usage notes====
* ''Crīso'' is a word for the female action during receptive vaginal sex, as opposed to ''[[ceveo]]'' for anal sex and ''[[futuo]]'' for the act of vaginal penetration (''[[paedico]]'' for anal penetration).

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+|crīsō}}

====See also====
* {{l|la|futuō}}
* {{l|la|cēveō}}
* {{l|la|paedīcō}}
* {{l|la|irrumō}}

===References===
* {{R:L&S}}
* {{R:Elementary Lewis}}
* {{R:Gaffiot}}

{{C|la|Sex}}
