Page 1749 curo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{af|la|cūra|-ō|id2=denominative}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|cūrō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+.p3inf.poet-sync-perf|cūrō}}

# to [[arrange]], [[see to]], [[attend]] to, [[take]] [[care]] of, [[look after]], [[ensure]], [[tend]] to
#: {{syn|la|accūrō|cū̆stōdiō|servō|videō|cōnsulō|prōcūrō|colō|cōnsultō|respiciō|serviō|caveō}}
#: {{ux|la|Romani templa deorum magna diligentia '''curant.'''|The Romans '''care''' for the temples of the gods with great diligence.}}
#* [[w:Spinoza|Benedictus de Spinoza]], Tractatus Politicus
#*: sedulo '''curavi''', humanas actiones non ridere, non lugere, neque detestari, sed intelligere
#*:: I '''have laboured''' diligently, not to mock, lament, or execrate human actions; but to understand them.
# to [[heal]], [[cure]]
#: {{ux|la|similia similibus '''curantur'''|likes '''cure''' likes}}
# to [[govern]], [[command]], [[preside]] over
#: {{syn|la|praesum}}
# to [[refresh]] {{gloss|when occurring with ''corpus''}}
