#* {{Q|la|Horace|Epistles|1|11|27|quote=Caelum, nōn animum mūtant, quī trāns mare '''currunt'''.|trans=They change the sky, not their souls, those who '''run''' across the sea.}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[hurry]], [[hasten]], [[speed]]
#: {{syn|la|ruō|accurrō|trepidō|festīnō|prōvolō|prōripiō|properō|corripiō|affluō|mātūrō|prōsiliō}}
#: {{ant|la|retardō|moror|cūnctor|dubitō|prōtrahō|trahō|differō}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[move]], [[travel]], [[proceed]]
# {{lb|la|transitive|of a race, journey|with accusative}} to run
# {{lb|la|transitive|with accusative}} to travel through, [[traverse]], run

====Conjugation====
