Page 1811 deduco: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|la|2014|September|26}}

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|dē-|dūcō|gloss2=lead, pull}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|dēdūcō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg|dēdūcō}}

# to [[lead]] or [[bring]] out or away, [[divert]]; [[escort]], [[accompany]], [[conduct]] (out of one's house as a mark of respect or for protection)
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Amphitruo|215|quote=respondent bello se et suos tutari posse proinde uti / propere de suis finibus exercitus '''deducerent'''|trans=They answered that they were able in warfare to protect themselves and theirs, and that at once they must '''lead''' the army with all haste '''out''' of their territories.}}
# to lead, [[fetch]], [[bring]] or [[draw]] down; [[weigh]] down, [[outweigh]]
# to [[deduct]], [[subtract]], [[diminish]], [[reduce]]
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|De Officiis|1|18|59|quote={{...}} ut boni ratiocinatores officiorum esse possimus et addendo '''deducendo'''que videre quae reliqui summa fiat ex quo quantum cuique debeatur intellegas|trans={{...}}, in order to become good calculators of duty, able by adding and '''subtracting''' to strike a balance correctly and find out just how much is due to each individual.}}
# to [[stretch]] out, [[extend]], draw out
#* {{Q|la|Vitruvius|De architectura|9|7|2|quote=et '''deducto''' circino ab eo centro ad lineam planitiae ubi erit littera B circinatio circuli describatur quae dicitur meridiana|trans=and '''extending''' the compasses from that centre to the extremity B of the said line, let a circle be described; this is called the meridian.}}
# to lead forth or conduct a [[colony]] to a certain place; [[found]] {{qualifier|a colony}}
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|Philippicae|13|31|quote=veteranorum colonias '''deductas''' lege senatus consulto sustulistis|trans=You, by a resolution of the senate, have removed the colonies of the veterans which had been '''settled''' by law.}}
# {{lb|la|legal}} to bring to [[trial]]; bring before a [[tribunal]] as a [[witness]]
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|Pro Flacco|6|9|quote=sed sunt in illo numero multi boni docti pudentes qui ad hoc iudicium '''deducti''' non sunt|trans=but there are in that number many virtuous, learned, modest men, who have not been '''brought''' here to this '''trial'''.}}
# {{lb|la|legal}} to [[withhold]]
#* {{Q|la|Gaius|Institutiones|2|33|quote=non enim ipse ususfructus mancipatur sed cum in mancipanda proprietate '''deducatur'''|trans=For the usufruct itself is not mancipated, but in mancipating the property the usufruct is '''withheld'''.}}
# {{lb|la|military}} to [[withdraw]], [[remove]], draw off, lead off {{qualifier|troops from one place to another}}; conduct or bring to a place
#* {{Q|la|Julius Caesar|Commentarii de Bello Civili|3|34|quote=Caesar Antonii exercitu coniuncto '''deducta''' Orico legione, quam tuendae orae maritimae causa posuerat|trans=Caesar, having '''withdrawn''' his garrisons from the sea-coast, as we have related above, left three cohorts at Oricum to defend the town}}
# {{lb|la|nautical}} to draw out a [[ship]] {{qualifier|from a port}}, [[launch]]
#* {{Q|la|Julius Caesar|Commentarii de Bello Civili|2|3|2|quote={{...}} ex navalibus eorum navem '''deducit'''|trans={{...}} '''drew out''' one of their ships out of dock.}}
# {{lb|la|rare|nautical}} to draw a ship into port
#* {{Q|la|Julius Caesar|Commentarii de Bello Civili|1|36|2|quote=onerarias naves, quas ubique possunt deprehendunt atque in portum '''deducunt'''|trans=They seize all the merchantmen they could meet with, and '''draw''' them '''into''' the harbor.}}
# {{lb|la|in weaving}} to [[spin]] or draw out {{qualifier|the thread}}; [[weave]]
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Metamorphoses|4|36|quote=e quibus una levi '''deducens''' pollice filum|trans=Then one of them speaks, '''spinning''' the thread lightly with her thumb}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[mislead]], [[seduce]], [[entice]], [[win over]], [[induce]]
#* {{Q|la|Julius Caesar|Bello Gallico|7|37|quote=celeriter adulescentibus et oratione magistratus et praemio '''deductis'''|trans=The young men being easily '''won over''' by the speech of the magistrate and the bribe}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively|of a literary composition}} to [[spin]] out, [[elaborate]], [[prepare]], [[describe]], [[compose]]
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Metamorphoses|1|3-4|quote={{...}} primaque ab origine mundi / ad mea perpetuum '''deducite''' tempora carmen /|trans={{...}} and '''spin out''' a continuous thread of words, from the world's first origins to my own time}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively|of the origin of words}} to [[derive]], [[discover]], deduce
#* {{Q|la|Pliny the Elder|Naturalis Historia|25|4|44|quote=quartum genus panaces ab eodem Chirone repertum centaurion cognominatur sed et Pharnaceon in controversia inventionis a Pharnace rege '''deductum'''|trans=A fourth kind of panaceas, discovered also by Chiron, is denominated as "centaurion," but also "pharnacion," '''derived''' from King Pharnaces; it being a matter in dispute of faculty of invention.}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively|of physical evils}} to [[cure]], [[cleanse]], [[remove]]
#* {{Q|la|Horace|Epistles|1|2|48|quote=/ non domus et fundus non aeris acervus et auri / aegroto domini '''deduxit''' corpore febris / non animo curas|trans=Not house or grounds, not heaps of brass or gold will '''cure''' the frame of fever's heat and cold or '''cleanse''' the heart of care.}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively|borrowed from the idea of spinning}} to [[make]] [[finer]], [[thinner]] or [[weaker]], [[attenuate]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|irreg|dēdūcō}}

