Page 1817 defendo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*gʷʰen-}}
From {{af|la|dē-|*fendō|t2=hit, thrust}}, from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*fendō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*gʷʰen-|t=to strike, to kill}}. Compare {{m|la|offendō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|dēfendō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|dēfendō|dēfend|dēfēns}}

# to drive away
# to [[defend]], [[guard]] or [[protect]], to [[stand up for]], to [[stick up for]]
#: {{syn|la|salvō|tūtor|vindicō|cū̆stōdiō|sospitō|teneō|adimō|prōtegō|tegō|sustineō|adsum|ēripiō|arceō|mūniō|tueor|servō|prohibeō}}
#: {{ant|la|immineō|īnstō|obiectō}}
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|Catiline|Oratio in Catilinam Prima in Senatu Habita|6|quote=Quam diu quisquam erit qui te '''defendere''' [[audeo|audeat]], vives, et vives ita ut nunc vivis, multis meis et firmis praesidiis obsessus ne commovere te contra rem publicam possis. Multorum te etiam oculi et aures non sentientem, sicut adhuc fecerunt, speculabuntur atque custodient.|trans=As long as one person exists who can [[dare]] to '''defend''' you, you shall live; but you shall live as you do now, surrounded by my many and trusty guards, so that you shall not be able to stir one finger against the republic: many eyes and ears shall still observe and watch you, as they have hitherto done, though you shall not perceive them.}}

