Page 1827 deficio: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|la|difficiō||Mediaeval}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-}}
From {{affix|la|de-|facio}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|dēficiō|eccl=yes}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|dēficiō|dēfēc|dēfect}}

# {{lb|la|intransitive|{{l|la|a|ab}} + ablative or {{l|la|ad}} + accusative}} to [[move away]], [[leave]], [[withdraw]], [[break away]]
#: {{uxi|la|{{l|la|ab}} {{l|la|aliqua}} {{l|la|re}} '''deficere'''|t= to break away from something}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to be [[exhausted]], [[run out]], [[fail]]
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to be [[discouraged]], [[disappoint]] or [[let down]]
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[finish up]], [[die]]
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[forsake]], [[desert]] or [[abandon]]
# {{lb|la|passive|reflexive}}  to be [[lacking]] in, to [[fall short]], have [[shortcomings]], [[fail]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3.sigm|dēficiō|dēfēc|dēfect|dēfex}}

====Quotations====
*'''526–527''', [[w:Priscianus Caesariensis|Priscianus Caesariensis]], ''Institutiones Grammaticae'', De Dictione
*:vides ergo per se ipsam syllabam '''deficere''' praedictorum ratione nec aliter posse examussim tractari, nisi posita sit in dictione.
*'''845''', the same as it appears in the [[w:St. Gall Priscian Glosses|St. Gall Priscian Glosses]]
*:uidesgͦ p̛se ips''am''syllabã'''difficere''' p͞dictor̄ ratione, necalit̄ posse examosim tractari n͗ posita indictione sit.
*::So you see that in and of itself the syllable is insufficient because of the aforementioned, and cannot otherwise exactly be used unless it is placed in a word.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|die}} {{l|la|pereō}}, {{l|la|morior}}, {{l|la|intereo}}, {{l|la|exspiro}}, {{l|la|defungor}}, {{l|la|decedo}}, {{l|la|aboleo}}, {{l|la|occumbō}}, {{l|la|cadō}}, {{l|la|excēdō}}, {{l|la|discedo}}
* {{sense|retire}} {{l|la|facessō}}, {{l|la|dēcēdō}}, {{l|la|discēdō}}, {{l|la|cēdō}}, {{l|la|concēdō}}, {{l|la|excēdō}}, {{l|la|regredior}}, {{l|la|subtrahō}}, {{l|la|subdūcō}}, {{l|la|inclīnō}}, {{l|la|recēdō}}, {{l|la|recipiō}}, {{l|la|āmoveō}}, {{l|la|referō}}, {{l|la|vertō}}
* {{sense|move away}} {{l|la|evado}}, {{l|la|exeo}}, {{l|la|discedo}}, {{l|la|facesso}}, {{l|la|decedo}}, {{l|la|cedo}}
* {{sense|abandon}} {{l|la|dēserō}}, {{l|la|relinquō}}, {{l|la|omittō}}, {{l|la|dēdō}}, {{l|la|concēdō}}, {{l|la|dēcēdō}}, {{l|la|linquō}}, {{l|la|dēsinō}}, {{l|la|reddō}}, {{l|la|remittō}}, {{l|la|dēstituō}}, {{l|la|oblīvīscor}}, {{l|la|cēdō}}, {{l|la|permittō}}, {{l|la|dissimulō}}, {{l|la|trādō}}, {{l|la|addīcō}}, {{l|la|praetereō}}, {{l|la|neglegō}}, {{l|la|pōnō}}, {{l|la|tribuō}}
* {{sense|lacking}} {{l|la|egeō}}, {{l|la|indigeō}}, {{l|la|delinquō}}, {{l|la|careō}}, {{l|la|dēsum}}, {{l|la|cessō}}, {{l|la|perdō}}
* {{sense|discourage}} {{l|la|profligō}}, {{l|la|dēfatīgō}}
