{{la-verb|3|dēmittō|dēmīs|dēmiss}}

# to [[send]] or [[bring]] down, [[cause]] to [[hang]] or [[fall]] down; [[drop]], [[flow]], [[shed]], [[sag]], [[let]] fall
# to  [[sink]], [[lower]], [[put]] down
#: {{syn|la|dēmergō|immergō|summergō|mergō|sepeliō|prōcumbō|supprimō}}
#* {{Q|la|Julius Caesar|Bello Gallico|1|32|quote=Animadvertit Caesar unos ex omnibus Sequanos nihil earum rerum facere quas ceteri facerent sed tristes capite '''demisso''' terram intueri.|trans=Caesar noticed that the Sequani were the only people of all who did none of those things which the others did, but, with their heads '''bowed down''', gazed on the earth in sadness.}}
# to [[cast]] down, [[throw]], [[thrust]], [[plunge]], [[drive]]
# {{lb|la|with se}} to let oneself down, [[stoop]], [[descend]], [[walk]] or [[ride]] down
# {{lb|la|military}} to send, bring or [[lead]] [[soldier]]s down into a [[lower]] place
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to cast down, [[demote]]; [[depress]], [[dispirit]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[engage]] in, [[enter]] or [[embark]] upon, [[meddle]] with

