Page 2032 desum: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{prefix|la|dē|sum}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|dēsum|eccl=1}}
* Note: The ēe found in forms such as dēesse, dēerunt, dēest frequently scans in poetry as a single syllable (an example of synizesis).

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg|dēsum}}

# to be [[wanting]]/[[lacking]] (+ [[Appendix:Glossary#dative case|dative]])
#: {{syn|la|careō|egeō|indigeō|dēlinquō|deficiō|cessō|perdō}}
#: {{ant|la|flōreō|niteō|abundō|affluō}}
#: {{ux|la|Dominus pāscit mē et nihil mihī '''dēerit'''.|The Lord is my shepherd and nothing '''shall I want'''.|lit=The Lord tends me as a shepherd and nothing for me '''will be lacking'''.}}
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Titus Livius|Titus Livius]], [[w:Ab Urbe Condita Libri|Ab Urbe Condita]], I, 36|quote={{l|la|equitem}} {{l|la|maxime}} {{l|la|suis}} '''deesse''' {{l|la|viribus}} {{l|la|ratus}}|t=thought that cavalry was what he chiefly lacked}}
# to [[fall short]] of, [[fail]] to [[obtain]], [[miss]]
#: {{syn|la|discēdō|dēficiō|cadō|dēlinquō}}
#: {{ant|la|perficiō|impetrō|perpetrō|ēvincō}}
# to [[abandon]], to [[desert]], to [[neglect]]
#: {{syn|la|relinquō|omittō|dēdō|concēdō|dēcēdō|dēserō|reddō|remittō|dēstituō|dēficiō|oblīvīscor|cēdō|permittō|dissimulō|trādō|addīcō|praetereō|neglegō|pōnō}}
#: {{ux|la|Dīmicantī dē fāmā '''dēesse'''.|t='''To abandon''' one whose reputation is attacked.|lit='''To abandon''' against the pummeling of fame.}}
# to be [[away]], to be [[absent]], to be [[missing]]
#: {{syn|la|absum}}
#: {{ant|la|adsum|stō}}

====Usage notes====
Due to the lack of passive forms, "to be missed" as in "to not get hit" is expressed with the following translation: English [object missed in subject form] + [form of ''to be''] + ''missed by'' + [object that misses in object form] becomes [object that misses in subject form] + [form of desum] + [object missed in object form]. "She is missed by us," as in "She does not get hit by us," for example, becomes "Eam desumus," which literally means "We miss her," as in "We do not hit her."

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|irreg|dēsum}}

===References===
* {{R:L&S|dēsum|desum}}
* {{R:Elementary Lewis}}
* {{R:Gaffiot|dēsum|p=510}}
* {{R:M&A}}
* {{R:OLD|1|dēsum|529}}
-------- end text --------
