Page 2085 differo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*bʰer-|*telh₂-|id2=bear}}
From {{prefix|la|dis|ferō|gloss1=apart|gloss2=carry, bear}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|differō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg|differō|dis|dī}}

# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[carry]] different ways, [[spread]], [[scatter]], [[disperse]], [[separate]]
#: {{syn|la|diffundō|fundō|effundō|confundō|dēfundō|dissipō|indūcō|sternō}}
# {{lb|la|transitive|figuratively}} to [[distract]], [[disquiet]] or [[disturb]] someone; [[confound]]
#: {{syn|la|disturbō|turbō|perturbō|sollicitō|agitō}}
# {{lb|la|transitive|figuratively}} to spread, [[publish]], [[circulate]], [[divulge]]; [[cry]] down, [[defame]]
# {{lb|la|transitive|figuratively}} to [[defer]], [[put off]], [[protract]], [[delay]], [[adjourn]]
#: {{syn|la|moror|dētineō|cūnctor|retardō|tardō|dubitō|prōtrahō|trahō}}
#: {{ant|la|ruō|currō|accurrō|trepidō|festīnō|prōvolō|properō|corripiō|affluō|mātūrō}}
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Proverbs|13|12|quote=Spēs quae '''differtur''' adflīgit animam: lignum vītae dēsīderium veniēns.|trans=''Hope that is '''deferred''' afflicteth the soul: desire when it cometh, is a tree of life.'' (Douay-Rheims trans., Challoner rev.: '''1752''' CE)}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to be [[different]], [[differ]], [[vary]]
#: {{syn|la|distō|dissideō|abhorreō}}

====Conjugation====
Irregular, but resembling the third conjugation. The principal parts come from several different words originally.
{{la-conj|irreg|differō|dis|dī}}

