Page 2147 disco: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|discō|eccl=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*deḱ-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*diskō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*didḱsḱéti|*di-dḱ-sḱe/o-}}, reduplicated durative form of {{m|ine-pro|*deḱ-||to take}}. From the same root as {{m|la|doceō}}; unrelated to {{m|la|discipulus}}.

Cognates include {{cog|grc|δέχομαι}}, whereas {{m|grc|δαῆναι}} is attributed to another root, {{m|ine-pro|*dens-}}, together with {{m|grc|δεδαώς}}, {{m|grc|δήνεα}} and {{m|grc|διδάσκω}}.

====Verb====
{{la-verb|3|discō|didic|discit}}

# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[learn]]
#: {{syn|la|capiō|percipiō|concipiō|comprehendō|intellegō|cognoscō|noscō|agnoscō|animadvertō|calleō|sciō}}
#: {{ux|la|Aut '''disce''' aut discēde.|Either '''learn''' or go away.}}
#: {{uxi|la|{{l|la|artem}} '''discere '''|t=to '''learn''' an art}}
#: {{uxi|la|{{l|la|aliquid}} {{l|la|ab}} {{l|la|aliquo}} '''discere '''|t=to '''learn''' something from someone}}
# {{lb|la|transitive}} {{lb|la|Late Latin}} to [[teach]]
#: {{syn|la|ērudiō|ēducō|doceō|ēdoceō|īnstruō|imbuō|fingō}}
# {{lb|la|drama|transitive}} to [[study]], [[practice]]
#: {{syn|la|studeō}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|3|discō|didic|discit}}

