Page 2208 dissimulo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*sem-}}
From {{affix|la|dissimilis|t1=unlike|-ō|id2=denominative}}, with ''i'' changed to ''u'' before a thick ''l''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|dissimulō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|dissimulō}}

# to [[conceal]], [[hide]], or [[dissimulate]] a state of mind
#: {{syn|la|vēlō|occultō|indūcō|operiō|obnūbō|occulō|condō|recondō|verrō|obruō|adoperiō|nūbō|tegō|abdō|abscondō|cooperiō|comprimō|prōtegō|premō|opprimō|mergō}}
#: {{ant|la|adaperiō|aperiō|patefaciō}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|516|quote='''Dissimulant''' et nūbe cavā speculantur amictī|trans='''''They hide their feelings''' and, veiled by the hollow cloud, they watch.''<br/>(Aeneas and Achates are '''hiding themselves''' within a divine cloud of mist, yet also '''concealing their emotions''' upon seeing fellow Trojans thought lost at sea.)''}}
# to [[dissemble]] or [[disguise]], [[pretend]]
