Page 2255 dormio: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*dormiō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*drem-||to run, sleep}}.<ref>{{R:Nocentini|hw=dormire}}</ref><ref>{{R:itc:EDL}}</ref>

Cognates include {{cog|cu|дрѣмати||to drowse, doze}}, {{cog|ru|дрема́ть}}, {{cog|sa|द्राति||to sleep}}, {{cog|grc|δαρθάνω||I sleep}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|dormiō}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-dormio.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|4++.nopass|dormiō}}

# to [[sleep]]
#: {{syn|la|obdormīscō|obdormiō|dormītō|obdormītō|cubō}}
#: {{ant|la|expergīscor|vigilō}}
#: {{ux|la|Eō '''dormītum'''.|I'm going to '''sleep'''.}}
#: {{ux|la|'''Dormītūrī''' tē salūtant.|Those (we) who '''are about to sleep''' salute you.}}
#* {{Q|la|Catullus|Carmina|5|quote=Nōbīs cum semel occidit brevis lūx, nox est perpetua ūna '''dormienda'''.|t=When the brief light has set on us, we must '''sleep''' one eternal night.}}
#* {{Q|la|Horace|Sermones|2|1|7|quote=vērum nequeō '''dormīre'''|t=In truth, I can't '''sleep'''.}}
#* '''4th-century CE''', Jerome of Stridon (St. Jerome), ''Vulgate'', 24:27:
#*: parum inquam '''dormiēs''' modicum '''dormitābis''' pauxillum manūs cōnserēs ut quiēscās
#*:: ''Thou wilt '''sleep''' a little, said I, thou wilt '''slumber''' a little, thou wilt fold thy hands a little to rest.''
#*::: (trans. Douay-Rheims Bible)

