Page 2259 drenso: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{unknown|la}}. Initial /dr/ does not occur in inherited Latin words that underwent regular development.  Possibly onomatopoeic. If borrowed from a Celtic or Germanic language, could be from {{der|la|ine-pro|*dʰer-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*dʰrēn-||drone; to murmur}}: initial *dʰ developed to /f/ in Latin, but to /d/ in those language groups. Compare {{cog|en|drone}}, {{m|en|dor}} and {{cog|grc|θρῆνος||dirge, lament}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|drēnsō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1.nopass|drēnsō}}

# {{lb|la|intransitive|of swans}} to [[cry]]

====Conjugation====
No perfect is attested.
{{la-conj|1.nopass|drēnsō}}

===References===
* {{R:L&S}}
* {{R:Gaffiot}}

