Page 2289 edo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₁ed-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*edō}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*h₁édti}}. The long vowel in some of the forms is probably due to {{w|Lachmann's law}}.

Cognates include {{cog|grc|ἔδω}}, {{cog|sa|अत्ति|tr=átti|}}, {{cog|hit|sc=Xsux|𒂊𒀉𒈪|tr=eidmi||I eat}}, {{cog|ang|etan}} ({{cog|en|eat}}), {{cog|lt|ėsti}} and {{cog|cy|ysu}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|edō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|irreg|edō}}

# to [[eat]]
#: {{syn|la|adedō|vēscor|vorō|pāscor|prandeō|cēnō|cōnsūmō}}
#: {{uxi|la|Tunc, modo '''edere''' volebat.|t=At that time, he just wanted '''to eat'''.}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|irreg|edō}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der2|la|adedō|comedō|edāx|edibilis|edūlis|ēsca|ēsor|ēsuriō|inedia|ēsus|obedō|ambadedō|ambedō|exedō|peredō|subedō|epulum}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|la|mandūcō}}

====References====
