* {{l|la|ecferō}}
* {{l|la|exferō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|irreg|efferō|ex|ē}}

# to [[bring]], [[bear]], [[carry]], [[take]] out, forth, away; [[transport]]
# to carry out (of the house) for [[burial]], bear to the [[grave]], [[bury]]
# to bring forth, bear, [[produce]], [[yield]]
# to [[emit]], [[discharge]], [[release]], [[send out]], send or bring forth
# to [[lift up]], [[elevate]], [[raise]], [[exalt]]; [[display]]; [[rescue]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[set forth]], [[spread]] abroad, [[utter]], [[publish]], [[proclaim]], [[pronounce]], [[express]], [[declare]], [[divulge]], [[make known]]
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Caesar|Caesar]]|[[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]]|VII, 1|quote=Priusquam eorum clandestina consilia '''efferantur'''|t=Before their secret plan be '''divulged'''}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively|usually|_|passive}} to [[carry away]], [[transport]], [[hurry]] or [[sweep]] away
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to raise, [[elevate]], [[exalt]], [[extol]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively|of speech or writing}} to [[exaggerate]], [[aggrandize]], [[embellish]], [[increase]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively|with se}} to elevate oneself; [[rise]], [[advance]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively|with se}} to be [[puff up|puffed up]], to be made [[haughty]] or [[proud]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively|rare}} to carry out to the [[end]], [[support]], [[endure]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|irreg|efferō|ex|ē}}

