Page 2451 escendo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|exscendō}}, {{l|la|excendō}}

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|la|ex|scandō|gloss2=to mount}}. The spelling with ''esc-'' instead of ''exsc-'' is probably caused by a replacement of /eksk/ with /esk/ (as in the word {{m|la|sescentī}}, standing for sex-centī), not by use of the long-vowel allomorph {{m|la|ē-}}, which is only regularly found before a voiced consonant ({{m|la|ēpōtō}} is an isolated exception).<ref>Leumann, Manu (1977) ''Lateinische Laut- und Formenlehre'', [https://books.google.com/books?id=ig4F_lvsZUYC&pg=PA203 Page 203]</ref> 

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|escendō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|escendō|escend|escēns}}

# to [[ascend]], [[go up]], [[mount]]
#: {{syn|la|īnscendō|cōnscendō|ascendō|succēdō|scandō|superscandō|suprascandō|ēnītor|subeō|ērēpō}}
#: {{ant|la|dēscendō|dēcurrō}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|escendō|escend|escēns}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|la|escēnsiō}}

===References===
<references/>

