===Etymology 1===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₁ed-}}
From {{suffix|la|edō|t1=I eat|-turiō|pos2=desiderative suffix}}.

====Verb====
{{la-verb|4++|ēsuriō}}

# to be [[hungry]], to [[hunger]] for something
#: '''''ēsurīs'''ne?'' - ''(Ita) '''ēsuriō'''.''
#:: Are you '''hungry'''? - (Yes) I am '''hungry'''.

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|4++|ēsuriō}}

=====Descendants=====
From the present participle {{m|la|ēsuriens}}:
* {{desc|en|esurient|bor=1}}

=====See also=====
* {{l|la|sitiō||to be thirsty}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{af|la|ēsuriō|-ō|t1=to be hungry|id2=noun}}.

====Noun====
{{la-noun|ēsuriō<3>|g=m}}

# a person that is [[hungry]], a [[hungry]] man

=====Declension=====
{{la-ndecl|ēsuriō<3>}}

===References===
* {{R:L&S}}
* {{R:Elementary Lewis}}
* {{R:Gaffiot}}
* {{R:M&A}}

