Page 2594 exorior: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{prefix|la|ex|orior}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|exorior}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|exorior|pres_actv_inf=exorīrī|exort}}

# to [[come]] out or forth, [[appear]]
#: {{syn|la|orior|coorior|oborior|ēmergō|pāreō|appāreō}}
#: {{ant|la|concēdō|decēdō|cēdō|intereō|discēdō|excēdō|pereō}}
# to [[become]]
# to [[begin]]
#: {{syn|la|incohō|occipiō|incipiō|coepiō|ōrdior|initiō|ineō|ingredior|aggredior|sūmō|moveō|committō|mōlior}}
#: {{ant|la|subsistō|dēsistō|cessō}}

====Usage notes====
* Part of a small group of verbs, all with a short-vowel root, displaying both 3rd and 4th conjugation forms.
* Present active infinitive only {{m|la|exorīrī}}, other 4th conjugation forms occur, particularly in manuscripts.
* Past participle exclusively {{m|la|exortus}}, future participle exclusively {{m|la|exoritūrus}}, gerund almost exclusively {{m|la|exoriundus}}.

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|exorior|exort|pres_actv_inf=exorīrī|1s_impf_actv_subj=exorīrer/exorerer|2s_impf_actv_subj=exorīrēris/exorīrēre/exorerēris/exorerēre|3s_impf_actv_subj=exorīrētur/exorerētur|1p_impf_actv_subj=exorīrēmur/exorerēmur|2p_impf_actv_subj=exorīrēminī/exorerēminī|3p_impf_actv_subj=exorīrentur/exorerentur}}

