Page 2605 expectoro: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{af|la|ex-|pectus|gloss2=chest; mind, spirit}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|expectorō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1.nopass|expectorō}}

# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[banish]] from one's [[mind]]
# {{lb|la|post-Classical}} to [[clear]] from one's [[chest]], [[lungs]]

====Usage notes====
The sense "banish from one's mind" was seen as archaic by Classical grammarians. The word was likely formed anew, with a more literal meaning, by Renaissance medical writers.

