Page 2612 expergiscor: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Probably a middle (passive in form) from {{m|la|ex}} + {{m|la|per}} + {{m|la|regō}} + {{m|la|-ēscō}}. Alternative etymology derives the last two syllables from unattested {{m|la||*griscor}}, based on {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₁ger-||to awaken}}, which dissimilated to {{m|la||*giscor}} after {{m|la|per-}}.<ref>{{R:ine:LIV|head=*h₁ger-|page=240}}</ref> It is not known how the transitive sense for English "wake up" got no direct counterpart, putting expergiscor in a similar situation to Spanish {{m|es|gustar}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|expergīscor}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|expergīscor|experrēct}} {{lb|la|intransitive}}

# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[awake]], to [[wake up]] (bestir oneself)
#: {{syn|la|vigilō}}
#: {{ant|la|obdormīscō|dormiō|obdormiō|dormītō|obdormītō|cubō}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|expergīscor|experrēct}}

===See also===
* {{l|la|expergēfaciō}}

===References===
<references/>

===Further reading===
* {{R:L&S}}
* {{R:Elementary Lewis}}
* {{R:Gaffiot}}
