Page 2614 experior: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*per-|id=risk}}
From {{m|la|ex||out}} + {{m|la|peritus||experienced, expert}}, perfect active participle of the unattested verb {{m|la|*perior||I go through}}, itself from {{der|la|ine-pro|*per-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|4.p3inf|experior|expert}}

# to [[attempt]], to [[try]]; to [[test]], to [[put to the test]], to [[find out]], to [[prove]]; therefore, to make trial of a person or thing
#: {{syn|la|periclitor|probō|temptō|spectō|explōrō}}
#* {{Q|la|Julius Caesar|Bello Gallico|1|44|quote=Si iterum '''experiri''' velint, se iterum paratum esse decertare; si pace uti velint, iniquum esse de stipendio recusare, quod sua voluntate ad id tempus pependerint.|trans=''If they chose '''to attempt''' a second trial, he was ready to encounter them again; but if they chose to enjoy peace, it was unfair to refuse the tribute, which of their own free-will they had paid up to that time.''}}
#* {{Q|la|{{w|Cicero|Marcus Tullius Cicero}}|{{w|Letters to Atticus|Epistulae ad Atticum}}|book 9, letter 10, section 3|year=44 BCE|quote=ut verum loquar, aetas iam a diuturnis laboribus devexa ad otium domesticarum me rerum delectatione mollivit. nunc si vel periculose experiundum erit, '''experiar certe''' ut hinc avolem. ante oportuit fortasse; sed ea quae scripsisti me tardarunt et auctoritas maxime tua.|trans=''To speak the truth, in my declining years I am, after my long labours and softened by the comforts of domestic life, inclined to rest. But now, even if the experience is dangerous, '''I shall at any rate try''' to fly away. Perhaps I ought to have done so earlier; but the aforesaid considerations, and above all your advice, served to detain me.''}}
#* {{Q|la|{{w|Cornelius Nepos}}|{{w|Excellentium Imperatorum Vitae}}|Liber Datames, chapter 2, section 3|year=~40 BCE|quote=is regi dicto audiens non erat. quam ob causam bello eum persequi constituit eique rei praefecit Datamen, propinquum Paphlagonis: namque ex fratre et sorore erant nati. quam ob causam Datames primum '''experiri''' voluit, ut sine armis propinquum ad officium reduceret. ad quem cum venisset sine praesidio, quod ab amico nullas vereretur insidias, paene interiit: nam Thuys eum clam interficere voluit.|trans=''Because that man (Thuys) was disobedient to him, the king decided to wage war on him and entrusted Datames, who was related to the Paphlagonian and sibling with him, with this commission. So Datames wanted '''to make an attempt''' to get his relative back to obedience without using force of arms. However, when he went to him without a guard because he feared no pursuit from his friend, he almost perished; for Thuys intended to secretly murder him.''}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|4|814|quote=‘magna fidēs avium est, '''experiāmur''' avēs.’|trans=''‘‘Great is the belief of bird omens; '''we shall put''' the birds '''to the test'''.’’''<br/>({{w|Romulus and Remus}} resort to {{w|augury}} or bird divination to settle their dispute.)}}
# to [[experience]], to [[go through]], to [[observe]], to [[suffer]], to [[endure]], to [[sustain]], to [[witness]]
#: {{syn|la|ūtor}}
# to [[do]], [[fare]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|4.p3inf|experior|expert}}

====Derived terms====
