===Etymology 1===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁(y)-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro||*fēlājō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁(y)-||to suck, suckle}}. Cognates include {{cog|sa|धयति}}, {{cog|grc|θηλή}}, {{cog|got|𐌳𐌰𐌳𐌳𐌾𐌰𐌽||suckle}}, and {{cog|cu|доити}}. Related to {{m|la|fēmina}}, {{m|la|fīlius}}, {{m|la|fētus}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|fēllō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|1+|fēllō}}<ref>{{R:L&S}}</ref><ref>{{R:Gaffiot}}</ref>

# to [[suck]]
# {{lb|la|vulgar|in particular}} to [[fellate]], [[perform]] [[fellatio]], [[suck off]]
#* {{quote-book|la|year=1st century {{CE}}|author=w:Martial|title=Epigrams|section=2.50|text=Quod '''fellas''' et aquam potas, nil, Lesbia, peccas:<br>qua tibi parte opus est, Lesbia, sumis aquam.|t=Because '''you suck''' [cock] and drink water, Lesbia, you err in nothing:<br>in just the part you ought to be, Lesbia, you're making use of the water.}}

=====Conjugation=====
