Page 2763 fero: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*bʰer-|*telh₂-|id2=bear}}
A {{glossary|suppletive}} paradigm consisting of two different roots.

The present stem is from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*ferō}} (infinitive {{m|itc-pro|*ferzi}}), from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*bʰéreti|t=to bear, carry}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}. Cognates include {{cog|sa|भरति|tr=bhárati}}, {{cog|fa|بار|tr=bâr}}, {{cog|xcl|բերեմ}}, {{cog|grc|φέρω}}, {{cog|ang|beran}} ({{cog|en|bear#Etymology_2}}).

The perfect stem, originally of {{m|la|tollō}}, is from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*tetolai}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*tetólh₂e|t=to be holding up}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*telh₂-}}. The stem of {{m|la|lātus}} has the same root, reduced from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*tlātos}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*tl̥h₂tós}}. It is cognate with {{cog|en|thole|t=to endure}}, {{cog|de|dulden|t=to endure}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|ferō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg|ferō}}

# to [[bear]], [[carry]]
#: {{syn|la|gerō|portō|vehō|efferō|trahō}}
#: {{uxi|la|partum '''ferre'''|to '''be''' with child, to  '''be''' pregnant (lit., ''to '''carry''' an offspring/fetus/embryo/one's young'')}}
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Genesis|1|2|quote=Terra [[autem]] erat [[inānis]] et [[vacuus|vacua]], et [[tenebrae]] erant super [[facies|faciem]] [[abyssus|abyssī]]: et [[spīritus]] Deī [[fero|ferēbātur]] super [[aqua|aquās]].|trans=And the earth was void and empty, and darkness was upon the face of the deep; and the spirit of God '''moved''' over the waters.}}
# to [[support]], [[hold up]]
# to [[suffer]], [[tolerate]], [[endure]]
#: {{syn|la|tolerō|sufferō|subeō|perferō|perpetior|recipiō|accipiō|sinō|patiō|sustentō|dūrō|sustineō}}
# to [[report]]
# to [[consider]]
# to [[cast]] (a vote); to [[pass]] or [[ratify]] (a law)
# to [[propose]]
# to [[win]]
# to [[create]]
# to [[bring forth]]; to [[put in motion]]; to [[move forward]]
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[lead]]
# to [[narrate]], [[recount]], [[quote]], [[cite]]
#: {{syn|la|referō|prōdō|pandō|trādō|dicitur}}
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Titus Livius|Titus Livius]]|[[w:Ab Urbe Condita Libri|Ab Urbe Condita]]|I, 4|quote=[[w:Faustulus|Faustulo]] {{l|la|fuisse}} {{l|la|nomen}} '''ferunt'''|t=It is '''narrated''' that his name was Faustulus}}

