Page 2792 flagro: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|flag;rō}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*flagrāō}}, from {{m|itc-pro|*flagros||burning}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro||*bʰl̥g-ro-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*bʰel-||shine}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL}}</ref> Cognate with {{cog|la|flamma||flame, fire}} (< {{cog|itc-pro|*flagma}} < {{cog|ine-pro||*bʰl̥g-mh₂-}}), {{cog|grc|φλέγω||I burn}}, {{cog|sa|भ्रज|tr=bhrája||fire, shining}}, {{cog|it|brace||embers, glowing coals}}.

====Verb====
{{la-verb|1+|flagrō}}

# to [[burn]], [[blaze]]
#: {{syn|la|[[uro|ūror]]|ārdeō|cōnflagrō|īnflammō|flammō|incendō|accendō|cremō|adoleō|caleō|dēflagrō|ferveō}}
#* '''106 - 43 {{B.C.E.}}''' — [[w:en:Marcus Tullius Cicero|Cicero]], ''Letters to Atticus'' 7:17.4
#*: ''tōtam enim Italiam '''flagrātūram''' bellō intellegō.''
#*:: For I perceive that all Italy will be blazing with war.

=====Conjugation=====
* Passive forms are predominantly post-Classical.
