#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|5|263-266|quote=‘sī bene '''flōruerint''' segetēs, erit āreā dīves;<br/>sī bene '''flōruerit''' vīnea, Bacchus erit;<br/>sī bene '''flōruerint''' oleae, nitidissimus annus,<br/>pōmaque prōventum temporis huius habent.’|trans=''“If the crops '''blossom''' well, the threshing floor will be rich; if the vineyard '''blossoms''' well, Bacchus will be [pleased]; if the olive trees '''blossom''' well, the year [will be] most polished [with oil], and fruits [will also] have the prosperity of this season.”''<br/>(Translating the Latin future perfect tense as English present tense. The poetic voice is that of {{w|Flora (mythology)}}.)}}
