Page 2816 foedo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{m|la|foedus||filthy}}. Compare {{cog|ang|bædan||to defile, pollute}}. More at {{l|en|bad}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|foedō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|foedō}}

# to make [[foul]] or [[filthy]], [[soil]], [[dirty]]; [[defile]], [[pollute]], [[disfigure]], [[mar]], [[deform]]
#* {{Q|la|Claudian|Panegyricus de Sexto Consulatu Honorii Augusti|537|thru=540|quote=Ipse favens votis solitoque decentior aër, quamvis adsiduo noctem '''foedaverat''' imbre, principis et solis radiis detersa removit nubila.|trans=The very weather, favoring our prayers and more decent than usual, although '''it had marred''' the night continually with rain, removed the clouds, wiped away by means of the rays of the sun and the emperor.}}
#* '''1425—1450''', (MS. Selden 55, Bodleian Library, Oxford) ''Vita Beati Eduardi Regis et Confessoris'', p. 371, lines 327-329:
#*: {{quote|la|''Mira Dei virtus! trabeam non ulcera '''foedant'''; purpuream regis nec fluxus sanguinis atri splendorem vestis minuit, sed fortius auxit.''
|translation=The extraordinary virtue of God! The sores do not '''defile''' the [[w:trabea|trabea]]; nor did the flow of black blood diminish the splendor of the clothes, the purple of the king, but more strongly emphasized it.}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[dishonor]], [[disgrace]]
#* {{Q|la|Pliny the Elder|Naturalis Historia|29|7|quote=(Graeci) nos quoque dictitant barbaros et spurcius nos quam alios Οπικων appellatione '''foedant'''.|trans=(The Greeks) also assert repeatedly that we are barbarians and that we are dirtier than others, '''dishonor''' us by calling us philistines.}}
#* '''1509—1513''', [[w:Ludovico Ariosto|Ludovico Ariosto]], ''De Diversis Amoribus'':
#*: {{quote|la|''Humanone trucem '''foedabo''' sanguine dextram, ut meus assiduo sub bove crescat ager?''
|translation='''Shall I disgrace''' my savage right hand with human blood, so that my field may continually thrive under the ox?}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+|foedō}}

===Adjective===
{{head|la|adjective form|head=foedō}}

# {{inflection of|la|foedus||dat//abl|m//n|s}}

===References===
* {{R:L&S}}
* {{R:Elementary Lewis}}
* {{R:Gaffiot}}
* {{R:M&A}}
