Page 2827 foro: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|forō}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*bʰerH-||to pierce, strike}}, with [[e-grade]] reflex attested in {{m|la|feriō}}. According to some the verb is [[denominal]] from {{m|ine-pro|*bʰorH-h₂||hole}}.

Compare, also from Proto-Indo-European: {{cog|lt|bárti||to accuse, scold}}, {{cog|cu|брати||to fight}}, {{cog|is|berja||to beat}}, {{cog|en|bore}}.

====Verb====
{{la-verb|1+|forō}}

# to [[bore]]
# to [[pierce]]
#* {{Q|la|T. Maccius Plautus|Mostellaria|1|1|quote=O carnuficium cribrum, quod credo fore, <br
/>ita te '''forabunt''' patibulatum per vias <br
/>stimulis carnufices, si huc reveniat senex.|trans=O I guess you will be the executioner's sieve, <br
/> for with pricks he will '''pierce''' you <br
/> gibbeted, as soon as the old man back comes}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|1+|forō}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|la|forābilis}}
* {{l|la|forāmen}}
* {{l|la|forātus}}
* {{l|la|perforō}}

