#: {{syn|la|īnfringō|irrumpō|rumpō|violō}}
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Lucas|9|16|quote=Acceptis autem quinque panibus et duobus piscibus, respexit in caelum et benedixit illis, et '''fregit''' et distribuit discipulis suis, ut ponerent ante turbas.|trans=Then he took the five loaves and the two fishes, and looking up to heaven, he blessed them, and '''broke''' them and gave them to the disciples to set before the multitude.}}
# {{lb|la|figurative}} to [[break]], [[shatter]] {{gl|a promise, a treaty, someone's ideas (dreams, projects), someone's spirit}}
# {{lb|la|figurative}} to [[break up]] into pieces {{gl|a war from too many battles, a nation}}
# {{lb|la|figurative}} to [[reduce]], [[weaken]] {{gl|one's desires, a nation}}
