Page 2843 fremo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*fremō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*bʰrem-}}. Cognates include {{cog|grc|βρέμω}}, {{cog|gmh|bremen}}, {{cog|cy|brefu}},<ref>http://www.indoeuropean.nl/cgi-bin/response.cgi?root=leiden&morpho=0&basename=\data\ie\greek&first=1581</ref> and obsolete {{cog|en|breme||famous; tempestuous}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|fremō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|fremō|fremu|fremit}}

# {{lb|la|transitive|with accusative}} to [[murmur]], [[mutter]], [[grumble]], [[growl]] at or after something
#: {{syn|la|mussitō}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|559-560|quote=Tālibus Īlioneus; cūnctī simul ōre '''fremēbant''' / Dardanidae.|trans=''With such [words spoke] Ilioneus; together all the Dardans '''were murmuring''' aloud [their assent].''<br/>(Ilioneus and other Dardan, i.e. Trojan, envoys are addressing Queen Dido; the meaning in-context is that of agreement which is audible – [[ore]], “by or with mouth” – yet respectful to her royal court.)}}
# {{lb|la|transitive|with accusative}} to [[complain]] [[loudly]]
#: {{syn|la|conqueror|queror|plōrō}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[roar]], [[growl]], [[hum]], [[rumble]], [[buzz]], [[howl]], [[snort]], [[rage]], murmur, mutter

