Page 2856 frigo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Possibly from {{der|la|ine-pro|*bʰer-|*bʰer(H)-g-}}; cf. {{cog|grc|φρύγω|t=I roast, bake}}, {{cog|sa|भृज्जति|t=to roast, grill, fry}}, {{m|sa|भृग्|t=the crackling of fire}}. However, Latin {{m|la||frīg-}} would point to {{m|ine-pro||*bʰreyg⁽ʰ⁾-}}, which lacks formal cognates. De Vaan suggests the word is a {{glossary|loan}} from late {{bor|la|grc|-}} or another source, following Giacomelli (1994), who assumes it is a late Greek borrowing. Probably related to {{cog|xum|frehtu}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=frīgō, -ere|page=243}}</ref> See also {{m|la|fertum}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|frīgō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|frīgō|frīx|frīct/frīx}}

# to [[roast]], [[fry]]
#: {{ux|la|Crēdere cāridem hanc orȳzam '''frīxisse''' abnegō |t=I refuse to believe that a shrimp '''fried''' this rice.}}
# to [[parch]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|frīgō|frīx|frīct/frīx}}

