Page 2888 furo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{unc|la}}. Used to calque Greek {{m|grc|Ἐρινύς}}, spirits of punishment in mythology. Possibly cognate with {{cog|sla-pro|*buřa}} (cf. {{cog|ru|буря||storm}}) and {{cog|sa|भुरति||to palpitate, quiver}}, which would point to {{der|la|ine-pro|*bʰwer-|*bʰur-}}.<ref>{{R:ru:Vasmer|буря}}</ref> Other proposed Proto-Indo-European origins include {{m|ine-pro|*dʰewh₂-||to smoke}}<ref>{{R:es:Roberts:2014}}</ref> and {{m|ine-pro|*dʰewH-||to shake; to rumble, roar}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|furō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|3.nopass|furō|furu}}

# to [[rave]] or [[rage]]
#: {{syn|la|saeviō|īrāscor|indignor|obīrāscor|queror}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|3.nopass|furō|furu}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|la|furenter}}
* {{l|la|furia}}
* {{l|la|furibundus}}
* {{l|la|furor}}

