Page 2892 fustigo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|la|fūstis|t1=a club, cudgel|-igō|t2=act with, do something with|id2=denominative}}, the latter a [[suffixal]] form of {{m|la|agō||I do, act}}. The long -ī- can be explained as a retention of the i-stem + the initial vowel of ''-igō'', cf. {{m|la|vectīgal}}, {{m|la|castīgō}}, and possibly {{m|la|fatīgō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|fūstīgō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|fūstīgō}}

# to [[club]] someone to [[death]]
#* {{Q|la|Victor Vitensis|Historia persecutionis Africae provinciae|2|14|year=c. 480-489|quote=In episcopos saevitia. [...] Tunc et venerabiles Mansuetum, Germanum, Fusculum, et multos alios '''fustigavit'''.|t=Fierce violence against bishops. [...] Therefore '''he beat''' the venerable Mansuetus, Germanus and Fusculus, and many others, '''with a club to death'''.}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+|fūstīgō}}

