Page 2910 gero: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₂eǵ-}}
From {{der|la|itc-pro|*gezō}} and cognate with {{cog|xfa|𐌊𐌄𐌔𐌄𐌕}}. According to De Vaan,<ref>{{R:itc:EDL}}</ref> from a post-PIE {{m|ine-pro|*h₂ǵ-es-}}, an extension of the {{der|la|ine-pro|-}} root {{m|ine-pro|*h₂eǵ-}} (from which {{m|la|agō}}); compare {{cog|gem-pro|*kas-|t=to bring up; throw}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|gerō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|gerō|gess|gest}}

# to [[carry]], [[bear]]
#: {{syn|la|ferō|portō|vehō|traho|effero}}
#: {{uxi|la|partum '''gerere'''|to '''be''' pregnant (lit., ''to be '''carrying''' an offspring/fetus/embryo/one's young'')}}
#: {{uxi|la|uterum '''gerere'''|to '''be''' pregnant (lit., ''to be '''bearing''' the womb'')}}
# to [[manage]], [[conduct]] {{gloss|e.g., one's affairs}}
#: {{syn|la|moderor|regō|prōcūrō|dispēnsō}}
# to [[rule]], [[govern]]
#: {{syn|la|dominor|imperō|magistrō|imperitō|rēgnō|regō|moderor|ōrdinō}}
# to [[wear]] (i.e. have on clothing)
#: {{syn|la|portō|vestītus}}
# to [[have]] or [[possess]] (of traits)
#: {{syn|la|habeo|teneo}}
# to [[perform]], [[accomplish]]
#: {{syn|la|perficiō|dēfungor|cōnficiō|agō|cumulō|conclūdō|condō|peragō|absolvō|inclūdō|claudō|expleō|fungor|efficiō|nāvō|patrō|exsequor|perpetrō|trānsigō|exhauriō}}
# to [[exhibit]], [[display]], [[reveal]]
#: {{syn|la|praebeō|ostendō|ostentō|expōnō|prōpōnō|prōferō|prōtrahō|acclārō|prōdō|indicō|profiteor|vulgō|praestō|coarguō|fateor}}
# to [[carry]] [[on]] or [[out]], [[wage]]
#: {{uxi|la|Bellum '''gerere'''|'''to wage''' war}}
#: {{uxi|la|Bellum '''gerant''' aliī.|Let others '''wage''' war.}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|23-24|quote=Id metuēns, veterisque memor Sāturnia bellī,<br/>'''prīma quod''' ad Trōiam prō cārīs '''gesserat''' Argīs.|trans=''Saturn’s [daughter was] fearing this [destiny], and [she was] ever-mindful of the old war against Troy '''which she had been the first to wage''' on behalf of her beloved Argos.''<br/>(A daughter of Saturn, Juno – having favored the Greeks and the Greek city Argos – had fought the Trojan war, and now fears the eventual rise of Rome. See: {{w|Juno (mythology)}}; {{w|Argos, Peloponnese}}.)}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|5|59|quote=‘Mārtis opus iuvenēs animōsaque bella '''gerēbant''' [...].’|trans=''‘‘Young men '''were carrying out''' the work of Mars and courageous wars [...].’’''<br/>(The voice is that of the muse {{w|Urania}}.)}}
# {{lb|la|reflexive}} to [[behave]], [[conduct]], [[comport]]

====Conjugation====
