Page 2969 haurio: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*auzjō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₂ews-|t=to scoop, draw water}}, whence also {{cog|gem-pro|*ausaną|t=to scoop, draw water}} and {{cog|grc|αὔω|t=to light a fire}}, with the {{ic|/h-/}} likely inserted by {{glossary|hypercorrection}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|hauriō|281}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|hauriō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|4|hauriō|haus|haust}}

# to [[draw]] (especially water), [[drain]]
# to drain, [[drink up]], [[swallow]]; [[absorb]]
#: {{syn|la|ēbibō|exhauriō}}
# {{lb|la|of blood}} to [[spill]], [[shed]]
# to [[devour]], [[consume]], [[exhaust]], [[deplete]], [[use up]]; [[engulf]]
#: {{syn|la|exhauriō|abūtor|absūmō|cōnsūmō|conterō|terō|accīdō}}
# to [[tear up]], [[pluck]] out, draw out; [[dig up]], [[hollow out]]
#: {{syn|la|carpō|āvellō|vellō|dēripiō}}
# to draw, [[derive]], [[borrow]], [[take]]
#: {{syn|la|capiō|trahō|dūcō}}
#* {{Q|la|Apuleius|3|24|quote=abiectīs properē laciniīs tōtīs, avidē manūs immersī et '''haurītō''' plūsculō cūncta corporis meī membra perfricuī.|t=I quickly threw off all my clothes, and eagerly put immersed my hands [in the jar with the magical substance], and '''having drawn''' a sizeable amount, I rubbed all parts of my body.}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|4|hauriō|haus|haust}}
* The supine stem ''haurītum'' is also attested (in the ablative ''haurītū'', in Apuleius), alongside the perfect participle ''haurītus'' and future active participle ''haurītūrus'' and ''hausūrus'' (the latter in various poets), even if uncommonly.

