Page 3009 iaceo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|la|jaceō}} {{qualifier|chiefly New Latin}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*(H)yeh₁-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*jakēō}}. [[w:Stative verb|Stative]] counterpart of {{m|la|iaciō||to throw}}. The meaning must have shifted from “I am thrown down” to “I lie”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|jaceō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2+.nopass|iaceō}}

# to [[lie]] [[prostrate]], [[lie down]]; [[recline]]
#: {{syn|la|cubō}}
#* Cur in terra '''iaces'''? — ''“Why '''are you lying''' on the ground?”''
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|1|218|quote=pauper ubīque '''iacet'''|trans=''and everywhere the poor man '''lies prostrated'''''}}
# to be [[sick]], lie ill
#: {{syn|la|aegrōtō|cubō}}
#: {{ant|la|valeō}}
# to [[linger]], [[stop]], [[tarry]], [[remain]]
# to be [[placed]] or [[situated]], lie
# to be [[low]], [[flat]] or [[level]]
# to lie [[still]]
# to have [[fall]]en, lie [[dead]]
# to lie in [[ruins]]
# to [[hang]] down loose
# {{lb|la|of the face or eyes}} to be [[fixed]] on the ground or [[cast]] down
# to be [[indolent]], [[idle]] or [[inactive]]
#: {{syn|la|langueō|dēsideō|vacō|cessō|resideō|sileō|conquiēscō}}
# to be of no [[avail]], lie [[dormant]] or [[abandoned]]
# to [[lodge]], [[dwell]], [[abide]]
#: {{syn|la|obsideō|cōnsīdō|possideō|habitō|subsīdō|resideō|incolō|colō|stabulō|vīvō|versō}}
# to lie [[overthrown]]; to be [[refuted]], [[fail]]; to be [[despised]]
# {{lb|la|of speech or language}} to be [[languid]], [[dull]] or [[lifeless]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|2+.nopass|iaceō}}

