# {{lb|la|chiefly|Old Latin|and|Late Latin}} to [[pollute]], [[defile]]
#* {{Q|la|Apuleius|Metamorphoses|1|18|quote=nox acerba dīrās et trucēs imāginēs obtulit, ut adhūc mē crēdam cruōre hūmānō aspersum atque '''impiātum'''.|t=the rough night brought me such dreadful and harsh dreams that I still feel splashed and '''polluted''' with human blood.}}

====Usage notes====
Rarely used in Classical Latin, but encountered in Plautus, the archaizing Apuleius, and Late Latin authors such as Ammianus Marcellinus and Prudentius.

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+|impiō}}

===References===
* {{R:L&S}}
* {{R:Gaffiot}}
* {{R:NLW}}
