#* {{Q|la|Hyginus|Fabulae|125|year=64 BCE - 17 CE|quote=Ulixes, cum videret eius immanitati atque feritati resistere se non posse, vino quod a Marone acceperat eum '''inebriavit'''.|t=Odysseus, now seeing he couldn't resist the [Cyclops's] size and strength, '''made''' him '''drunk''' with the vine he had received from Maro.}}
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Proverbia|5|19-20|quote=Ubera eius '''inebrient''' te omni tempore; in amore illius delectare iugiter. / Quare seducēris, fili mi, ab aliena, et foveris sinu alterius?|t=May her [your wife's] breasts '''inebriate''' you at all times; delight constantly in her love. Why would you be seduced by another woman, my son, and so favour another's bosom?}}
# to [[saturate]] something with a liquid (e.g. [[overwater]]ing plants)
#* {{Q|la|Pliny the Elder|Naturalis Historia|9|139|quote=Non est satis abstulisse gemmae nomen amethystum: rursum absolutum '''inebriatur''' Tyrio.|t=It is not enough to have extracted amethyst (the precious stone's name): '''it should be saturated''' again with Tyrian purple to perfection.}}

