Page 3508 invideo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|la|in-|id1=after|t1=after|videō|t2=see, observe; understand}}. The meaning developed from “look back at” to “look askance at” to “envy”.<ref>{{R:ine:LIPP|vol=2|pages=243}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|invideō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2|invideō|invīd|invīs}}

# {{lb|la|ambitransitive}} to [[look]] [[askance]] or [[maliciously]] at, [[cast]] an [[evil]] [[eye]] upon
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to be [[prejudiced]] against someone or [[influenced]] by [[prejudice]]
## {{lb|la|by extension}} to be [[unwilling]] or [[loath]]; [[begrudge]]; [[refuse]], [[deny]]; [[hinder]], [[prevent]]
##* {{Q|la|Ovid|Metamorphoses|4|154|thru=157|quote=hoc tamen amborum verbis estote rogati,<br/>o multum miseri meus illiusque parentes,<br/>ut, quos certus amor, quos hora novissima iunxit,<br/>conponi tumulo non '''invideatis''' eodem|trans=''Wretched parents of Pyramus and Thisbe, listen to us,<br/>Listen to both our prayers, do not '''begrudge''' us,<br/>Whom death has joined, Iying at last together<br/>In the same tomb.''}}
## {{lb|la|by extension}} to [[envy]]; [[emulate]], [[aspire]] to [[rival]]
##: {{syn|la|aemulor}}
##* {{Q|la|Ovid|Metamorphoses|5|657|thru=659|quote=barbarus '''invidit''' tantique ut muneris auctor<br/>ipse sit, hospitio recipit somnoque gravatum<br/>adgreditur ferro|trans=''The barbarian '''envies''' him; and that he himself may be deemed the author of so great a benefit,<br/>he receives him with hospitality, and, when overpowered with sleep,<br/>he attacks him with the sword.''}}
##* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Proverbs|28|22|quote=Vir, quī festīnat dītārī, et aliīs '''invidet''', ignōrat quod egestās superveniet eī.|trans=''A man, that maketh haste to be rich, and '''envieth''' others, is ignorant that poverty shall come upon him.''<br/>''(Douay-Rheims trans., Challoner rev.: '''1752''' CE)''}}

====Usage notes====
Used in the following constructions: (1) can use the accusative with things or the dative with persons; and (2) can use the dative with the person or thing that causes envy; or the dative and/or ablative.

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|2|invideō|invīd|invīs}}

