Page 3528 irrumo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{af|la|in-|ruma|-ō|t2=teat|id3=denominative|id1=in}}. The original meaning is hypothesized to have been "give suck to; [[suckle]]; nurse"; compare the development of {{m|la|fēllo|t=to suck; to fellate}}.<ref>{{cite-book |last=Adams |first=J.N. |date=1990 |title=The Latin Sexual Vocabulary|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=GDP9VHGbF1AC&pg=PA126 |publisher=JHU Press |page=126 |isbn=9780801841064 |text=''Irrumo'' in etymology reflects the popular obsession among Latin speakers with a similarity felt between feeding and certain sexual practices [...] It is a denominative of ''ruma'' / ''rumis'', 'teat', and would originally have meant 'put in the teat'.}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|irrumō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|irrumō}}

# {{lb|la|vulgar}} to [[facefuck]], [[irrumate]]
#* {{Q|la|Catullus|Carmina|16|1|quote=[[pēdīcō|Pēdīcābo]] ego vōs et '''irrumābō'''.|t=I will sodomize you and '''facefuck''' you.}}
# to [[abuse]], [[defile]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+|irrumō}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|la|irrumātio}}
* {{l|la|irrumātor}}

====Descendants====
