Page 3547 iuvo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From older {{der|la|la|iuvere}}, apparently a simple [[w:Thematic_vowel#Verbs|thematic verb]], to which ''iuvāre'' may originally be an [[iterative]]. Maybe cognate with {{cog|hit|iyauwatta|t=to be healed, recover}} ([[middle voice]], meaning developed from "to help oneself"), in which case it is reconstructable as {{der|la|ine-pro||*h₁i-h₁éwH-ti|t=to help}}, from root {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₁ewH-}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=iuvō}}</ref><ref>{{R:ine:LIV|pages=243-44}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|juvō}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-iuvo.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1|iuvō|iūv|iūt}}

# to [[help]], [[aid]]; [[save]]
#: {{syn|la|adiūtō|adiuvō|foveō|assistō|succurrō|sublevō|prōficiō|prōsum|adsum}}
#: {{ant|la|officiō}}
#: {{uxi|la|[[w:Fortune favours the bold|audaces fortuna '''iuvat''']]|t=Fortune '''favours''' the brave}} ([[w:Virgil|Virgil]], [[w:Aeneid|Aeneid]])
# to [[delight]], [[gratify]], [[please]]
#: {{syn|la|dēlectō|fruor|congrātulor|exhilarō}}

