===Etymology 2===
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*(s)leh₂b-||to hang loosely, be weak}}. Cognate with {{m|la|labō}}, {{cog|en|sleep}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|lābor}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|3|lābor|lāps}}

# {{senseid|la|slip}} to [[slip]], [[slide]], [[glide]]
# to [[fall]], sink down
# to [[slip]], [[stumble]]
# to [[vanish]], [[pass]] [[away]], [[elapse]], [[escape]]
#: {{syn|la|fugiō|effugiō|ēvādō|refugiō|cōnfugiō|diffugiō|aufugiō|prōfugiō|āvolō|ēripiō|ēlābor}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|6|771-772|quote=Tempora '''lābuntur''', tacitīsque senēscimus annīs,<br/>et fugiunt frēnō nōn remorante diēs.|trans=''Times '''pass away''', and with years unnoticed we grow old, and days flee with no bridle holding [them] back.''}}
# {{senseid|la|be mistaken}} to be mistaken, [[be wrong]], [[err]], commit a fault
#: {{syn|la|dēlinquō|errō|committō|offendō}}

=====Conjugation=====
This verb takes the future passive participle {{m|la|lābundus}} instead of ''*lābendus''.
