===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*lakjō||to draw, pull}}, with no known cognates in any other Indo-European languages.

Unused outside of glosses, reconstructed by [[grammarian]] Festus Grammaticus to explain its derivatives, see {{m|la|laqueus}}, {{m|la|lacessō}} and frequentative {{m|la|lactō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|laciō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|laciō|licu|lact}} {{tlb|la|very rare}}

# to [[entice]], [[ensnare]]
#* {{RQ:Paul.Fest.|116|15
|passage='''Lacit''' dēcipiendō indūcit. Lax etenim fraus est.
|translation='''''Lacit''''', deceives by beguiling. For {{m|la|lax}} means deceit.}}
#* '''8th C. {{CE|nodots=yes}}''', ''Glossae codicis Sangallensis'', leaf 75 verso in ''Corpus Glossariorum Latinorum'' (volume IV), [[w:Georg Goetz|Georg Goetz]] (editor), [[w:Bibliotheca Teubneriana|Bibliotheca Teubneriana]], page [https://archive.org/stream/corpusglossario01leipgoog#page/n295/mode/1up 253], line 41:
#*: {{quote|la|'''Lacit''' captat suādet
|translation='''''Lacit''''': to entice, to deceive}}

