Page 3584 laedo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Of {{unc|la|nocap=1}} origin<ref>{{R:la:WH|head=laedo|page=749|vol=1}}</ref>; proposed derivations include:
* From a {{der|la|ine-pro|-}} root common to {{cog|grc|λίθος||stone}}, {{m|grc|λίστρον||spade, shovel}} and {{cog|lv|lîžu||to clear a land}}.
* From {{der|la|ine-pro|-}} {{m|ine-pro|*(s)leyd-|*slaid-, *sled-}}, a root common to {{cog|gem-pro|*slītaną|t=to tear apart}}.
* From a {{der|la|ine-pro|-}} root common to {{cog|non|lesta||to damage}}, {{m|non|lǫstr||damage}} and {{cog|grc|λαιδρός||bold}}.
* From {{der|la|ine-pro|*deh₂y-dʰeh₁-e/o-||to put in one's share}}, a compound of {{compound|ine-pro|*deh₂y-|*dʰeh₁-}}.<ref>[https://www.academia.edu/40366912/What_became_of_Sabine_l_An_overlooked_Proto-Italic_sound_law Prósper, Blanca María (2019), What became of "Sabine l"? An overlooked Proto-Italic sound law]</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|laedō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|laedō|laes|laes}}

# to [[strike]], [[collide]], [[hurt]]
# to [[offend]]
# to [[thwart]]
# to [[betray]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|laedō|laes|laes}}

