Page 3611 lateo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*leh₂-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*latēō||t=to be hidden}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*leh₂-||to hide}}. Compare cognate {{cog|grc-dor|λᾱ́θω||to escape notice}}, variant of {{cog|grc|λανθάνω}};´also compare {{cog|grc-ion|λάθρῃ||secretly, by stealth; unbeknownst to}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|eccl=yes|vul=1|lateō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2.nopass|lateō|latu}}

# to [[conceal]], [[hide]], [[lie]] [[hidden]], [[lurk]], [[skulk]]
#: {{ux|la|'''Latet''' anguis in herbā.|t=A snake '''hides''' in the grass.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|la|Sub nōmine pācis bellum '''latet'''.|t=War '''lurks''' under the name of peace.|inline=1}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|2|72|quote=posita sub nive terra '''latet'''|trans=''the earth '''lies hidden''' under fallen snow''}}
# to keep out of [[sight]]
# to be [[hidden]] and in safety
# to [[live]] in concealment; to live [[retired]]
# {{lb|la|intransitive|transitive}} to [[escape]] [[notice]], [[remain]] unknown
#: {{ux|la|Bene quī '''latuit''', bene vīxit.|t=He who has well '''remained unknown''' has lived well.|inline=1}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|130|quote=nec '''latuēre''' dolī frātrem Jūnōnis et īrae||t=Nor did the tricks and the angers of Juno '''escape''' her brother's '''notice'''.}}
# to be [[obscure]] or [[unknown]], [[lie]] [[hidden]]
#: {{ux|la|Id quā ratiōne cōnsecūtus sit '''latet'''.|t=It '''is unknown''' how he obtained that.|inline=1}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|2.nopass|lateō|latu}}

