===Etymology 1===
{{unk|la|Disputed}}. Often hypothesized as from {{der|la|ine-pro|*leh₂t-|t=to grant; to possess}} or {{m|ine-pro|*leh₁-|*leh₁-t-|to let, grant, provide}}, when compared with {{cog|grc|λάτρις||hired servant}} and {{cog|gem-pro|*lēþą||ownership, possession}}. However, Beekes rejects an Indo-European etymology on phonetic grounds and instead posits {{der|la|qsb-grc}} origin for the Greek; he believes {{m+|la||latrō}} is rather borrowed from unattested {{bor|la|grc||*λάτρων}}.<ref>{{R:grc:EDG|head=λάτρον|pages=837–838}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|lat;rō}}

====Noun====
{{la-noun|latrō<3>|g=m}}

