Page 3625 lego: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*leǵ-}}
From {{der|la|itc-pro|*legō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*leǵ-}}. Cognates include {{cog|grc|λέγω|t=I speak, I choose, I mean}} and {{cog|sq|mbledh}}. May be related to {{m|la|lēx}}.<ref>{{R:Etymonline|entry=legal}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|legō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|3|legō|lēg|lēct}}

# to [[choose]], [[select]]
#: {{syn|la|dēligō|ēligō|optō|adoptō|dēsūmō|sēpōnō|dēstinō|sūmō|capiō|creō}}
# to [[appoint]]
#: {{syn|la|dēlēgō|dēsignō|assignō|mandō|dēmandō|tribuō|īnstituō|impertiō|elēgō|appōnō|prōdō|cōnsociō|ōrdinō|distribuō|attribuō|discrībō|addīcō}}
#* {{Q|la|Livy|Ab Urbe Condita|26|1|quote={{...}} dum ne quem militem '''legeret''' ex eo numero quibus senatus missionem reditumque in patriam negasset ante belli finem.|year=27-25 BCE|trans={{...}} provided he did not '''choose''' any soldier from those to whom the Senate had refused discharge and a return home before the end of the war}}
# {{senseid|la|gather}} to [[collect]], [[gather]], bring together
#: {{syn|la|cōgō|contrahō|cōnferō|congerō|coniungō|concieō|cōnserō|convehō|cōnstruō|glomerō|concitō|colligō}}
# to [[take out]], [[pick out]], [[extract]], [[remove]]
# to [[take]] to one's self [[unjustly]], [[carry off]], [[steal]], [[purloin]], [[plunder]], [[abstract]]
#: {{syn|la|āmoveō|removeō|adimō|dēmō|eximō|tollō|auferō|āvertō|abdūcō|excipiō|extrahō|ēvehō}}
# to [[read]]
#:{{uxi|la|Librōs '''lege'''.|'''Read''' books.}}
#:{{uxi|la|'''Lēgistī'''ne hunc librum?|Have you '''read''' this book?}}
#:{{uxi|la|Lingua Graeca est; nōn potest '''legī'''.|It's Greek; it cannot be '''read'''.}}
#* {{Q|la|Martial|Epigrams|7|77|quote=Exigis, ut nostrōs dōnem tibi, Tucca, libellōs.<br />Nōn faciam: nam vīs vēndere, nōn '''legere'''.|trans=You demand that I give our [⇒ my] little books to you, Tucca.<br/>I will not do [it]: for you want to sell [them], not to '''read''' [them].}}
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin}} to [[teach]], [[profess]]
#: {{syn|la|doceō|discō|īnstruō|ēducō|ērudiō|ēdoceō|magistrō|fingō}}

