#: {{syn|la|perlūstrō}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[circle]], move in a circle [[around]]. {{q|because the priest offering such sacrifice did so}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Ibis|111|thru=112|quote=Exul inops errēs aliēnaque līmina '''lūstrēs''',<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;exiguumque petās ōre tremente cibum.|trans=May you wander as a poor exile and '''go round''' others' thresholds,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;and ask with a trembling mouth for a bit of food.}}
# to [[wander]] over, [[traverse]], [[roam]]
#: {{syn|la|errō|pervagor|peragrō|vagor|discurrō|pererrō|perlūstrō|pālor}}
