===Etymology 2===
In sense 1, from {{suffix|la|lustrum|alt1=lustra|ō|t1=[[brothel]], place of debauchery|pos2=noun-forming suffix|id2=noun}} (compare {{m|la|lustror|t=to frequent brothels}}).<ref name="De Vaan">{{R:itc:EDL|head=lutum|page=355}}</ref> Sense 2 is possibly a reinterpretation based on the alternative sense of {{m|la|lustrum|lustra|t=[[wilds]], [[woods]], [[forest]]}} or influenced by the etymologically unrelated verb {{m|la||lūstrō| t=wander over, traverse, roam}} (see above).

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|lustrō}}

====Noun====
{{la-noun|lustrō<3>|g=m}} {{tlb|la|uncommon}}

# frequenter of [[brothel|brothels]]/places of ill repute<ref name="De Vaan"></ref><ref name="Gaffiot">{{R:Gaffiot}}</ref>
#* {{Q|la|Gnaeus Naevius|Com|118|quote=Pessimorum pessime, audax, [[ganeo]] '''lustro''' [[aleo]]!|refn=<ref name=Ribbeck>{{cite-book|title=Scaenicae Romanorum poesis fragmenta|volume=2 Comicorum fragmenta|editor=Ribbeck, Otto|year=1898|location=Leipzig|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/scaenicaeromanor02ribbuoft/page/30/mode/2up|page=31}}</ref>|trans=Worst of the worst, bold, glutton, '''[[barfly]]''', gambler|transauthor=Amy Richlin<ref>{{cite-book|author=Amy Richlin|year=2017|title=Slave Theater in the Roman Republic: Plautus and Popular Comedy|page=165|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=88g-DwAAQBAJ&pg=PA165}}</ref>|transyear=2017}}
#* {{Q|la|Gnaeus Naevius|Com|120|quote=[[vagus|Vagus]] est et '''lustro'''|refn=<ref name=Ribbeck></ref>}}
# [[vagabond]], [[wanderer]], [[roamer]]<ref name="L&S">{{R:L&S}}</ref>
#* {{Q|la||Thesaurus novus Latinitatis|313|year=c. 1150-1180|quote=hic '''lustro''', nis ·i· ille qui vagus est et nihil agit nisi fora lustrat, unde Naevius de quodam: vagus, inquit, est et lustro|notes=first published by [[w:Angelo Mai|Angelo Mai]] in Auctores Classici Vol. 8; authorship now attributed to [[w:Osbern of Gloucester|Osbernus of Gloucester]]|refn=<ref name=Ribbeck></ref>}}
#* {{Q|la|Osbern of Gloucester|Derivationes|193|year=c. 1150-1180|quote=Errabundus, erratilis, vagus, '''lustrones''', qui vagi sunt et instabiles|refn=<ref>{{cite-book|title=Classicorum auctorum e vaticanis codicibus editorum tomus 1.10. ... curante Angelo Maio Vaticanae Bibliothecae Praefecto Tomus 8|year=1836|page=193|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_XAHW9aVTCEAC/page/192}}</ref><ref>{{R:DMLBS}}</ref>}}

