=====References=====
* {{R:L&S}}
* {{R:Elementary Lewis}}
* Enrico Olivetti. [https://www.dizionario-latino.com/dizionario-latino-italiano.php?lemma=MANDO300 Dizionario] Latino
* {{R:Gaffiot}}
* {{R:M&A}}

===Etymology 2===
{{unc|la}}, but probably from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*mandnō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*menth₂-}}, from a root {{m|ine-pro|*meth₂-}}. For the phonetic development, ''LIV'' and de Vaan suggest that a nasal-infixed verb {{m|ine-pro||{{nowrap|*m̥t-né-h₂-ti}} ~ {{nowrap|*m̥t-n̥-h₂-énti}}}} underwent voicing {{glossary|assimilation}} of {{m|itc-pro||*mat-n-}} > {{m|itc-pro||*mad-n-}} followed by {{glossary|metathesis}} of {{m|itc-pro||*madn-}} > {{m|itc-pro||*mand-}} on the way to Latin,<ref>{{R:ine:LIV|head=*''meth₂-'' ‘wegreißen’|pages=442–443}}</ref><ref>{{R:itc:EDL|mandō, -ere|pages=361–362|passage=PIt. *''mand-n-'' ‘to stir > chew’; PIE *mt-n(é)-h₂- [pr.] ‘to stir, whirl’}}</ref> parallel to the development of {{m|la|pandō}} from {{m|ine-pro|*peth₂-}}. The semantic development is disputed:
* De Vaan 2008 suggests {{der|la|ine-pro|*menth₂-|t=to stir, whirl}} > "chew", as in {{cog|txb|mintanaṃ||to mix (clay with water)}}, {{cog|sa|मन्थति|tr=mánthati|t=to whirl, rub, shake}}, {{cog|os|yzmæntyn}}, {{m|os|æzmæntun||to shake, stir around}}, {{cog|lt|mę̃sti||to mix}}, {{cog|cu|мѧсти||to stir, trouble}}.
* WH, IEW, LIV, Meiser refer it to {{der|la|ine-pro|*menth₂-|t=tear away}}, as in {{cog|sa-ved|मथीत्|tr=máthīt}}, {{cog|sa|मथ्नाति|tr=mathnā́ti||to rob, snatch away; kill; seize by force; to stir; to injure}}, {{cog|xto|mäntācär|pos=2pl.||you are injured}}.

Other possible cognates include:
* {{cog|la|māsū̆cius||voracious}}; possibly also {{cog|la|māla}}, depending on its etymology.
* {{cog|grc|μασάομαι||to chew}}, {{m|grc|μαστιχάω||to gnash the teeth}} (whence {{m+|la|masticō}}), {{cog|grc|μάσταξ||mouth, jaws}}. On the basis of Latin and Greek, {{der|la|ine-pro|*mendʰ-||to chew}} was once proposed; however, the Greek cognates suffer etymological issues which may indicate {{cog|qsb-grc}} {{cog|qfa-sub}} origin.<ref>{{R:grc:EDG|909|μασάομαι}}</ref><ref>{{R:grc:EDG|911|μάσταξ, -ακος}}</ref>
* words for “mouth” or “jaw”: {{cog|gem-pro|*munþaz}}, {{m+|la|mentum||chin}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|3|mandō|mand|māns}}

# {{senseid|la|chew}} to [[chew]], [[masticate]]
#: {{syn|la|masticō|manducō|ruminō}}
# to [[bite]], [[gnaw]]
# {{lb|la|Late Latin}} to [[eat]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|3|mandō|mand|māns}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|la|mandibula}}
* {{l|la|mandūcus}}
* {{l|la|mandūcō}}

