{{univerbation|la|manū|t1=in/by the hand|teneō|t2=to hold}}, one of the meanings being "to hold fast". Appears to underlie numerous {{w|Western Romance}} forms, but unknown in southern varieties and not attested in this use until the 11th century, therefore likely to be a calque of the {{calque|la|roa|maintenir|notext=1}} forms themselves.

