Page 3752 masturbor: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{unc|la}}. Traditionally suggested to be a compound of {{m|la|manus||hand}} + {{m|la|turbāre|t=to unsettle, throw in to disorder}}, or a deformed compound of {{m|la|manus|t=hand}} + {{m|la|stuprāre|t=to defile (the self)}}, from {{m|la|stuprum}}, with influence from {{m|la|turbāre}}.  In that case the vowel ''a'' would be expected to be long and nasalized, via /mans.t-/, as in {{m|la|mōnstrum}}. Some suggest the first part to be an unattested meaning of {{m|la|mās|t=the male}} as “penis” (see de Vaan).

Watkins has traced the root to a {{der|la|ine-pro|*mostr̥gʰ-}}, extended and metathesised from {{m|ine-pro|*mosgʰos|t=marrow}}, also found in {{cog|ae|𐬨𐬀𐬯𐬙𐬆𐬭𐬆𐬔𐬀𐬥|t=brains}} and {{cog|txb|mrestīwe|t=marrow}}. The semantic relationship is due to the widely attested belief that semen descends from the brain through the bones and is the same substance as brain matter and bone marrow; compare “the symbolic autofellatio of {{w|Fionn mac Cumhaill|Finn mac Cumaill}}'s gnawing his thumb to the marrow” and the obsolete meaning of {{m|en|marrow||semen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|masturbor}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|masturbor}}

# to [[masturbate]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+|masturbor}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|la|masturbātiō}}
* {{l|la|masturbātor}}

===References===
* {{R:L&S}}
* {{R:du Cange|MASTURBARE}}
* {{R:Gaffiot|p=953/2}}
* {{R:OLD|1|masturbor|1,082/2}}
* {{R:OED2|masturbate}}
* {{R:ine:HKD||535}}
* {{R:NLW|masturbo}}
* {{R:itc:EDL|head=mās, maris}}
