From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*mentjōr}}, denominal verb from {{m|la|mens|mēns, mentis|mind}}. The meaning "to lie" stems from a [[semantic shift]] "to be inventive, have second thoughts" > "to lie, conjure up". Compare {{m|la|comminīscor}} also from this root and again with these meanings.

