===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*(s)mer-|id=allot}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*merēō}}, cognate of Ancient Greek {{l|grc|μέρος||share, portion}} (from {{der|la|ine-pro|*(s)mer-||to assign, allot}}) {{suf|la||-eō}}. See also {{cog|la|merx}}, {{cog|grc|μείρομαι||to receive as one's portion or due}} and {{cog|hit|𒈥𒀝𒍣|tr=mar-ak-zi|ts=marktsi|t=to cut up, divide (a sacrifice), separate, unravel}}.

