Page 3799 minuo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*minwō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*mey-||small, little}}, either {{m|ine-pro||*mi-néw-ti}}<ref>{{R:gem:PIEPG|page=139}}</ref> or {{m|ine-pro||*mi-néh₁-ti}}. Cognate with {{cog|sa|मीनाति|tr=minā́ti|t=to lessen, diminish, damage}} (also {{m|sa|मिनोति|tr=minóti}}), {{cog|grc|μινύθω||to lessen; to disappear}}, {{cog|kw|minow||to reduce}}, {{cog|got|𐌼𐌹𐌽𐍃||less}}, {{cog|cu|мьнйии||smaller, lesser, younger}}, {{cog|txb|maiwe||small, young}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=minor, -or, -us|pages=381–382}}</ref> Related to {{m|la|minor}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|minuō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|3|minuō|minu|minūt}}

# to [[make]] smaller, [[lessen]], [[diminish]], [[reduce]]
#: {{syn|la|diminuō|dēminuō|imminuō|tenuō|premō|corripiō}}
#: {{ant|la|augeō|amplificō|extendō|accumulō|cumulō|multiplicō}}
# to [[attenuate]], [[appease]], [[suppress]], [[repress]], [[quell]]
#: {{syn|la|coerceo}}
# to [[dismember]], [[tear apart]], [[break]]
#: {{syn|la|findo|rumpo}}
# to [[restrict]], [[confine]], [[limit]]
#: {{syn|la|fīniō|līmitō|delīmitō|claudō|urgeō|moderor|inclūdō}}
#: {{uxi|la|{{l|la|animos}} '''minuere'''|t=to restrict the wrath}}
# to [[remove]], [[subtract]], [[detract]]
# to [[reduce]] the [[importance]]
# to [[undermine]], [[weaken]], [[debilitate]], [[soften]]
#: {{syn|la|atterō|dēterō|frangō|effēminō|tenuō|cōnsūmō|afficiō}}
#: {{ant|la|firmō|cōnfirmō|mūniō|fortificō|cōnsolidō|sistō}}
# to [[eliminate]], [[delete]], [[remove]]
# {{lb|la|poetic}} to [[cease]], [[stop]], [[give up]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|3|minuō|minu|minūt}}

