Page 3804 misceo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*meyḱ-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*mikskō||to mix}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro||*miḱ-sḱé-}}, inchoative present of {{m|ine-pro|*meyǵ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*meyḱ-||to mix}}. The second conjugation of this verb is unexplained. Cognate with {{cog|goh|miskian}}, {{m|goh|miskan||to mix}} ({{cog|de|mischen}}), {{cog|cy|mysgu||to mix}}, {{cog|grc|μίγνυμι||to mix}}, {{cog|cu|мѣсити||to mix}}, {{cog|lt|mišti}} and {{m|lt|maišyti||to mix}}, {{cog|sa|मिश्र||mixed}}, {{cog|fa|آمیختن||tr=âmixtan|mix}}; {{cog|ang|māsc||mixture, mash}}. More at {{m|en|mash}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=misceō|pages=382-383}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|misceō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2.p3inf|misceō|miscu|mixt/mist}}

# to [[mix]]
#: {{syn|la|commisceō|cōnfundō}}
# to [[mingle]], [[intermingle]]
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Proverbs|14|13|quote=Rīsus dolōre '''miscēbitur''', et extrēma gaudiī lūctus occupat|trans=''Laughter '''shall be mingled''' with sorrow, and mourning taketh hold of the end of joy.''<br/>(Douay-Rheims trans., Challoner rev.: '''1752''' CE)}}
# {{lb|la|poetic}} a disturbance of the natural order, as in a storm: to [[disturb]], to [[throw]] into [[confusion]], to [[confuse]], [[confound]], [[embroil]]
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|133-134|quote=“Iam caelum terramque meō sine nūmine, ventī,<br/>'''miscēre''', et tantās audētis tollere mōlēs?”|trans=''“Now heaven and earth – without my divine assent, you winds! – you dare '''to disturb''', and raise such swells [of seawater]?”''<br/>(Neptune upbraids the winds.)}}

====Conjugation====
* The fourth principal part may be {{m|la|mixtum}} or {{m|la|mistum}}.
{{la-conj|2.p3inf|misceō|miscu|mixt/mist}}

