Page 3817 mito: -------- begin text --------

===Verb===
{{head|la|verb|head=mītō|third-person singular present active indicative|mītāt}}; ''[[Appendix:Latin third conjugation|third conjugation]]''

# {{alternative form of|la|from=Early Latin|mittō}}
#* '''7th–5th century BC''', {{w|Duenos inscription}}:
#*: {{quote|la|𐌉𐌏𐌖𐌄𐌔𐌀𐌕𐌃𐌄𐌉𐌖𐌏𐌔𐌒𐌏𐌉𐌌𐌄𐌃'''𐌌𐌉𐌕𐌀𐌕'''𐌍𐌄𐌉𐌕𐌄𐌃𐌄𐌍𐌃𐌏𐌂𐌏𐌔𐌌𐌉𐌔𐌖𐌉𐌓𐌂𐌏𐌔𐌉𐌄𐌃|tr=IOVESATDEIVOSQOIMED'''MITAT'''NEITEDENDOCOSMISVIRCOSIED<br/>iouesāt deivos qoi mēd '''mītāt''', nei tēd endō cosmis vircō siēd|t=The person who '''sends''' me prays to the gods, lest the girl be not kind towards thee}}

[[Category:Old Latin lemmas]]

-------- end text --------
Page 3818 mitto: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Likely from {{m|la|mītō}} via the so-called ''littera-rule'', from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*meitō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*meytH-|*meyth₂-|exchange, remove}}, an extension of the root {{m|ine-pro|*mey-||change}}. From the original meaning “to exchange” a [[semantic shift]] occurred to “to give, bestow” and then “to let go, send”. Cognate to {{cog|spx|meitims}}, {{m|spx|meitimúm||monument|pos=nom. and acc. sg. respectively}}. External cognates include {{cog|sa|मेथेते||to become hostile, quarrel}}, and {{cog|got|𐌹𐌽𐌼𐌰𐌹𐌳𐌾𐌰𐌽||to change}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|mittō, -ere|384}}</ref><ref>{{R:Etymonline|mission}}</ref>

Based on the attested [[hapax legomenon]] {{m|la|cōsmittō}} for {{m|la|committō}}, some<ref>{{R:ine:IEW|vol=III|page=968}}</ref> reconstruct the root with an initial ''s-,'' but De Vaan regards the hapax as not trustworthy enough.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|mittō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|mittō|mīs|miss}}

# to [[send]], [[dispatch]], [[cause]] to go, [[let go]], [[release]], [[discharge]]
# to [[put out]], [[extend]], [[reach out]] (one's hand)
# to [[announce]], [[tell]], [[report]], send [[word]], [[advise]]
# {{lb|la|chiefly|_|poetic}} to [[yield]], [[furnish]], [[produce]], [[export]]
# to [[put an end]] to
# to [[let]] or [[bring]] out, [[put]] or send forth, send out, [[emit]]; let [[blood]], [[bleed]]; [[utter]] a [[sound]], [[speak]], [[say]]
#: {{syn|la|ēmittō|iaciō}}
# to [[throw]], [[hurl]], [[fling]], [[cast]], [[launch]], [[send]]; [[throw down]], [[sprinkle]]
#: {{syn|la|coniciō|iniciō|adiciō|obiciō|abiciō|permittō|iaciō|iactō|iaculor|impingō|ēmittō|trāiciō|lībrō}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|2|565-566|quote=“Dēseruēre omnēs dēfessī, et corpora saltū<br/>ad terram '''mīsēre''' aut ignibus aegra dedēre.”|trans=''“All [of my men], exhausted, had given up [the fight], and with a leap '''had flung''' [themselves] to the ground [below] or else consigned their weakened bodies to the flames.”''<br/>(Syncopation: mīsēre, mīsēr[unt].)}}
# to [[attend]], [[guide]], [[escort]]
# to [[dedicate]] {{gloss|a book or poem to someone to compliment them}}
# to [[dismiss]], [[disregard]]
#* [[w:Vergil|Vergil]]. ''[[w:Aeneid|Aeneid]]'', VI, 85
#*: '''''mitte''' hanc de pectore curam''
#*:: '''Dismiss''' this anxiety from your heart
# {{lb|la|chiefly|_|poetic}}  to [[pass over]], [[forbear]], [[cease]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|mittō|mīs|miss}}

