Page 3820 moderor: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|moderō}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*med-}}
From the same root as {{m|la|modus||measure, manner|g=m}}, but not directly derived from this noun, which declines in Latin as a masculine ''o-''stem. The form ''moderor'' was presumably built on a neuter ''s''-stem noun derived from Proto-Indo-European {{m|ine-pro|*med-|t=to measure}} + {{m|ine-pro|*-os|pos=noun-forming suffix}}, whose existence is also indirectly attested by the ''-es-'' found in {{m|la|modestus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+.p3inf|moderor}}

# to set a [[measure]] or [[bound]]s to; [[moderate]], [[mitigate]], [[allay]], [[qualify]]. {{+obj|la|dative}}
#: {{syn|la|molliō|sopiō|lēniō|mītigō|sileō|sedō|domō}}
# to [[restrain]]
#: {{syn|la|fīniō|supprimō|refrēnō|obstō|arceō|intersaepiō|claudō|interclūdō|retineō|coerceō|delīmitō|līmitō|moror}}
# {{lb|la|by extension}} to [[manage]], [[arrange]], [[regulate]], [[rule]], [[guide]], [[govern]], [[direct]], [[control]]. {{q|dative or accusative}}
#: {{syn|la|dominor|imperō|gerō|imperitō|rēgnō|regō|magistrō|ōrdinō|dispēnsō}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+.p3inf|moderor}}

