Page 3850 mugio: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*mug-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*mūg-}}, {{onomatopoeic|la|title=onomatopoeic}} form, reminiscent of cow's lowing. Cognates include {{cog|grc|μῡκάομαι||to low, bellow}}, {{cog|lt|mū̃kti||to bellow}} and {{cog|ru|мыча́ть||to moo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|mūgiō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|4++.nopass|mūgiō}}

# to [[moo]], [[low]], [[bellow]]
# {{lb|la|of inanimate things}} to [[roar]], [[rumble]], [[bray]], [[groan]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|4++.nopass|mūgiō}}

====Derived terms====
{{der2|la|admūgiō|immūgiō|mūgīnor|mūgītor|mūgītus|remūgiō}}

