Page 3852 mulco: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Maybe a denominal to a noun {{der|la|itc-pro|*molkā-}}, from the same ultimate source as {{m|la|mulceo|t=I caress, stroke}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|mulcō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|mulcō}}

# to [[beat up]], handle [[roughly]]
#* {{Q|la|Suetonius|De vita Caesarum|I|17|quote=Vettium pignoribus captis et direpta supellectile male '''mulcatum''' ac pro rostris in contione paene discerptum coiecit in carcerem; eodem Nouium quaestorem, quod compellari apud se maiorem potestatem passus esset.|trans=As for Vettius, after his bond was declared forfeit and his goods seized, he was roughly handled by the populace assembled before the rostra, and all but torn to pieces.}}
# {{lb|la|of inanimate things}} to [[damage]], [[injure]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+.sigm|mulcō}}

===See also===
* {{l|la|mulceō}}

===References===
* {{R:L&S}}
* {{R:Elementary Lewis}}
* {{R:Gaffiot}}

