Page 3871 nanciscor: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₂neḱ-}}
From {{inh|la|ine-pro|*h₂eh₂nóḱe||has reached, attained}}, stative of {{m|ine-pro|*h₂neḱ-||to reach}}. Cognate with {{cog|sga|doánaic|(do·)ánaic|came, arrived}}, {{cog|sq|kënaq||to satisfy, be enough}}, {{cog|lt|nèšti||to carry}}, {{cog|grc|ἤνεγκα||I carried}} (aorist of {{m|grc|φέρω}}), {{cog|ang|ġenōg||enough}}, {{cog|cu|нести||to carry}}, {{cog|sa|अश्नोति|tr=aśnóti}}, {{m|sa|नशति|tr=náśati||attains}}, see {{cog|sa|नि}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|nancīscor}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|nancīscor|nact/nānct}}

# to [[meet with]], [[stumble]] on, [[encounter]], [[acquire]], [[get]], [[reach]], [[find]] something
#: {{syn|la|acquīrō|adipīscor|cōnsequor|parō|pariō|impetrō|potior|inveniō|mereō|sūmō|emō|comparō|apīscor|obtineō|conciliō|colligō|alliciō}}
#: {{ant|la|āmittō}}
#: {{uxi|la|cum plus otii '''nactus''' ero|t=when I have more free time|lit=when I will '''have met''' more leisure}}
# to [[contract]], [[catch]]
#: {{uxi|la|morbum nancisci|t=to fall ill}}
# {{lb|la|by extension}} to [[possess]] by [[birth]], have by [[nature]]

====Conjugation====
* The alternative supine {{m|la|nānctum}} is rare.
{{la-conj|3|nancīscor|nact/nānct}}

====Derived terms====
