===Etymology 1===
Frequentative of {{m|la|nō}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|natō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|1+|natō}}

# to [[swim]], [[float]]
#: {{ux|la|Cum in lacū '''natābat''', multōs piscēs vīdit.|When '''swimming''' in the lake, he saw many fish.}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} (especially of the eyes) to [[swim]] (as when drunken or dying); to be [[feeble]], [[failing]]; to [[fluctuate]], [[waver]], be [[uncertain]], [[unsteady]]; to move to and fro, not stand still
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|6|673|quote=‘nox erat, et vīnīs oculīque animīque '''natābant'''’|trans=''“It was night, and [their] eyesight as well as [their] minds '''were [unsteady,] swimming''' with wine [...].”''<br/>(The poetic voice of {{w|Minerva}} or Tritonia describes the aftermath of a merry feast.)}} 
# to [[stream]], [[flow]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|1+|natō}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{der3|la|ēnatō|supernatō|natābundus|natāns|natāticius|natātilis|natātiō|natātor|natatorium|natātōrium|natātōrius|natātūra|natātus}}

