Page 3895 nescio: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|la|2016|May|12}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|la|nōn sciō|nōsciō||substandard when used as a full synonym}}

===Etymology===
From Latin {{prefix|la|ne|sciō|gloss1=not|gloss2=I know}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|eccl=yes|nesciō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|4|nesciō|nescīv/nesci|nescīt}}

# to [[not]] [[know]], to be [[ignorant]], to [[not]] [[understand]]
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|565-566|quote=“Quis genus Aeneadum? Quis Troiae '''nesciat''' urbem,<br/>virtūtēsque, virōsque, aut tantī incendia bellī?”|trans=''“Who '''does not know''' the race of Aeneas? Who '''[has never heard of]''' the city of Troy, and its courage, and heroes, or the flames of that great war?”''}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|6|255-256|quote=sed quae '''nescieram''', quōrumque errōre tenēbar,<br/>cognita sunt nūllō praecipiente mihi.|trans=''But [those things] of which '''I had not known''', as well as those I misunderstood, were [suddenly] known to me without anyone having taught [them to me].''<br/>(The poet receives divine enlightenment during an encounter with {{w|Vesta (mythology)}}; see also {{w|Vestalia}}.)}}
#: {{syn|la|ignōrō}}
#: {{ant|la|sciō|sentiō|cōnsciō|nōscō|inveniō}}
#* {{Q|la|Carl von Linné, ''Critica botanica''|quote={{l|la|nomina|Nōmina}} {{l|la|si|sī}} '''nescīs''', {{l|la|perit}} {{l|la|et}} {{l|la|cognitio}} {{l|la|rerum|rērum}}|t=If you '''do not know''' names, the knowledge of the things is also lost}}
#* From ''[[w:Pro Caelio|For Marcus Caelius]]'' by {{w|Cicero}} (Latin and English translation may be found [http://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text.jsp?doc=Perseus:abo:phi,0474,024:15:35 here], also [[wikisource:en:Pro Marco Caelio|English]] and [[wikisource:la:Pro Marco Caelio|Latin]] on Wikisource)
#*: ''Quae tu quoniam mente '''nescio''' qua effrenata atque praecipiti in forum deferri iudiciumque voluisti, aut diluas oportet ac falsa esse doceas aut nihil neque crimini tuo neque testimonio credendum esse fateare.''
#*:: And as for you, since, through some unbridled and headlong fury which I '''cannot comprehend''' you have chosen these things to be brought into court, and dilated on at this trial, you must either efface the charges yourself, and show that they are without foundation, or else you must confess that no credit is to be given to any accusations which you may make, or to any evidence which you may give.
#: {{uxi|la|{{l|la|nomen|Nōmen}} '''nesciō''' ([[N. N.]])|t='''I do not know''' the name}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|4|nesciō|nescīv/nesci|nescīt}}

