Page 3909 nitor: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*kneygʷʰ-|t=to bend, to droop}}. Cognate with {{m|la|nicō}}, {{m|la|connīveō}}, {{m|la|nictō}}, {{cog|gem-pro|*hnīwaną}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|nītor}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|3|nītor|nīs/nīx}}

# to [[bear]] or [[rest]] upon something, [[lean on]]; to be [[support|supported]] by; to be [[base|based on]]
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Cicero|Cicero]]|[[w:De Officiis|De Officiis]]|I, 122|quote=Quorum consilio atque auctoritate '''nitatur'''|t=[so as to] be '''supported by''' their advise and their reputation}}
# to [[press]] forward, [[advance]]
# to [[mount]], [[climb]], [[ascend]]; [[fly]]
# to [[strain]] in [[give birth|giving birth]]; [[bring forth]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[strive]], [[struggle]], [[exert]] oneself, [[make an effort]], [[labor]], [[endeavor]]
#: {{syn|la|lūctor|certō|cōnītor|cōnor|temptō|ēlabōrō|appetō|īnsequor|affectō|tendō|quaerō|studeō|contendō|pugnō|molior|perīclitor|ēnītor|adnītor|labōrō|spectō}}
#* {{Q|la|Sallust|Bellum Catilinae|quote=Omnīs hominēs quī sēsē student praestāre cēterīs animālibus summā ope '''nītī''' decet nē vītam silentiō trānseant veluti pecora|trans=It is suitable for all who wish to be better than animals '''to struggle''' with their best effort in order not to go through life in silence like cattle.}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[try]] to [[prove]], [[contend]] in argument, [[argue]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[rest]], [[rely]], [[depend]] upon

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|3|nītor|nīs/nīx}}

=====Derived terms=====
