===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*neḱ-}}
From {{der|la|itc-pro|*nokeō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro||*noḱéye-}}, causative of the root {{m|ine-pro|*neḱ-||perish, disappear}}. Cognate with {{cog|sa|नश्यति||disappear, perish}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|noceō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2+.p3inf|noceō}}

# {{lb|la|with dative}} to [[injure]], do [[harm]] to, [[hurt]], [[damage]]
#: {{syn|la|feriō|vulnerō|secō|īnfestō}}
#* {{Q|la|Publilius Syrus|Sententiae|quote=Bonīs '''nocet''' quisquis pepercit malīs.|trans=He '''does harm''' to the good, whoever has been lenient to the bad}}

====Usage notes====
* The injury caused may be physical or emotional.

====Conjugation====
* In practice, the only passive forms met with in Latin are the third-person singular forms.
{{la-conj|2+.p3inf.sigm|noceō|||nox}}

