Page 3922 nosco: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|gnōscō}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*ǵneh₃-}}
From earlier {{m|la|gnōscō}}, from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*gnōskō}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*ǵn̥h₃sḱéti}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|eccl=yes|nōscō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3.poet-sync-perf|nōscō|nōv|nōt}}

# to become [[acquainted]] with something, [[learn]] about it
#: {{syn|la|intellegō|cognosco|cerno|tongeo|prehendō}}
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|Tusculanae Disputationes|1|52|quote=Cum igitur "'''nosce''' te" dicit, hoc dicit: "'''nosce''' animum tuum". Nam corpus quidem quasi vas est aut aliquod animi receptaculum.|t=Therefore when he [the [[Pythian]] [[Apollo]]] says, "'''Know''' thyself", this is what it means: "'''Know''' your mind". The body is of course like a vase, or some other container for the mind.}}
# {{lb|la|in perfect tenses and past participle}} to [[know]], [[recognize]], be [[acquainted]] with, i.e.; in possession of knowledge
#: {{syn|la|agnōscō|cognōscō|inveniō|sentiō|cōnsciō|sapiō|sciō|scīscō|intellegō|percipiō|discernō|tongeō|cernō|audiō}}
#: {{ant|la|ignōrō|nesciō}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Ars Amatoria|1|1-2|quote= Sī quis in hōc artem populō nōn '''nōvit''' amandī, / hoc legat et lēctō carmine doctus amet.|t=If anyone does not '''know''' the art of loving, may they read this, and having both read the poem and been taught, love.}}
#* ''Hīc Nātus Ubīque '''Nōtus'''''
#*: Born Here, '''Known''' Everywhere ([[motto]] of the [https://web.archive.org/web/20051120113742/http://www.instituto-allende.edu.mx/english/misc/ANESA.htm Allende Institute] in reference to [[w:Ignacio Allende|Ignacio de Allende]])
# {{lb|la|rare}} to [[recognize]] someone, be [[familiar]] with
#: {{syn|la|recognōscō|cognōscō|agnōscō}}
# {{lb|la|euphemism}} to have had [[sex]] with, have ever [[slept]] with
#: {{syn|la|cognōscō}}
#* {{Q|la|Catullus|72|quote=Dīcēbās quondam sōlum tē '''nōsse''' Catullum, / Lesbia, nec prae mē velle tenēre Iovem.|t=You used to say, some time ago, that you only ever '''slept with''' [me] Catullus, Lesbia, and that you didn't want to hold [even] Jupiter more than me.}}
# to [[accept]] a [[reason]] or [[excuse]]
#: {{syn|la|accipiō|cōnservō}}
# {{lb|la|Late Latin|Christianity|in the perfect}} to [[acknowledge]], [[submit]] to (God)
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Acta Apostolorum|19|15|quote=Respondens autem spiritus nequam dixit eis, Iesum '''novi''' et Paulum scio, vos autem qui estis?|t=A wicked spirit replied to them, "I '''acknowledge''' Jesus, and I know Paul, but who are all of you?}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|nōscō|nōv|nōt}}

