Page 3936 nuncupo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*keh₂p-}}
From {{m|la|nōmen||name}} and {{m|la|capiō||seize, catch}}. De Vaan says the original compound must have been a nominal of the form *''nōmiceps'', with the meaning 'taking a name, declaring', from which was derived a verb of the first conjugation that subsequently passed through the following stages: *''nōmicupāre'' > *''nōmcupāre'' > *''nomcupāre'' > ''nuncupāre''<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=nōmen|page=412}}</ref>.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|nū̆ncupō}}

The length of the vowel in the first syllable is uncertain: De Vaan (2008) gives it as short (see etymology above), but Marx (1901) and Lewis (1895) give it as long.<ref>{{cite-book|author=Charles E. Bennett|title=The Latin Language – a historical outline of its sounds, inflections, and syntax|chapter=Hidden Quantity|location=Boston|publisher=Allyn and Bacon|year=1907|page=70|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/latinlanguagehis00bennuoft/page/70|authorlink=Charles E. Bennett (scholar)}}</ref> 

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|nū̆ncupō}}

# to [[call]] by name; to [[name]]
# {{lb|la|legal}} to [[publicly]] name or [[appoint]] as [[heir]]
# to [[vow]] publicly
# to [[announce]] [[publicly]] or [[officially]]
#: {{syn|la|adnūntiō|dēnūntiō|nūntiō|indicō|prōdō|renūntiō|profiteor|ēdīcō|praedicō|cōntiōnor|referō}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+.sigm|nū̆ncupō}}

====Derived terms====
{{top2}}
* {{l|la|nū̆ncupātim}}
* {{l|la|nū̆ncupātiō}}
* {{l|la|nū̆ncupātīvē}}
* {{l|la|nū̆ncupātīvus}}
* {{l|la|nū̆ncupātor}}
{{bottom}}

====Descendants====
