Page 4007 oboedio: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|la|obaudiō}}
* {{alter|la|obēdiō}}

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|ob-|audio}}. In Latin, ''ob'' + ''audire'' would have been expected to become Classical Latin *''obūdiō'' (compare ''in'' + ''claudō'' becoming ''inclūdō''), but it has been theorized that the usual law court associations of the word for obeying encouraged a false [[archaism]] from ''ū'' to ''oe'', to ''oboediō'' (compare Old Latin ''oinos'' → Classical Latin ''ūnus'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|oboediō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|4++|oboediō}}

# to [[obey]], yield obedience to
#: {{syn|la|obtemperō|pāreō|exaudiō}}
#: {{ant|la|recalcitrō}}
# to be subject to, to [[serve]]
#: {{syn|la|serviō|appāreō}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|4++|oboediō}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|la|inoboediō}}
* {{l|la|oboediēns}}

