Page 4089 occupo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*keh₂p-}}
From {{m|la|ob-}} and the root of {{m|la|capiō|t=capture, seize}}. The difference in conjugation is explained by De Vaan, citing Steinbauer 1989, as the result of derivation via the denominal suffix {{m|la|-ō|-ō, -āre|id=denominative}} from some intermediate nominal (such as an unattested noun or adjective *''occeps'', *''occupis''), instead of direct composition of the prefix with the base verb.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=capiō|page=90}}</ref> Compare {{m|la|anticipō}}, {{m|la|nū̆ncupō}}, {{m|la|participō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|occupō}}

