Page 4093 odi: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|la|odiō<q:present tense>|ōdīvī<q:perfect tense>||pcl}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₃ed-|id=hate}}
From {{der|la|ine-pro||*h₃e-h₃ód-e ~ h₃e-h₃d-ḗr}}, reduplicated perfect from the root {{m|ine-pro|*h₃ed-|t=to hate; to start hating?}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|odī|425}}</ref><ref>{{R:ine:LIV|*h₃ed-|296}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|ōdī}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|4.sup-futr-actv-only|ōdī|ōs}}

# to have an [[aversion]] towards, to [[hate]], [[dislike]]
#* {{Q|la|Horace|Odes|1|38|1|thru=2|transauthor=A.Z. Foreman|quote=Persicōs '''ōdī''', puer, apparātūs,<br>displicent nexae philyrā corōnae.|trans=My boy: I '''hate''' the filigree of Persia.</br>Linden-sewn garlands chafe me with their glamor.}}
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Exodus|20|5|quote=Nōn adōrābis ea, neque colēs: ego sum Dominus Deus tuus fortis, zēlōtēs, vīsitāns inīquitātem patrum in fīliōs, in tertiam et quārtam generātiōnem eōrum quī '''ōdērunt''' mē.|trans=Thou shalt not bow down thyself to them, nor serve them: for I the LORD thy God am a jealous God, visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children unto the third and fourth generation of them that '''hate''' me.}}
# {{lb|la|with|infinitive}} to feel [[reluctant]] to, to [[hate]] to, to be [[loath]] to
#* {{Q|la|Horace|Odes|2|16|quote=Laetus in praesēns animus quod ultrā est<br>'''ōderit''' cūrāre{{...}}|t=And let the mind that's happy in the moment<br>'Bout that which lies before '''be loath''' to worry}}

====Usage notes====
{{attn|la|unclear wording}}
Irregular for historical reasons as well as to avoid near-homophony (especially for non-urban speakers) with forms of {{m|la|audeō}} and {{m|la|audiō}}:
* Used to express a stative meaning, inheriting the [[Proto-Indo-European]] usage. As a result, no usual aspectual distinction (imperfect-perfect) is possible.
* The perfect tense expresses a present stative meaning. The pluperfect expresses a past stative meaning.
* {{m|la|perōsus|Perōsus}} and {{m|la|exōsus}} are used in place of present active participles; {{m|la|ōsus}} is archaic in this function.
* To express the passive meaning, various expressions with {{m|la|odium}} are mainly used.

The form {{m|la|odīvī}}, classically a [[solecism]], is attested already by the end of the Republic in the past [[aorist]]ic function; in [[Late Latin]], the imperfect {{m|la|odiō}} becomes common (see it for details), supplementing {{m|la|ōdī}} in the present, while {{m|la|perōsus}} and {{m|la|exōsus}} acquire the passive meaning.

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|4.sup-futr-actv-only|ōdī|ōs}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|la|ōsus}}
* {{l|la|ōsor}}
* {{l|la|ōdibilis}}

====Related terms====
{{top2}}
* {{l|la|odiō}}
* {{l|la|odium}}
* {{l|la|odiōsē}}
* {{l|la|odiōsus}}
* {{l|la|perōsus}}
* {{l|la|exōsus}}
{{bottom}}

====Descendants====
{{top2}}
