-------- end text --------
Page 4094 odio: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
A regularizing substitute for the highly irregular {{m|la|ōdī}} and the various synonymous expressions with {{m|la|odium}} of Classical Latin, first attested as {{m|la|ōdīvit}} in [[w:Marc Antony|Cicero]] and attributed to [[w:Marc Antony|Marc Antony]]. It is likely that this perfect form was the first stage of the verb's development, via [[hypercorrection]] of the then-current ''īvī > ī'' contraction; later this was extended to other tenses on the model of verbs like {{m|la|audiō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|odiō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|4|odiō|ōdīv|ōs}}

# {{lb|la|Late Latin}} {{alternative form of|la|ōdī}}
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|Philippicae|13|19|41|thru=42|quote=Sed iam vidēte magnī et clārī virī admīrābilem gravitātem atque cōnstantiam:<br>'Mihi quidem cōnstat nec meam contumēliam nec meōrum ferre, nec dēserere partīs quās Pompeius '''ōdīvit''' nec veterānōs sēdibus suīs movērī patī nec singulōs ad cruciātum trahī nec fallere fidem quam dedī Dolābellae—'<br>Omittō alia: 'fidem Dolābellae,' sānctissimī virī, dēserere homo pius nōn potest.|trans=Now observe the incredible seriousness and resolution of a great and distinguished [[w:Mark Anthony|man]]:<br>'I am determined not to tolerate insult to me or to my friends, nor to desert the party which [[w:Pompey|Pompey]] '''hated''', nor to allow the veterans to be evicted from their homes nor to be dragged one by one to crucifixion, nor to betray my pledge to [[w:Dolabella|Dolabella]]—'<br>I leave out the rest: he cannot, as a man of honor, betray his pledge to that model of integrity, Dolabella.}}
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Psalms|100|3|thru=4|quote=Nōn prōpōnēbam ante oculōs meōs rem iniūstam; facientēs praevāricātiōnēs '''ōdīvī'''.|trans=I did not set before my eyes any unjust thing; I '''hated''' the workers of iniquities.}}

====Usage notes====
* The only forms of this verb mentioned by any grammarian are the infinitive, the infinitive-derived past imperfect subjunctive, and the supine in the periphrastic future {{m|la|ōsum}} {{m|la|īre}}.<ref>[https://digiliblt.uniupo.it/xtf/view?docId=dlt000085/dlt000085.xml;query=odire digilibLT: Ars Grammatica (Charisius)]</ref><ref>[https://digiliblt.uniupo.it/xtf/search?keyword=osum+ire&lang=en digilibLT search]</ref>
* Consult {{m|la|ōdī}} for more information.

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|4|odiō|ōdīv|ōs}}

===Noun===
{{head|la|noun form|head=odiō}}

# {{inflection of|la|odium||dat//abl|s}}

