Page 4097 offendo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*gʷʰen-}}
From {{affix|la|ob-|gloss1=against|*fendō|gloss2=hit, thrust}}, from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*fendō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*gʷʰen-||to strike, to kill}}. Compare {{m|la|dēfendō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|offendō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|offendō|offend|offēns}}

# to [[hit]], [[thrust]], [[strike]] against something
#* {{quote-book|la|year=c. 40 {{BCE}}|title=[[:s:la:De Bello Hispaniensi#23|De Bello Hispaniensi]]|section=chapter 23|text=Ita cum eius [mīlitis] compar proelium facere coepisset, cum undique sē circumvenīrī animum advertisset, ingressus pedem '''offendit'''.|t=So, although his [the soldier's] partner had begun to fight, when he noticed that he was being surrounded on all sides, after starting to leave, he '''hit''' his foot.}}
#* {{quote-book|la|year=30 {{BCE}}|author=[[:w:Quintus Horatius Flaccus|Quintus Horatius Flaccus]]|title=[[:w:Satires (Horace)|Sermo]] 1.2|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170527231012/http://www.horatius.net/index.xps?2.801|archivedate=2017-05-27|url=http://www.horatius.net/index.xps?2.801|section=lines 74-78|text=Quidquid sum ego, quamvīs<br/>īnfrā Lūcīlī cēnsum ingeniumque, tamen mē<br/>cum magnīs vīxisse invīta fatēbitur ūsque<br/>invidia et fragilī quaerēns inlīdere dentem<br/>'''offendet''' solidō [...]|t=Whatever I am like, though<br/>inferior to the wealth and talent of Lucilius, nevertheless, that I<br/>have lived with great men [is something that] reluctant envy will fully admit<br/>and, seeking to sink her tooth into something soft,<br/>'''will strike it''' against something solid [...]}}
#* {{quote-book|la|year=c. 95 {{CE}}|author=[[:w:Quintilian|Quintilian]]|title=[[:w:Institutio Oratoria|Institutio Oratoria]]|section=book 6, chapter 3, line 67|url=http://www.hs-augsburg.de/~harsch/Chronologia/Lspost01/Quintilianus/qui_in06.html#04|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200603184535/https://www.hs-augsburg.de/~harsch/Chronologia/Lspost01/Quintilianus/qui_in06.html|archivedate=2020-06-03|text=An nōn plūrima dīcuntur quod refert Cicerō dē homine praelongō, caput eum ad fornicem Fabium '''offendisse''' [...]|t=Rather, not many things are said like what Cicero reports about a very tall man, that he '''hit''' his head on the Fabian arch [...]}}
# to [[meet]], [[encounter]] (someone)
#: {{syn|la|inveniō|obeō|occurrō|congredior|prōcēdō}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[suffer]] [[damage]], receive an [[injury]]
# to [[fail]], be [[unfortunate]]
# to [[find fault]], take [[offence]]
# to [[stumble]], [[blunder]], commit offence or [[sin]]
#: {{syn|la|committō|dēlinquō|lābor|errō}}
# to [[shock]], [[vex]], [[offend]], [[mortify]], [[scandalize]]

