Page 4182 pappo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|la|papō}}

===Etymology===
{{unk|la|Unclear}}. Possibly a nursery word of {{onomatopoeic|la|title=imitative}} origin<ref>Johnson, Edwin Lee (1931): Latin words of common English, p. 73</ref><ref>{{R:American Heritage Dictionary}}</ref>, or from {{der|la|ine-pro|*peh₂-||eat, feed}}) from which are derived {{m|la|pāscō}}, {{m|la|pastor}}, {{m|la|pābulum}}, {{m|la|pābulor}}.

Compare with {{cog|en|pap}}, {{cog|pt|papar}}, Bulgarian [[папам]], Serbo-Croatian {{m|sh|папати}}/{{m|sh|papati}}, German {{m|de|Pappe}}, Czech {{m|cs|papat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|pappō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1.nopass|pappō|pappāv}}

# to [[eat]], eat [[pap]]
#: ''liberto opus est quod '''pappet''','' Plaut. Ep. 5, 2, 62

