Page 4183 parabolo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{af|la|parabola|-ō|id2=denominative|t1=parable, comparison|pos2=verb-forming suffix}}. First attested from 678 CE in northern France.<ref>{{R:FEW|7|612|parabolare}}</ref>

====Verb====
{{la-verb|1+|parabolō}} {{tlb|la|EML.}}

# to make clear by metaphors<ref>{{R:Niermeyer|parabolare|760/2}}</ref>
# to [[talk]]; [[speak]]; [[communicate]] using [[word]]s<ref name="du Cange"/>
#: {{ux|la|Nostri seniores, sicut audistis, '''parabolaverunt''' simul et consideraverunt cum communibus illorum fidelibus de Dei servitio, etc.}}
# {{lb|la|New Latin}} to compare<ref>{{R:NLW|parabolo|2/016606|17.09.10}}</ref>

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|1+|parabolō}}

=====Descendants=====
{{hcol|3}}
