** {{desc|co|parlà}}
** {{desc|it|parlare}} {{see desc}}
** {{desc|nap|parlà}}
**: {{desc|roa-tar|parlare}}
** {{desc|scn|parrari|alts=1}}
** {{desc|ia|parlar|bor=1}}
* North Italian:
** {{desc|lij|parlâ}}
** {{desc|vec|parlar}}
* Gallo-Romance:
** {{desc|ca|parlar}}
** {{desc|frp|parlar}}
** {{desc|oc|parlar}}
** {{desc|fro|parler}} {{see desc}}
** → Iberia:
*** {{desc|an|parlar}}
*** {{desc|ast|parllar}}
*** {{desc|ext|palral|alts=1}}
*** {{desc|pt|palrar}}
*** {{desctree|es|parlar}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|la|grc|παραβολεύομαι||venture, lack regard, run hazard}}, as a Latin gloss for [http://www.blueletterbible.org/Bible.cfm?b=Phl&c=2&t=KJV#s=t_concf_1105030 {{Q|grc|NT|Ep. Philem.|2|30|form=inline}}].<ref name="du Cange">{{R:du Cange|parabolare|parabolare}}</ref>

====Verb====
{{la-verb|1+|parabolō}}

# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin}} endanger, lack regard for, to risk<ref name="du Cange"/>
#: '''''Parabolatus''' est de anima sua''

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|1+|parabolō}}

