Page 4184 parco: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|parcō}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₂erk-}}
From {{der|la|itc-pro|*pearkō|*pe-arkō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₂erk-}} (whence {{m|la|arceō}}). See also {{m|la|parcus}}.

Others make it cognate with {{cog|grc|σπαρνός||rare}}, {{cog|en|spare}}.

====Verb====
{{la-verb|3|parcō|peperc/pars|pars}}

# {{lb|la|+ [[Appendix:Glossary#dative case|dative]] or [[Appendix:Glossary#accusative case|accusative]]}} to [[spare]], [[save up]], [[economise]]
#: {{syn|la|reservo}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively|+ [[Appendix:Glossary#dative case|dative]]}} to [[forgive]] someone, [[have]] [[mercy]] for, to be [[lenient]] to
#: {{syn|la|ignōscō|āmittō|remittō|dōnō|dīmittō|perdōnō|condōnō}}
#* {{Q|la|Publilius Syrus|Sententiae|quote=Bonīs nocet quisquis '''pepercit''' malīs.|trans=He does harm to the good, whoever '''has been lenient''' to the bad}}
#* {{Q|la|Augustus|Res Gestae Divi Augusti|quote=victorque omnibus veniam petentibus civibus '''peperci'''.|trans=... and victorious, '''I spared''' all the citizens desiring pardon.}}
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Caesar|Caesar]]|[[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]]|VII, 28|quote=Non aetate confectis, non mulieribus, non infantibus '''pepercerunt'''|t=They '''spared''' neither old men, women, or children}}
# to [[let]] alone, [[omit]]
#: {{syn|la|praetereō|omittō|permittō|āmittō|remittō|neglegō}}
# {{lb|la|+ [[Appendix:Glossary#dative case|dative]] or {{l|la|a}}/{{l|la|ab}} + [[Appendix:Glossary#ablative case|ablative]]}} to [[refrain]], [[abstain]], [[avoid]]
