===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*per-|id=fare}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*parjō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*perh₃-||to produce, beget}}.<ref>{{R:ine:LIV}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|pariō|eccl=1}}
* {{hyph|la|pa|rio}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|pariō|peper|part|futr_actv_inf=[[paritūrus]] [[esse]]|futr_actv_ptc=[[paritūrus]]}}

# to [[bear]], to [[give birth]] to
#: {{syn|la|prōcreō|genō|gignō|suscipiō|prōdō|ēdō|creō|enitor|conitor|efficiō}}
#: {{ant|la|necō}}
#* [[w:Vulgate|Vulgate]], [http://www.sacredbible.org/vulgate1822/scans2/II-249.jpg Isaiah 7:14]
#*: ''ecce virgo concipiet, et '''pariet''' filium, et vocabitur nomen eius Emmanuel''
#*:: behold, a virgin shall conceive, and '''bear''' a son, and shall call his name Immanuel.
# to [[spawn]], [[produce]], [[generate]], [[beget]]
#* [[w:Terence|Terentius]], [[w:Andria|Andria]]
#*: ''obsequium amīcōs, vēritās ōdium '''parit'''''
#*:: [[obsequiousness|Obsequiousness]] '''begets''' friends, truthfulness hatred.
# to [[procure]], [[acquire]]
#: {{syn|la|acquīrō|adipīscor|cōnsequor|parō|impetrō|mereō|sūmō|emō|comparō|potior|inveniō|apīscor|obtineō|conciliō|nancīscor|colligō|alliciō}}
#: {{ant|la|āmittō}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[cause]], [[provoke]], [[arouse]]
#: {{syn|la|ēdō|importō|offerō|addūcō|iniciō}}

