Page 4196 pasco: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*peh₂-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*pāskō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*peh₂-||to protect, shepherd}}. Compare {{cog|grc|ποιμαίνω||to tend, feed, nourish}}.

Cognates include {{cog|grc-att|ποιμήν||shepherd}}, {{cog|sa|पाति|tr=pā́ti||to protect}}, {{cog|ang|fōda}} and {{m|ang|fedan|fēdan}} ({{cog|en|food}} and {{m|en|feed}}), {{cog|cu|пасти||to pasture}}, {{cog|ru|пища}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|pāscō|eccl=1}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3.poet-sync-perf|pāscō|pāv|pāst}}

# to [[feed]], [[nourish]], maintain, support
#: {{syn|la|nūtriō|sagīnō|pāscor|alō|sustentō|foveō}}
# to [[pasture]], [[drive]] to [[pasture]], [[tend]], [[attend]]
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|1|204|quote='''pāscēbat'''que suās ipse senātor ovēs|trans=''and the senator himself '''was tending''' his own sheep''}}
# to feed, [[supply]], [[cultivate]], let grow
# {{lb|la|of animals}} to [[graze]], browse
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|184-186|quote=Nāvem in cōnspectū nūllam, trīs lītore cervōs<br/>prōspicit errantīs; hōs tōta armenta sequuntur<br/>ā tergō, et longum per vallīs '''pāscitur''' agmen.|trans=''[There is] not a ship in sight, [but] he sees three stags wandering along the shore; their whole herds are following behind, the long band '''grazing''' through the valley.''}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to feast, delight, satisfy, feed, gratify
# to consume, lay waste, ravage, desolate
# {{lb|la|metaphorical|Biblical|Ecclesiastical Latin}} to [[tend]] to as a [[shepherd]] or [[pastor]]; [[cherish]], nourish, [[care for]], feed [[spiritually]]
#: [[w:Vulgate|Vulgate]], [[w:Psalms|Psalm]] 22:1 <small>(Psalmi iuxta Heb. 23:1)</small> {{ux|la|Dominus '''pāscit''' mē et nihil mihī dēerit.|The Lord '''is my shepherd''' and nothing ''shall I want''.|lit=The Lord '''tends me as a shepherd''' and nothing for me will be lacking.}}

