From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*pāskō|*pāskōr|t=I am fed, driven to pasture}} from {{der|la|ine-pro|*peh₂-||to protect, shepherd}}, equivalent to the passive of {{m|la|pāscō}}. {{der|la|LL.|pāscārī}} from change in conjugation of {{m|la|pāscī}}. Compare passive voice {{cog|grc|ποιμαίνω|ποιμαίνεσθαι|t=to pasture, graze, feed}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|pāscor|eccl=1|vul=1}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|pāscor|pāst}}

# to [[feed]] oneself; to [[eat]]
#: {{syn|la|adedō|edō|vorō|prandeō|vēscor|cēnō|cōnsūmō}}
# to [[graze]], [[feed]], [[nourish]], [[pasture]], [[browse]]; [[traverse]], [[roam]] the [[pastures]]
#: {{syn|la|nūtriō|sagīnō|alō|pāscō|sustentō|foveō}}
# to [[eat up]], [[consume]], [[devour]]
# {{lb|la|figurative}} to [[feast]], [[nourish]], [[satisfy]], [[gratify]], [[delight]], [[enjoy oneself]]
#: {{syn|la|gaudeō|expleō}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|pāscor|pāst}}

====Derived terms====
