Page 4204 patior: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|la|patiō}}

===Etymology===
Apparently denominative from {{der|la|ine-pro|*ph₁-tós}}, participle of {{m|ine-pro|*peh₁-||to hurt}}. Cognate with {{m|la|paene}}, {{m|la|paeniteō}}, {{m|la|pēnūria}}, {{cog|grc|πῆμα}}, {{m|grc|πηρός}}, {{cog|ang|feond||devil, enemy}} ({{cog|en|fiend}}), {{cog|got|𐍆𐌰𐌹𐌰𐌽||to blame}}, {{cog|sla-pro|*patiti||to suffer, to fare misfortune}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|patior}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|patior|pass}}

# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[suffer]], [[endure]], [[tolerate]]
#: {{syn|la|tolerō|patiō|sufferō|subeō|perferō|perpetior|recipiō|accipiō|sinō|ferō|dūrō|sustineō|sustentō}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|1|157-158|quote=tum '''patitur''' cultus ager et renovātur arātrō|trans=''That is when the field '''endures''' cultivation, and is renewed by the plough.''<br/>[Note: This verse by the poet Ovid can '''endure''' a more figurative translation or '''permit''' a more literal reading of the word '''patitur.''']}}
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[allow]], [[acquiesce]], [[permit]], [[submit]]
#: {{syn|la|permittō|admittō}}
#: {{ux|la|'''Patere''' lēgem quam ipse fēcistī / tulistī.|'''Submit''' to the law which you yourself made / proposed.}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[exist]], [[live]]
#: {{ux|la|'''Pati''' sine regno|To '''live''' without a king.}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|patior|pass}}

====Derived terms====
{{col2|la|compatior|patiēns|passibilis|patibilis|passiō|passus|perpetior|praepatior|prōpatior}}

