Page 4214 paveo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*pawēō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*paw-||to strike, hit}}. The sense development would be "to strike" > "to strike with fear".

Cognates include {{m|la|paviō}}, {{m|la|puteus}}, {{m|la|pudeō}}, {{m|la|repudium}}, and possibly {{m|la|tripudium}} and {{m|la|putō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|paveō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2.poet-sync-perf|paveō|pāv}}

# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to be [[struck]] with fear, to be afraid or [[terrified]]; [[tremble]] or [[quake]] with fear
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[fear]], [[dread]] or be terrified by

====Conjugation====
* This verb has only limited passive conjugation; only third-person passive forms are attested in surviving sources.
{{la-conj|2.poet-sync-perf|paveō|pāv}}

