===Etymology 3===
From {{af|la|pēs|-ō|alt1=ped-|t1=foot|pos2=noun-forming suffix|id2=noun}}. Found only in late glosses. Replaced the Classical equivalent {{m|la|pedĕs}}, since the latter was at risk of homophony with {{m|la|pedēs|pos="feet", and other inflexions thereof}} due to ongoing sound changes in the vernacular.<ref>{{R:FEW|8|146|pĕdo}}</ref> Romance inherited sense 1, often with transferred meanings like 'footsoldier', 'peasant'.

====Noun====
{{la-noun|pedō<3>|g=m}} {{tlb|la|LL.}}? <!-- 'Found only late, in glosses' - FEW. But how late? -->

# [[pedestrian]]
# [[person]] with [[broad]] [[feet]]
#: {{syn|la|pānsa}}
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin|military}} [[foot soldier]]

