Page 4254 percipio: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{affix|la|per-|gloss1=through|capiō|gloss2=capture, seize; understand}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|percipiō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|percipiō|percēp|percept}}

# to [[seize]] or [[take on]] ([[entirely]]); [[assume]]; [[earn]]; [[occupy]], [[keep]] (i.e. maintain control)
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Caesar|Caesar]]|[[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]]|VII, 27|quote=Cohortatus ut aliquando pro tantis laboribus fructum victoriae '''perciperent'''|t=Exhorts them to finally '''seize''' the fruit of victory in exchange for their exertions}}
# to [[perceive]], [[observe]], [[notice]]
#: {{syn|la|observō}}
# to [[feel]], [[perceive]]
#: {{syn|la|sapiō|sentiō|cernō|cōnspicor}}
# to [[learn]], [[know]], [[conceive]], [[comprehend]], [[understand]]
#: {{syn|la|agnōscō|cognōscō|inveniō|sentiō|comperiō|cōnsciō|sapiō|sciō|nōscō|scīscō|intellegō|discernō|tongeō|cernō|audiō}}
#: {{ant|la|ignōrō|nesciō}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|4|938|quote=‘causam '''percipe'''’ flāmen ait.|trans=''‘‘'''Understand''' the reason,’’ the flamen said.''<br/>(Spoken by the {{w|Flamen Quirinalis}}; see also {{w|flamen}}.)}}

====Conjugation====
