===Etymology===
{{affix|la|perennis|-ō|id2=denominative}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|perennō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|perennō}}

# {{lb|la|transitive|post-Augustan}} to keep or preserve long
#* {{Q|la|Col.||12|20|8|quote=ea res, etiamsi non in totum '''perennat''', certe usque in alteram vindemiam plerumque vini saporem servat}}
#* {{Q|la|Col.||12|19|2}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive|in|_|poetry|and|in|_|post-Augustan|_|prose}} to last for many years, to last, continue, endure
#* {{Q|la|Ov.|A. A.|3|42|quote=arte '''perennat''' amor}}
#* {{Q|la|Col.||1|9|2|quote=ut diutius '''perennent''' boves}}
#* {{Q|la|Col.||2|9|18}}
#* {{Q|la|Ov.|F.|1|721|quote=domus}}
#* {{Q|la|Sol.||52|28|quote=Apud Ctesiam legitur quasdam feminas ibi semel parere natosque canos ilico fieri; esse rursum gentem alteram, quae in iuuenta cana sit, nigrescat in senectute, ultra aeui nostri terminos '''perennantem'''.}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive|Late Latin}} to last for a year
#* {{Q|la|Macr.|S.|1|12|6|quote=Huius etiam prima die ignem novum Vestae aris accendebant, ut incipiente anno cura denuo servandi novati ignis inciperet: eodem quoque ingrediente mense tam in regia curiisque atque flaminum domibus laureae veteres novis laureis mutabantur: eodem quoque mense et publice et privatim ad Annam Perennam sacrificatum itur, ut annare '''perennareque''' commode liceat.}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+|perennō}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|la|perannō}}

====Descendants====
