===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*peyḱ-|id=mark}}
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*peyḱ-||to mark, paint; spot, color}}, possibly via intermediate {{m|itc-pro||*pink-}} plus voicing assimilation, from the nasal-infixed form {{m|ine-pro||*pinéḱti ~ *pinḱénti}}; cognate with {{der|la|grc|ποικίλος||spotted, embroidered}}, {{cog|sla-pro|*pьstrъ||multicolored, variegated}} (e.g. {{cog|cs|pestrý}}). Pokorny also links to the root: {{m+|grc|πικρός||sharp, keen}}, {{m+|sla-pro|*pьsati||paint, write}} (see {{m+|cs|psát}}, {{cog|ru|пятно́}}, {{m|ru|писать}} etc.), {{cog|gem-pro|*faihaz||spotted}} (whence {{cog|ang|fāh}}, {{cog|sco|faw}}). Compare also {{cog|sa|पिङ्क्ते||to paint, tinge, dye}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|pingō}}

===Verb===
