Page 4443 placeo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
See the related {{m|la|plācō|t=to appease, placate}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|placeō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2+.opt-semi-depon|placeō}}

# {{lb|la|with dative}} to be [[pleasing]] or [[agreeable]] to; to [[please]], to be [[nice]]; to be [[welcome]] or [[acceptable]]; to [[satisfy]], [[suit]] {{q|in a mental rather than a sensual way}}
#: {{syn|la|gaudeō|ovō|exhilarō|grātulor|congrātulor|fruor}}
#: {{ant|la|displiceō}}
#: {{uxi|la|sibi '''placēre'''|to be '''pleased''' with oneself, to act proud}}
#: {{uxi|la|'''placet''' mihi|I find this '''fine/nice'''}}
#: {{uxi|la|sī dīs '''placet'''|gods willing|lit=if it '''pleases''' the gods}}
#: {{uxi|la|'''placēns''' uxor|'''dear''' wife}}
#: {{uxi|la|hostia '''placens''' Deō|a sacrifice that '''pleases''' God}}
#: {{uxi|la|vidē sī satis '''placet'''|see if this '''suits'''}}
#: {{uxi|la|ita nōbīs '''placitum est''', ut{{...}}|I '''thought it fitting''' to{{...}}}}
#: {{uxi|la|senātuī '''placet'''|the Senate '''decrees'''}}
# {{lb|la|with dative}} to [[like]] {{q|the dative should be translated as the subject in English}}
# to [[resolve]], [[will]], [[order]], [[determine]]
#: {{syn|la|statuō|cernō|dēcernō|parō|cōnstituō}}

====Usage notes====
Designates pleasure in something that one finds agreeable, fitting, while {{m|la|libet}} refers to a pursuit of something desirable or pleasurable.

Contrasts with {{m|la|dēlectō|t=to please the senses, delight, entertain}}.

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|2+.opt-semi-depon|placeō}}

