Page 4444 placo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Traditionally uncertain. The relation with {{der|la|ine-pro|*pleh₂-|t=wide and flat}} offered by Pokorny is rejected by De Vaan, who suggests {{der|la|ine-pro|*pleHk-|t=pleasingness or permission}}, with only Tocharian relatives. If the laryngeal is ''h₂'', a semantically difficult relationship could be drawn to {{der|la|ine-pro|*pleh₂k-|t=to hit}}, whence {{cog|grc|πλήσσω|t=I strike}}. Related to {{m|la|placeō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|plācō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|plācō}}

# to [[appease]]
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|4|155-156|quote=supplicibus verbīs illam '''plācāte''': sub illā<br/>et fōrma et mōrēs et bona fāma manet.|trans='''''Appease''' her with humble supplications; under her [protection]<br/>abide [not only] beauty and character [but also] good reputation.''<br/>(See {{w|Venus (mythology)}}.)}}
# to [[placate]], [[pacify]], [[assuage]], [[soothe]], [[calm]], [[quiet]]
#: {{syn|la|domō|lēniō|sōpiō|sēdō|dēlēniō|mānsuēscō|mānsuētō|mītigō|compōnō|restinguō|commītigō|levō|ēlevō|allevō|alleviō|sileō|molliō}}
#: {{ant|la|sollicitō|excitō|īnstīgō|īnstinguō|efferō|exciō|perpellō|concieō|concitō|īnflammō|cieō|incendō}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|142-143|quote=Sīc ait, et dictō citius tumida aequora '''plācat''',<br/>collēctāsque fugat nūbēs, sōlemque redūcit.|trans=''Thus says [Neptune], and quicker than his speech he '''soothes''' the swollen waters, routs the gathered clouds, and brings back the sun.''}}
# to [[reconcile]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+|plācō}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|la|plācātiō}}

