#* {{Q|la|[[w:Julius Caesar|Caesar]], [[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]], VII, 10|quote='''Praestare''' visum est tamen omnis difficultates perpeti, quam tanta contumelia accepta omnium suorum voluntates alienare|However it seemed '''better''' to endure any hardship '''than''' to alienate the affections of all his allies, by submitting to such an insult}}
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Caesar|Caesar]], [[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]], VII, 17|quote='''Praestare''' omnes perferre acerbitates, quam non civibus Romanis, qui [[w:Cenabum|Cenabi]] perfidia Gallorum interissent, parentarent|It was '''better''' to sustain any hardship '''than''' to not avenge the Roman citizens who perished at Genabum by the perfidy of the Gauls}}
#: {{uxi|la|In acie praestare interfici quam non veterem belli gloriam [...] recuperare|It was '''better''' to be slain in battle, '''than''' not to recover the ancient glory in war}} ([[w:Caesar|Caesar]], [[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]], VII, 1)
# to be [[outstanding]], be [[exceeding]] in something, to [[excel]], [[stand out]], be [[superior]], to [[distinguish]] oneself, be [[excellent]], [[distinguished]], [[admirable]]
