Page 4641 prehendo: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|la|prēndō||Classical}}
* {{alt|la|praendō|praehendō|prindō||Late Latin}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*gʰed-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro||*praiɣendō}}, equivalent to {{affix|la|prae-|t1=fore-, pre-|*hendō|t2=to take, seize}} (not attested without prefix), from {{der|la|ine-pro|*gʰed-}}; akin to {{cog|grc|χανδάνω||hold, contain}}, and {{cog|en|get}}. The vowel probably underwent regular reduction in prefixed variants (''*-praind- > -prēnd-'') and was backported into the base form. Related to {{m|la|praeda||prey}} and {{m|la|hedera||ivy}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=Prehendō}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|prehendō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|prehendō|prehend|prehēns}}

# to [[lay]] [[hold]] of, [[seize]], [[grasp]], [[grab]], [[snatch]], [[take]], [[catch]]
#: {{syn|la|comprehendō|dēprehendō|apprehendō|capessō|teneō|capiō|arripiō|sūmō|prehēnsō}}
# to [[detain]] someone in order to [[speak]] with them, [[accost]], lay or catch hold of
# to [[take]] by [[surprise]], catch [[in the act]]
#: {{syn|la|opprimō|dēprehendō}}
# {{lb|la|of trees}} to [[take root]]
# {{lb|la|poetic}} to [[reach]], [[arrive at]], [[attain]]
#: {{syn|la|perveniō|adveniō|ēvādō|obeō|adsum|teneō|tangō}}
# {{lb|la|poetic}} to [[take in]], reach or [[embrace]] with the eye
# {{lb|la|figuratively|rare|of the mind}} to seize, [[apprehend]], [[comprehend]], grasp

====Usage notes====
Used in the following constructions: (3) uses the ablative, the genitive or {{m|la|in}} with the ablative.

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|prehendō|prehend|prehēns}}

====Derived terms====
{{top2}}
* {{l|la|apprehendō}}
* {{l|la|comprehendō}}
* {{l|la|dēprehendō}}
* {{l|la|prehensiō}} / {{l|la|prēnsiō}}
* {{l|la|prehensō}} / {{l|la|prēnsō}}
* {{l|la|prehensus}} / {{l|la|prēnsus}}
* {{l|la|reprehendō}}
{{bottom}}

