#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|1|157-158|quote=tum blandī solēs, ignōtaque '''prōdit''' hirundō<br/>et lūteum celsa sub trabe fīgit opus|trans=''Then is the sunshine refreshing; and the stranger swallow '''comes forth''', and builds her fabric of clay beneath the lofty rafter.''<br/>'''1851'''. ''The Fasti &c of Ovid.'' Trans. & notes by {{w|H. T. Riley}}. London: {{w|H. G. Bohn}}. pg. 13.}}
