===Etymology===
From {{pre|la|prō|habeō|t2=I have}}. Compare {{noncog|ang|forhealdan}} for the formation.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|prohibeō|eccl=yes}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-prohibeo.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2+|prohibeō}}

# to [[hold]] back or before, [[keep]] or [[ward]] off, [[restrain]]; [[avert]]; [[prevent]], [[hinder]]
#: {{syn|la|impediō|obstō|moror|arceō|cohibeō|supprimō|cūnctor|contineō|dētineō|retineō|refrēnō|tardō|intersaepiō|inclūdō|perimō|obstō|officiō}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|540-541|quote=“Hospitiō '''prohibēmur''' harēnae;<br/>bella cient, prīmāque vetant cōnsistere terrā.”|trans=''“'''We''' [Trojans] '''are being kept back''' from the refuge of the beach; [the Carthaginians] provoke hostilities, and they forbid [us] to set foot on the first [part of your] land [i.e., the shoreline].”''<br/>(Trojan envoy Ilioneus is addressing Queen Dido.)}}
# to [[forbid]], [[prohibit]]
#: {{syn|la|abdīcō|vetō}}
# to [[keep]], [[preserve]], [[defend]], [[protect]]
#: {{syn|la|salvō|tūtor|vindicō|servō|cū̆stōdiō|sospitō|teneō|adimō|prōtegō|tegō|adsum|sustineō|dēfendō|tueor|arceō}}
#: {{ant|la|immineō|īnstō|obiectō}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|525|quote=“ōrāmus '''prohibē''' īnfandōs ā nāvibus ignīs”|trans=''“We beg [you]: '''Keep''' dreadful fires [away] from [our] ships!”''<br/>(Ilioneus petitions Queen Dido to protect the Trojan fleet now moored near Carthage.)}}
# to [[keep]] someone (''[[Appendix:Glossary#accusative_case|accusative]]'') off something (''[[Appendix:Glossary#ablative_case|ablative]]'')
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Caesar|Caesar]]|[[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]]|VII, 14|quote={{l|la|ut}} {{l|la|pabulatione}} {{l|la|et}} {{l|la|commeatu}} {{l|la|Romani}} '''prohibeantur'''|t=So that the Romans should be '''prohibited''' from foraging and procuring the provisions}}

====Conjugation====
