Page 4792 puto: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|putō}}

===Etymology 1===
Either from {{suf|la|putus|ō|id2=denominative}}, or else from {{der|la|ine-pro|*paw-||to strike}}, which would make it cognate with {{m|la|puteus}}. For sense development, compare {{m|la|dēcīdō}}.

====Verb====
{{la-verb|1+.poet-sync-perf|putō}}

# (very rare) to [[clean]], [[cleanse]]
# to [[trim]], [[prune]], [[lop]]
# {{lb|la|figurative}} to [[arrange]], [[settle]]
# {{lb|la|figurative}} to [[value]], [[esteem]], [[deem]], [[regard]], [[consider]]
#* {{Q|la|Terence|Heauton Timorumenos|1|77|quote=Homō sum, hūmānī nihil ā mē aliēnum '''putō'''.|trans=I am a human, I '''consider''' nothing that is human alien to me.}}
#* {{Q|la|Catullus||12|4|quote=Hoc salsum esse '''putās'''?|trans=Do you '''think''' that's funny?}}
# {{lb|la|figurative}} to [[judge]], [[suspect]], [[suppose]]
#* {{Q|la|Suetonius|Life of Vespasian|23|4|quote=Prima quoque morbi accessione, ''Vae'', inquit, '''''puto''', deus fio.''|trans=As death drew near, <nowiki>[</nowiki>[[w:Vespasian|Vespasian]]<nowiki>]</nowiki> said, ''Dear me, I '''suspect''' I'm becoming a god.''}}
# {{lb|la|figurative}} to [[ponder]], consider, [[think about]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|1+.poet-sync-perf|putō}}

=====Synonyms=====
