Page 4801 quaero: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{qualifier|old desiderative?}}: {{l|la|quaesō}}

===Etymology===
{{unc|la}}. According to Nussbaum and de Vaan, from {{der|la|itc-pro|*kʷaizeō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*kʷeh₂-||to acquire}}, via a ''se/o''-present built upon an ''i''-present form {{m|ine-pro|*kʷeh₂-i-||to acquire}}. In this case, cognates would include Ancient Greek {{m|grc|πέπαμαι||to get, acquire}}, Old Prussian {{m|prg|quoi||I/you want}} and {{m|prg|quāits||desire}}, {{m+|lt|kviẽsti||to invite}}. 

In some sources etymologized as being from {{der|la|ine-pro|*kʷeys-|*kʷoys-, *kʷeys-|to see}}, but this was deemed uncertain by Schrijver in 1991.

[[w:Lexikon der indogermanischen Verben|LIV]] accepts Szemerényi's 1960 etymology that it is a derivation of {{m|ine-pro|*h₂eys-||to seek, ask}}, via the form {{m|ine-pro||*koaiseo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|quaerō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3.poet-sync-perf|quaerō|quaesīv/quaesi|quaesīt}}

# to [[seek]], [[look]] for
#: {{syn|la|requīrō|studeō|spectō|petō|appetō|affectō|cupiō|concupiō|inquīrō|conquīrō|expetō|dēstinō|sitiō|aveō|voveō|circumspiciō|tendō|intendō}}
#: {{ant|la|āversor|abhorreō|dēclīnō}}
#: {{uxi|la|'''Quaerendo''' {{l|la|invenietis}}|t=By seeking ye shall find}}
#: {{uxi|la|'''Quaerite''' {{l|la|Dominum}}|t=Seek ye the Lord}}
# to [[ask]], [[question]], seek or [[search]] for a thing, [[inquire]], [[query]], [[interrogate]]
#: {{syn|la|scīscitor|percontor|investīgō|scīscō|indāgō|interrogō|requīrō|rogitō|scrūtor}}
#: {{uxi|la|'''Quaeritur''' num mors malum sit.|t=The question is whether death is an evil.}}
# to [[strive]] for; [[endeavor]]; seek to [[obtain]]
#: {{syn|la|lūctor|certō|ēlabōrō|cōnītor|cōnor|ēnītor|appetō|affectō|tendō|quaesō|temptō|studeō|circumspiciō|īnsequor|contendō|adnītor|labōrō|pugnō|molior|perīclitor|nītor|spectō}}
# to [[miss]], [[lack]]
# to [[desire]], [[require]], [[want]], [[aim]] at
#: {{syn|la|requīrō|affectō|cupiō|aveō|studeō|concupiō|indigeō|sitiō|petō|expetō|spectō|voveō|appetō|dēstinō}}

