Page 4810 quiesco: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*kʷyeh₁-}}
From {{suffix|la|quiēs|t1=rest, repose; quiet|scō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|quiēscō|eccl=yes}}

Aulus Gellius (''Noctes Atticae,'' c. 177) reports that in the usual pronunciation of his time, the "e" was short; a friend of his justified this pronunciation by appeal to common usage when challenged by another friend who argued that it should be long by analogy with the long ē in ''calescit, nitescit, stupescit'' and in ''quiēs.'' On the other hand, there is inscriptional evidence of long "e" in this word in the form of inscriptions which mark it with an apex (CIL VI.6250 and 25521.)<ref>[https://penelope.uchicago.edu/Thayer/E/Roman/Texts/Gellius/7*.html#note51 Gellius, Attic Nights, Book VII.] Translated by J. C. Rolfe. First published with notes in Vol. II of the Loeb Classical Library edition, 1927. Republished online at LacusCurtius by Bill Thayer. Note 51.</ref>

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3.nopass.poet-sync-perf|quiēscō|quiēv|quiēt}}

# to [[rest]], [[sleep]], [[repose]]
#: {{syn|la|cessō|dormiō|conquiēscō|requiēscō|acquiēscō}}
# to [[cause]] to [[cease]], [[stop]], [[render]] [[quiet]]
# {{lb|la|especially of inanimate objects}} to be [[still]] or quiet, [[lie]] still
# to [[remain]] [[neutral]], [[abstain]] from [[action]], [[keep]] quiet, [[stand by]]
# {{lb|la|in speech}} to [[make]] a [[pause]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[suffer]] or [[allow]] [[quietly]]; [[permit]]
#: {{syn|la|cōnīveō}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to cease, [[leave]] off or [[desist]] from something
#: {{syn|la|cessō|subsistō|dēsistō|remittō|dēsinō|sistō|conticēscō|trānseō}}
#: {{ant|la|coepiō|incohō|incipiō}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3.nopass.poet-sync-perf|quiēscō|quiēv|quiēt}}

