Page 4815 quirito: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{unc|la}}, perhaps from  {{cog|la|queror||to complain}} through the form, though the phonetic and semantic developments are difficult to trace; alternatively, a variant of {{m|la|quirritāre||to squeal like a pig}}, from ''*quis'', an onomatopoeic rendition of squeaking. An ancient folk etymology understood it as  "to call for the help of the {{m|la|Quirites}}," the Roman constabulary. Compare the Frankish {{m|frk|*krītan|t=to cry out, scream, proclaim}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|quĭrītō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|quirītō}}

# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[call upon]] for [[help]]
# {{lb|la|intransitive| of orators}} to [[scream]], [[shriek]]
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[protest]] by screaming

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+|quirītō}}

