#* {{Q|la|Cicero|Philippicae|5|8|22|quote=cum eius promissis legiones fortissimae '''reclamassent''' {{...}}|trans=For when those gallant legions had '''cried out''' against his promises {{...}}}}
#* '''12/05 2012''', Herimannus Novocomensis, ''Ephemeris''
#*: '''Reclamatur''' in Ucraina.
#*:: '''There is being protested''' in Ukraine.
# to [[call]] for someone back, again, aloud or repeatedly
#* {{Q|la|Gaius Valerius Flaccus|Argonautica|8|172|quote=famulae pariter clamore supremo / in vacuos dant verba notos dominamque '''reclamant''' / nomine|trans=With them the handmaidens raise cries of last farewell and scatter words upon the empty breeze, as by name they '''call''' mistress '''back again'''.}}
# {{lb|la|poetic}} to [[reverberate]], [[reecho]], [[resound]]
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Georgicon|3|261|quote=nempe abruptis turbata procellis / nocte natat caeca serus freta, quem super ingens / porta tonat caeli, et scopulis inlisa '''reclamant''' / aequora|trans=See how he swims the straits in a confusion of steep waterspouts, late in the dark of night. Heavens mighty doorway thunders above him, and the waves striking the cliffs '''reecho'''.}}

