Page 4893 reduco: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*wredoukō}}. Equivalent to {{affix|la|re-|gloss1=back, again|dūcō|gloss2=lead}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|redūcō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg|redūcō}}

# to [[lead]], [[draw]], [[bring]] or [[conduct]] back; bring or [[accompany]] home
# {{lb|la|military|of troops}} to [[withdraw]], cause to [[retreat]], draw back, [[remove]]
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Caesar|Caesar]]|[[w:de Bello Gallico|de Bello Gallico]]|VII, 24|quote=Ut [...] alii turres '''reducerent'''|t=That [...] others should '''draw back''' the towers}}
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[bring back]], [[restore]], [[recall]], [[revive]], [[replace]]; [[reform]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to bring, [[produce]] or [[get out]] a quantity of
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to bring, [[make]] or [[reduce]] to a certain condition or quality
# to [[recall]] to the [[mind]], [[remember]], [[remind]]
#: {{syn|la|memorō|referō|moneō|retineō|meminī|admoneō}}
#: {{ant|la|oblīvīscor|oblitterō}}
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin}} to {{l|en|quell}}, to {{l|en|subdue}}, to {{l|en|subjugate}} {{defdate|10th C.}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|irreg|redūcō}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|I subjugate}} {{l|la|subiugō}} {{qualifier|Classical}}

====Derived terms====
{{top2}}
