===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*dʰeh₁-}}
From {{prefix|la|re-|gloss1=back; again|faciō|gloss2=do, make}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|reficiō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|reficiō|refēc|refect}}

# to [[make]] again, make [[anew]]; [[remake]], [[renew]], [[rebuild]], [[reconstruct]]
#: {{syn|la|iterō|integrō|redintegrō|renovō|novō|reparō|referō}}
# to [[restore]], [[repair]], [[fix]], [[refit]]
#: {{syn|la|ēmendō|reparō|corrigō|medeor}}
# to [[reappoint]], [[re-elect]]
# {{lb|la|of troops}} to [[recruit]], [[reinforce]]
# {{lb|la|of income}} to [[get back]], get in [[return]], make again
# {{lb|la|of the body or mind}} to make [[strong]] again, [[reinvigorate]], [[refresh]], [[revive]], recruit, restore
#: {{syn|la|reparō|exhilarō|revocō}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|3|711|quote=Postera cum tenerās aurōra '''refēcerit''' herbās|trans=''When the following dawn '''shall have refreshed''' the tender plants''<br/>Or, the future perfect tense is often translated as a more natural-sounding English present or perfect tense:<br/>''When the following dawn '''has refreshed''' the tender plants''}}
# to [[obtain]], [[earn]], [[get]], [[amass]], [[collect]]
#: {{syn|la|contrahō|conferō|convehō|cōnstruō|compellō|glomerō|congerō|cōgō}}

