Page 4951 rem acu tango: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|la|acū tangō}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|la|rem}} the accusative of {{m|la|rēs||thing, matter, issue}} + {{m|la|acū||with a needle}}, the ablative of {{m|la|acus||a needle}} + {{m|la|tangō||I touch}}. Literally meaning "I touch the issue with a needle", "I touch the matter with a needle", or "I touch it with a needle".

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|'rem acū tangō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|prefix=[[res|rem]] [[acus|acū]]|passive_prefix=[[rēs]] [[acus|acū]]|3|tangō|tetig|tāct}}

# {{lb|la|idiomatic}} to [[hit the nail on the head]]

====Usage notes====
* Usually used in the active perfect second person singular form {{m|la|rem acu tetigisti|'''rem acū tetigistī'''|'you have touched the matter with a needle'; you have hit the nail on the head}}, the word ''rem'' is sometimes omitted as in {{m|la|acū tetigistī||'you have touched with a needle'- you have hit the nail on the head}}. It is also used in the [[third person]]; {{m|la|rem acū tetigit||'he touched it with a needle'- he has hit the nail on the head}}.<ref>[http://books.google.is/books?id=bXGJuX1mDrwC&lpg=PP1&pg=PA201]</ref>

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3.nopass|rem acū tangō|rem acū tetig|rem acū tāct}}

===References===
<references/>

[[Category:Latin phrasal verbs]]
