{{glossary|intransitive|Intransitive}} with very few exceptions, e.g. {{w|Cicero}}, ''{{w|De Legibus}}'', 2.22.55: “{{lang|la|denicales, quae a nece appellatae sunt, quia '''residentur''' mortuis}}” (“the {{m|la|denicalis|denicales}} [days of purification], which are named from {{m|la|nex}} [death], because they are '''spent in idleness''' [‘idled’] for the dead”).

