Page 5076 retrovendo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*deh₃-}}
From Classical Latin {{compound|la|retrō|vēndō|t1=[[retro-]]: [[back]], [[again]]|t2=[[sell]]}}, from {{m|la|[[vēnum]] [[dō]]||[[give]] for [[sale]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|retrōvēndō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|retrōvēndō|retrōvēndid|retrōvēndit}}

# {{lb|la|Late Latin}} to [[resell]], [[revend]]

====Usage notes====
In Classical Latin, {{m|la|retrō}} was typically used as a coordinate adverb rather than a prefix. Similarly, the only passive forms used for {{m|la|vēndō}} were the past participle {{m|la|revēnditus}} and the future participle {{m|la|revēndendus}}; other forms were later supplied by analogy with {{m|la|vēneō}}.

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|retrōvēndō|retrōvēndid|retrōvēndit}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|la|revēndō}}

