===Etymology===
Either from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₃reǵ-}} and a {{doublet|la|regō|nocap=1}}, or from {{m|la|procō}} and a doublet of {{doublet|la|precor|notext=1}} and {{doublet|la|procus|notext=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|rogō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+.p3inf.poet-sync-perf|rogō}}

# to [[ask]], [[enquire]]
#: {{syn|la|interrogō}}
# to [[request]]
#: {{syn|la|requīrō|flagitō|efflagitō|exigō|exposcō|exorō|petō|rogitō|ērogō|expetō|precor|repetō}}
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Curculio|5|3|5|quote={{smallcaps|Cappadox}}: Iam iam faciam ut iusseris.<br>{{smallcaps|Therapontigonus}}: Quando vir bonus es, responde quod '''rogo'''.<br>{{smallcaps|Cappadox}}: Roga quod lubet.<sup>[http://www.thelatinlibrary.com/plautus/curculio.shtml]</sup>|trans={{smallcaps|Cappadox}}: Here, here, I’ll do as you say!<br>{{smallcaps|Therapontigonus}}: Now that you are decent, answer me what I '''ask'''.<br>{{smallcaps|Cappadox}}: Ask what you like.<sup>[http://artemis.austincollege.edu/acad/cml/rcape/comedy/5-3.html]</sup>}}
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Captivi|627|url=http://www.ihaystack.com/authors/m/plautus_titus_maccius/00016564_amphitryo_asinaria_aulularia_bacchides_captivi_amphi/00016564_englishlatin_utf8_p043.htm|quote=Haud istuc '''rogo'''. Fuistine liber? - Fui.|trans=That isn’t what I’m '''asking''' about. Were you a freeman? - I was.}}
# to [[beg]], [[solicit]], [[pray]] to (someone) for (something) {{q|with two accusatives}}
#: {{syn|la|supplicō|ōrō|obsecrō|expetō|efflāgitō|flāgitō|quaesō}}

