===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₁rewg-}}
From {{affix|la|*rūgō|-tō|pos1=I belch, whence {{m|la|rū̆ctus||belch}} and {{m|la|ērūgō}}|pos2=frequentative suffix}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₁rewg-||belch, roar}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|rocettan||I belch}} and {{cog|grc|ἐρεύγομαι||to belch, vomit, emit}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|rū̆ctō}}
* The ''u'' in the first syllable is short per De Vaan (2008)<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=-rūgō, -ere|page=529}}</ref> and Wartburg (1928–2002)<ref>{{R:FEW|10|539|rŭctare}}</ref>; long per Bennett (1907)<ref>{{R:Bennett 1907|page=64}}</ref> (who however says that there is Romance evidence for both long ū and short ŭ).

