Page 5155 salio: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|saliō}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*saljō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*sel-|t=to spring}}. Cognates include {{cog|grc|ἅλλομαι}} and {{cog|sa|सरति|tr=sárati}}.

====Verb====
{{la-verb|4|saliō|salu|salt}}

# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[leap]], [[jump]], [[bound]]
#: {{syn|la|trānsiliō|prōsiliō|assiliō|exsiliō|īnsultō|exsultō}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[spring]] [[forth]], [[flow]] [[down]]
# {{lb|la|transitive|of male animals}} to [[mount]] for [[copulation]]

=====Usage notes=====
The passive forms of this verb are very rare, pertaining only to the transitive sense of "mounting":
* {{Q|la|Ovid|Ars Amatoria|II|485|quote=Laeta '''salitur''' ovis: tauro quoque laeta iuvenca est|trans=The delighted sheep '''is mounted''': the heifer too is happy with a bull}}

