# to [[purify]]; to free from [[sin]]
#* {{RQ:Vulgate|ad Corinthios I|6|11|passage=et haec quidam fuistis sed abluti estis sed '''sanctificati''' estis sed iustificati estis in nomine Domini nostri Iesu Christi et in Spiritu Dei nostri|translation=And such were some of you: but ye are washed, but ye are '''sanctified''', but ye are justified in the name of the Lord Jesus, and by the Spirit of our God.}}
# to make [[acceptable]] or [[useful]] under [[religious]] law or practice
#* {{RQ:Vulgate|ad Timotheum I|4|4-5|passage=quia omnis creatura Dei bona et nihil reiciendum quod cum gratiarum actione percipitur: '''sanctificatur''' enim per verbum Dei et orationem|translation=For every creature of God is good, and nothing to be refused, if it be received with thanksgiving: For it is '''sanctified''' by the word of God and prayer}}

