Page 5168 sapio: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*seh₁p-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*sapiō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro||*sh₁p-i-|to notice}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*sep-|alt=*seh₁p-|to try, to research}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|sefa||mind, spirit, mood}} and possibly with {{cog|grc|σοφός||wisdom}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|sapiō}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-sapio.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3.nopass|sapiō|sapīv/sapi/sapu}}

# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[have]] [[taste]], have [[flavour]]
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[taste]] of, [[taste]] like, [[smack]] of, have a [[flavour]] of
#: {{syn|la|lambō}}
# {{lb|la|figurative|intransitive}} to have good taste; have [[sense]], [[discernment]]; be [[sensible]], [[discreet]], [[prudent]], [[wise]]
#: {{syn|la|sentiō|percipiō}}
# {{lb|la|figurative|transitive}} to [[know]], [[understand]] (mostly with general objects)
# {{lb|la|EML.}} to [[know]] how to do; to be [[able]] to do

