Page 5240 sepellio: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|la|sepeliō}}, with gemination of /l/. Found in imperial inscriptions. 

===Verb===
{{la-verb|4|sepelliō|sepellīv|sepult/sepellīt}}

# {{lb|la|non-standard}} to [[bury]]

====Reconstruction notes====
Early on there appears to have arisen a variant {{m|VL.||*sepulliō}} by analogy with the participle {{m|la|sepultus|sep'''u'''ltus}}. Some of the Romance forms may have adapted to reflexes of the prefix {{m|la|sub-}}. There seems to have been an early gemination of the /p/ in Italy, though this was not universal.

