# {{lb|la|figuratively}} to [[move]] [[slowly]] or [[imperceptibly]], to [[creep]] [[in]] or [[along]], [[proceed]] [[gradually]] {{q|of a thing or situation}}
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|2|268-269|quote=“Tempus erat quō prīma quiēs mortālibus aegrīs<br/>incipit et dōnō dīvum grātissima '''serpit'''.”|trans=''“It was the time when the first rest for careworn mortals begins, and as a gift of the gods '''it creeps in''' most pleasantly.”''<br/>(The [[irony]] of “[[incipit]]” and “serpit”: As the weary Trojans rest, Greek soldiers “creep” from the wooden horse; the nighttime attack “begins”.)}}

