Page 5278 sisto: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*steh₂-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*sistō}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*stísteh₂ti}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*steh₂-||stand}}. Related to {{m|la|stō||stand, be stood}}, from the same root, with which {{m|la||sistō}} shares its supine forms.

Cognates include {{cog|grc|ἵστημι}} and {{cog|sa|तिष्ठति|tr=tíṣṭhati}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|sistō|eccl=1}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|sistō|stit|stat}}

# {{lb|la|transitive}} to cause to [[stand]]; to [[set]]; to [[place]]
#: {{syn|la|collocō|loco|statuō|pōnō|fīgō|cōnstituō|struō|impōnō|defigo}}
# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[stop]], to [[halt]]
#: {{syn|la|resistō|retineō|prohibeō|impediō|intersaepio|cohibeō|arceō|teneō|obsto|adversor|exclūdō}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|VI|154|quote='''Sistite''' vōs lacrimās.|trans='''Halt''' your tears.}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[place]] oneself; to [[stand]]
#: {{syn|la|cōnstō|stō|cōnsistō|remaneō|maneō|haereō}}
# to [[stabilise]], [[consolidate]], [[strengthen]], [[reinforce]]
#: {{syn|la|firmō|cōnfirmō|mūniō|cōnsolidō|fortificō}}
#: {{ant|la|dēterō|atterō|minuō|frangō|tenuō|afficiō}}
# {{lb|la|transitive|legal}} to cause to [[appear]] in court
# {{lb|la|intransitive|legal}} to [[appear]] in court
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to [[stop]], to [[stand]] still; to [[halt]]; to stand firm
#: {{syn|la|cessō|subsistō|dēsistō|remittō|dēsinō|quiēscō|conticēscō|trānseō}}
#: {{ant|la|coepiō|incohō|incipiō}}
#: {{uxi|la|'''Siste!'''|'''Stop!'''}}

====Conjugation====
* Perfects of the form ''stetī'' for this verb are considered doubtful.
{{la-conj|3|sistō|stit|stat}}

