===Etymology===
{{word|la|ine|swé}}{{root|la|ine-pro|*lewh₁-}}
From {{af|la|se-|luō|t1=away|t2=to untie, set free, separate}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|solvō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|solvō|solv|solūt}}

# to [[loosen]], [[untie]], [[undo]]; [[free]] [up], [[release]], acquit, exempt
#: {{syn|la|rumpo|persolvo|absolvo|explicō|distraho|dissolvo}}
#: {{ant|la|ligō|colligō|illigō|cōnserō|cōnfīgō|adalligō|alligō|dēligō|nectō|cōnectō|dēfīgō|fīgō}}
# to [[solve]], [[explain]]
# to [[dissolve]], [[break]] up, separate
#: {{ux|la|similia similibus '''solvuntur'''|Like '''dissolves''' like.}}
# to [[relax]], [[slacken]], [[weaken]]
#* {{Q|la|Horace|Odes|2|2|4|thru=7|quote=Vīvet extentō Proculeius aevō,<br>nōtus in frātrēs animī paternī;<br>illum aget pennā metuente '''solvī'''<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fāma superstes.|trans=[[w:Proculeius|Proculeius]] shall live an extended age,<br>well known for his fatherly spirit to his brothers;<br>him will bear with feather scorning to '''be relaxed'''<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;enduring Fame.}}
# to [[cancel]], [[remove]], [[destroy]]
#: {{syn|la|cancellō}}
# to [[pay up]], fulfil
#: {{syn|la|ērogō|pendo|persolvo|luo|absolvo|dissolvo}}
# to [[undermine]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} (emotion, feelings) to [[get]] [[rid]] of, [[let]] [[go]] of, [[release]], [[dismiss]], [[loosen]]
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|562|quote=“'''Solvite''' corde metum, Teucrī, sēclūdite cūrās.”|trans=''“'''Release''' the fear within your heart[s], Teucrians, [and] banish worries.”''<br/>(Dido tells the Trojan envoys to “unbind” the inner physical tension which follows intense emotion.)}}
# to let down (hair)
# to open (a letter)
# to [[unfurl]]
# to raise (a siege)
# to dismiss (troops)
# to set sail (ships)

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|solvō|solv|solūt}}

