===Etymology 2===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*(s)teh₂-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*(s)ta(je)-tōd|t=must steal}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*(s)teh₂-}}, see also  {{cog|hit|tr=tāyezzi}}, {{m|hit|tr=tāyazzi|t=to steal}}, {{cog|sga|táid||thief}}, {{cog|sa|तायु|tr=tāyú|t=thief}}, {{cog|ae|𐬙𐬁𐬫𐬎|t=thief}}, {{cog|grc|τητάω||to deprive}}, {{m|grc|τηΰσιος||deceptive, (in) vain}} (Doric {{m|grc|τᾱΰσιος}}).<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|(s)ta|584}}</ref>

Failed to survive for its [[homonymy]] with the ordinary verb for “stand" (see Etymology 1 above).<ref>H. Rix, "Das letzte Wort der Duenos-Inschrif", MSS, '''46''', 1985, pp. 193 ff.; H. Eichner, "Reklameniamben aus Roms Königszeit", ''Die Sprache'', '''34''', 1988-90, p. 216.</ref>

====Verb====
{{head|la|verb|head=stō|singular future active imperative|statōd}}; ''[[Appendix:Latin first conjugation|first conjugation]]''

# {{lb|la|Old Latin lemma}} to [[steal]]
#* '''7th–5th century BC''', {{w|Duenos inscription}}:
#*: {{quote|la|𐌃𐌖𐌄𐌍𐌏𐌔𐌌𐌄𐌃𐌅𐌄𐌂𐌄𐌃𐌄𐌍𐌌𐌀𐌍𐌏𐌌𐌄𐌉𐌍𐌏𐌌𐌃𐌖𐌄𐌍𐌏𐌉𐌍𐌄𐌌𐌄𐌃𐌌𐌀𐌋𐌏'''𐌔𐌕𐌀𐌕𐌏𐌃'''|tr=DVENOSMEDFECEDENMANOMEINOMDVENOINEMEDMALO'''STATOD'''<br/>duenos mēd fēced en mānōm (m)einom duenōi nē mēd malo(s) '''statōd'''|t=A good man made me (in good intention?) for a good man; may I not be '''stolen''' by an evil man.}}

====References====
<references/>

