Page 5493 suffrago: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
This verb, its deponent version {{m|la|suffrāgor|t=to vote for, support, favor}}, and the related noun {{m|la|suffrāgium|t=voting tablet, ballot, vote}} come from  the prefix {{affix|la|sub-|t1=under}} combined with an {{unc|la|nocap=1}} root.

One proposal derives them from {{der|la|ine-pro|*bʰreg-||to break|nocat=1}}, the root of {{m|la|frangō|t=to break}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|pages=597-598|head=suffrāgium}}</ref> The semantic development might be along the same lines as in the related noun {{m|la|fragor|t=crash, din, uproar}}, with the sense "break, shatter, clash" shifting to "make clashing noises, make an uproar (in support of a candidate)" to "lend support, vote for someone".

Another proposal derives it from the same source as the noun {{m|la||suffrāgō}} (see below) and may have originally meant an ankle bone or knuckle bone.

====Pronunciation====
* {{la-IPA|suffrāgō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|1+|suffrāgō}}

# to [[support]]; to [[vote]] for

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|1+|suffrāgō}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|la|suffrāgor}}
* {{l|la|suffrāgium}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|ca|sufragar}}
* {{desc|gl|sufragar}}
* {{desc|it|suffragare}}
* {{desc|pt|sufragar}}
* {{desc|es|sufragar}}

