Page 5509 sum: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|la|esum|esom||archaic}}
* {{alt|la|essere||late, early medieval}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₁es-|*bʰuH-}}
The present stem is from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*ezom}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*h₁ésmi|t=I am, I exist}}. Note that the form {{m|la|sum}} doesn't go back directly to the Proto-Italic one, which should have given ''*erum,'' parallel for example to {{m|la|eris}} from {{m|itc-pro|*ezes}}. Instead, in the form's direct predecessor, the initial vowel was deleted and the consonant ''-z-,''  allophonically voiced between vowels, was devoiced to ''s'' instead of undergoing [[rhotacism]]. The archaically attested forms {{m|la|esum}} and {{m|la|esom}} show that the full form had also been preserved, but was pushed out of use by the Classical times. Note that although the forms {{m|la|es}} and {{m|la|est}} underwent the same [[apheresis]] of the initial vowel, this time both outcomes were preserved in the Classical language, with the shortened forms functioning as [[clitic]]s.<ref>{{cite-book|en|author=Giuseppe Pezzini|title=Terence and the Verb 'To Be' in Latin|date=2015-07-30|publisher=OUP Oxford|url=https://www.academia.edu/15349548/Terence_and_the_Verb_to_be_in_Latin|isbn=978-0-19-105582-9|page=23|url2=https://books.google.com/books?id=YE1zCgAAQBAJ&lpg=PA23&ots=dVdEoNjGVz&pg=PA23}}</ref><ref>Joseph and Wallace (1987: 687), Dunkel (1998: 89), Meiser (1998: 221), Baldi (1999), Bammesberger (2004), Clackson and Horrocks (2007: 66), Weiss (2009: 425).</ref>

Cognates include {{cog|grc|εἰμί}}, {{cog|sa|अस्मि|tr=ásmi}}, {{cog|fa|هستم|tr=hastam}} {{cog|xfa|𐌄𐌔𐌞}}, {{cog|ang|eom}} ({{cog|en|am}}).

The perfect stem is from {{inh|la|itc-pro|*fuiō|*(fe)fūai}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*bʰúHt|t=to become, be}} (whence also {{m|la|fīō|t=to become, to be made}}, and [[future]] and [[imperfect]] inflections {{m|la|-bō}}, {{m|la|-bam}}). Compare also the etymology at {{m|la|fore}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|sum|eccl=1}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-sum.ogg|Audio (Ecclesiastical)}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg|sum}}

# {{lb|la|copulative}} to [[be]], [[exist]], [[have]] {{+obj|la|dat}}
#: {{uxi|la|Civis romanus '''sum'''.|'''I am''' a Roman citizen.}}
#: {{uxi|la|'''Sum''' sine regno.|'''I am''' without a kingdom.}}
#: {{ux|la|Dixit duas res ei rubori '''fuisse'''.|He said that two things '''had''' abashed him.}}
#: {{ux|la|Mihi '''est''' multum tempus.|I '''have''' a lot of time.|lit=A lot of time '''is''' to me.}}
#* {{Q|la|Terence|Heauton Timorumenos|1|77|quote=Homō '''sum''', hūmānī nihil ā mē aliēnum putō.|t='''I am''' a man, I consider nothing that is human alien to me.}}
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|Catiline Orations|1|9|quote=Ō dī immortālēs, ubinam gentium '''sumus'''?|t=O ye immortal gods, where on earth '''are we'''?}}
#* {{quote-book|la|121 {{CE}}|w:Suetonius|w:[[The Twelve Caesars|''De Vita Caesarum'']]|||Alea iacta '''est'''.|The die '''is''' cast.|section=''[[w:Julius Caesar|Iulius]]'' [[s:la:De vita Caesarum libri VIII/Vita divi Iuli#[33]|33]]}}
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Exodus 20:12|quote=Honōrā patrem tuum et matrem tuam, ut '''sīs''' longaevus super terram, quam Dominus Deus tuus dabit tibi.|trans=Honour thy father and thy mother, that thou '''mayest be''' longlived upon the land which the Lord thy God will give thee.}}
#* {{quote-book|la|1647|w:René Descartes|''Meditationes de Prima Philosophia, in qua Dei existentia et animæ immortalitas demonstratur''|||Cogito, ergo '''sum'''.|I think, therefore '''I am'''.}}
# {{lb|la|existential}} [[there be]]
#* {{Q|la|Sen.|Hercules Oetaeus|1399|thru=1400|quote='''Est'''ne adhūc aliquid malī<br>in orbe mēcum?|trans='''Is there''' still anything bad<br>with me in the world?}}
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin|in the past tense}} to [[go]]
#: {{ux|la|Ad quod castrum vincendum Pisani '''fuerunt''' cum quinquaginta navibus, plattis et schafis, etc,
|t='''They went''' to conquer Pisanius' castle with fifty boats, engines, siege weapons, etc.}}
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin|Ecclesiastical Latin}}, imperative [[be]]
#* {{Q|la|Jerome|Vulgate|Proverbs 8:33|quote=Audīte disciplīnam et '''estōte''' sapientēs et nōlīte abicere eam.|trans=Hear instruction and '''be''' wise, and refuse it not.}}

