Page 5570 supersum: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{prefix|la|super|sum}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|supersum}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|irreg|supersum}}

# to be [[left over]]
# to [[survive]] (usually + [[Appendix:Glossary#dative case|dative]])
#: {{syn|la|vīvō|supervīvō}}
#: {{uxi|la|{{l|la|cladi}} '''superesse'''|t=to '''survive''' the disaster}}
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Titus Livius|Titus Livius]]|[[w:Ab Urbe Condita Libri|Ab Urbe Condita]]|I, 1|quote=Nihil praeter arma et naves '''superesset'''|t=Had nothing '''survived''' but their swords and ships}}
# to be  in [[abundance]], to [[abound]]
#: {{syn|la|abundō|flōreō|niteō|affluō|superfluō}}
#: {{ant|la|careō|egeō|dēsum|dēlinquō|deficiō|cessō}}
# to be [[superfluous]]
# to [[support]], [[advocate]] (for), [[defend]]

====Use====
Despite there being a passive for "to survive" in English, this verb is a completely active verb. Therefore, "to be survived" is expressed by reversing the subject and object.

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|irreg|supersum}}

