{{affix|la|sub-|sort=pilo}} + a {{m|la||-pīlō}} element as in {{m|la|compīlō||I rob, pillage, {{n-g|or}} steal from}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|la|subpīlō|suppeilō}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|1+|suppīlō}}

# {{lb|la|construed with the accusative of thing and dative of person}} to {{l|en|steal}} stealthily, to {{l|en|filch}}, to {{l|en|pilfer}}, to {{l|en|purloin}}
# {{lb|la|construed with the accusative of person}} to {{l|en|rob}} (someone) without being noticed, to {{l|en|strip}}, to {{l|en|pluck}}, to {{l|en|fleece}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{la-conj|1+|suppīlō}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|la|suppīlātrīx}} {{qual|New Latin}}
* {{l|la|suppilo|suppīlō²|pos=noun}}

====References====
* {{R:L&S|suppīlo (subp-)|suppilo}}
* {{R:Gaffiot|suppīlo (sub-)|p=1,523/2}}
* {{R:OLD|1|suppīlō¹ (subp-)|1,882/1}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{affix|la|suppilo|alt1=suppīlō¹|pos1=verb|-ō|pos2=suffix forming masculine agent nouns|id2=noun}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|la|subpīlō}}

====Noun====
