===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*ten-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*tenēō}}, stative from {{der|la|ine-pro|*ten-||to stretch, draw}}. See also {{cog|grc|τείνω}}, {{cog|fa|تنیدن|tr=tanidan||to weave}}, {{cog|sa|तनोति|tr=tanóti}} and {{cog|ang|þennan}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|teneō}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-teneo.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2|teneō|tenu|tent}}

# to [[hold]], [[have]]; to [[grasp]]
# to [[possess]], [[occupy]], [[control]]
# to [[watch]], [[guard]], [[maintain]], [[defend]]; to [[retain]], [[keep]]
# to [[reach]], [[attain]]; to [[gain]], [[acquire]], [[obtain]]
# to hold [[fast]], [[restrain]], [[detain]], [[check]], [[control]]; to [[bind]], [[fetter]]
# {{lb|la|reflexive}} to [[keep back]], [[remain]], [[stay]], hold position
# to [[know]], grasp, [[understand]], [[conceive]]
# to [[recollect]], [[retain]] [[knowledge]] of, [[remember]], [[bear in mind]]
# to [[insist]], [[uphold]]
# {{lb|la|of laws}} to be [[binding]] on; to bind, hold, [[obligate]]
# to [[arrive]] [[at]] [[a]] [[place]], [[reach]]
# to [[set]], [[fix]], [[hold]] on a fixed [[position]]
# to hold in [[prison]]
# to [[comprise]], [[contain]], [[include]], hold
# to hold someone's [[interest]], to be [[interesting]] {{q|to someone}}
#: {{ux|la|Hic liber me '''tenet'''.|This book interests me; I find this book interesting.}}
# to [[embrace]], [[hug]]

====Conjugation====
The supine form {{m|la||tenetum}} occurs only in compound verbs.
{{la-conj|2|teneō|tenu|tent}}

