{{root|la|ine-pro|*terh₁-}}
From {{inh|la|ine-pro|*terh₁-||to rub, rub by twisting, twist, turn}}.

See also {{cog|sco|thraw||to twist, turn, throw}}, Dutch {{m|nl|draaien||to turn}}, {{cog|nds|draien}}, {{m|nds|dreien||to turn (in a lathe)}}, German {{m|de|drehen||to turn}}, {{cog|da|dreje||to turn}}, {{cog|sv|dreja||to turn}}, {{cog|sq|dredh||to turn, twist, tremble}}, Russian {{m|ru|тереть||to rub}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|terō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|terō|trīv|trīt}}

# to [[rub]] or [[triturate]]
# to [[wear away]] or [[wear out]], [[consume]]
#: {{syn|la|hauriō|exhauriō|absūmō|cōnsūmō|dēterō|abūtor|conterō|atterō|tenuō|eneco|adedō|perago|accīdō|effundo}}
# to [[tread]]
# {{lb|la|time}} to [[pass]], [[spend]]
#: {{syn|la|dēgō|cōnsūmō|trānsmittō|tollō|eximō|trādūcō|agō}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|terō|trīv|trīt}}

