Page 5666 timeo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Presumably from {{der|la|ine-pro|*temH-}}. Perhaps cognate with {{m|la|tenebrae}}, {{l|la|tēmulentus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|timeō}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-timeo.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2|timeō|timu}}

# {{lb|la|transitive}} to [[fear]], be [[afraid]] of, [[apprehend]], be [[apprehensive]] of
#: {{syn|la|metuō|trepidō}}
#* {{Q|la|Publilius Syrus|Sententiae|quote=Stultum est '''timere''', quod vitare non potest.|trans=Fearing what cannot be avoided is foolish.}}
#* A phrase generally attributed to [[w:en:Thomas Aquinas|Thomas Aquinas]].
#*: [[w:en:homo unius libri|Hominem unius libri '''timeo''']].
#*:: I '''fear''' the man of one book.
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|2|48|quote=[[w:en:Timeo Danaos et dona ferentes|Equo ne credite, Teucri! Quidquid id est, '''timeo''' Danaos et dona ferentes]].|trans=Do not trust the horse, Trojans! Whatever it is, I '''fear''' the Danaans and the gifts they are bearing.}}
# {{lb|la|intransitive}} to be [[afraid]], to [[fear]], to be [[apprehensive]]
#: {{syn|la|extimēscō|vereor}}

====Usage notes====
* The verb ''timeō'' is a [[w:en:Verbs of fearing|Latin verb of fearing]].

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|2|timeō|timu}}

