Page 5678 tollo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*telh₂-|id=bear}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*tolnō}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*tl̥néh₂ti|*tl̥néh₂ti ~ *tl̥nh₂énti}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*telh₂-||to bear, carry}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|la|tolerō||to bear, endure}}, {{m|la|tulī||I bore}}, {{m|la|lātus||borne}}, {{m|la|tellūs||earth that bears}}. The perfect and supine stems of ''tollo'' were prefixed with {{m|la|sub||beneath}} to distinguish them from the original forms {{m|la|tetulī}} and {{m|la|lātum}}, which had become [[suppletive]]ly attached to the conjugation of {{m|la|ferō||to bear}}.

Farther cognate with Ancient Greek {{m|grc|τλάντος||bearing, suffering}}, {{m|grc|τολμέω||to carry, bear}}, {{m|grc|τελαμών||broad strap for bearing something}}, {{m|grc|Ἄτλας||the ‘Bearer’ of Heaven}}, Lithuanian {{m|lt|tiltas||bridge}}, Sanskrit {{m|sa|तुला||balance}}, {{m|sa|तुलयति||lifts up, weighs}}, Old English {{m|ang|þolian||to endure}} (English {{m|en|thole}}), Old Armenian {{m|xcl|թողում||I allow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|tollō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|tollō|sustul|sublāt}}

# to [[raise]], [[lift up]], [[elevate]]
#: {{syn|la|levō|ēlevō|allevō|ērigō|excellō|ēvehō|scandō|efferō|sublīmō|surgō|ēdō}}
#: {{ant|la|dēiciō|abiciō}}
#* [[w:Vergil|Vergil]]. ''[[w:Aeneid|Aeneid]]''
#*: Clāmōrēs simul horrendōs ad sīdera '''tollit'''.
#*:: At the same time he '''raised''' horrible cries to the stars.
# to [[remove]], [[take away]], [[steal]], [[rob]]
#: {{syn|la|āmoveō|auferō|diripiō|rapiō|fraudō|corripiō|adimō|eripiō|rēmoveō|āvertō|dēmō|exhauriō|praedor|eximō|legō|agō|extorqueō}}
#:: Agnus Deī, quī '''tollis''' peccāta mundī, miserēre nōbīs.
#::: Lamb of God, you who '''takes away''' the sins of the world, have mercy on us.
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|In Verrem|i|17|45|quote=Noctū clam '''sustulit''' signa pulcherrima atque antīquissima.|year=70 BCE|trans='''He took away''' secretly by night the very beautiful and very ancient statues.}}
# to [[destroy]]
#: {{syn|la|ruīnō|occīdō|dēvāstō|ēvāstō|vāstō|perdō|dēstruō|dīruō|aboleō|exscindō|accīdō|populor|interimō|absūmō|impellō|sepeliō|perimō|trucīdō}}
#: {{ant|la|ēmendō|reficiō|reparō|corrigō|medeor}}
# to [[kill]]
#: {{syn|la|ēnecō|occīdō|interimō|cōnficiō|caedō|obtruncō|necō|percutiō|interficiō|trucīdō|perimō|sōpiō|peragō|dēiciō|iugulō|absūmō|cōnsūmō}}
# to [[cancel]], [[annul]], [[eliminate]], [[abolish]]
#: {{syn|la|abrogō|aboleō}}
# {{lb|la|of time}} to [[consume]], [[spend]], [[pass]]
#: {{syn|la|dēgō|terō|cōnsūmō|trānsmittō|eximō|trādūcō|agō}}
# to [[erect]], [[build]], [[construct]]
#: {{syn|la|fundō|condō|figō}}
# to [[spread]], [[disseminate]]
#: {{syn|la|effundō|fundō}}

