Page 5681 tono: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*tonaō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*(s)tenh₂-||to thunder}}, replacing the likely earlier form {{m|la|tonere||thunder}}. One of few Latin verbs (as {{m|la|domō}}) only classed in the 1st conj. by the action of sound laws.  Cognate with {{cog|non|Þórr||Thor}}, {{cog|en|thunder}}.

PIE root likely related to {{cog|ine-pro|*(s)ten-||to sigh, groan}}, {{cog|grc|στένω||to moan, sigh, groan}}, {{cog|de|stöhnen|t=to groan, moan}}, {{cog|ru|стена́ть|t=to moan, groan}}.

Different root and not demonstrably related to Proto-Indo-European {{m|ine-pro|*ten-||stretch}}, whence Ancient Greek {{m|grc|τείνω||to stretch}}, {{m|grc|τόνος||chord, tone, tension}} and (with an extension) Latin {{m|la|tendere||to stretch}}. Unrelated to Latin {{m|la|tonus||stretching, tone}}, a borrowing from Ancient Greek.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|tonō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1|tonō|tonu|tonit}}

# to [[thunder]]
# to speak [[thunderously]], [[make]] a [[loud]], [[thundering]] [[noise]]
#: {{syn|la|conclāmō|clāmō|vōcificō|vōciferor|clāmitō|inclāmō}}
# to [[resound]] like thunder

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1|tonō|tonu|tonit}}

====Derived terms====
