===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₁ews-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*ouzō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₁ews-||to burn}}, the same source as the second element of Proto-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*aimuzjǭ||ashes}}; see {{m|en|ember}}. Cognate with {{cog|grc|εὕω||to singe}}, {{cog|sa|ओषति|tr= óṣati||to burn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|ūrō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|ūrō|uss|ust}}

# to [[burn]], [[consume]], [[inflame]]
#: {{syn|la|īnflammō|flammō|cōnflagrō|flagrō|incendō|accendō|ārdeō|cremō|adoleō}}
#* {{Q|la|P. Vergilius Maro|Georgicon|1|77-79|quote='''Urit''' enim lini campum seges, '''urit''' avenae,<br
/>'''urunt''' Lethaeo perfusa papavera somno<br
/>|trans=The flax '''burns''' as the cornfield and so '''burns''' the oat<br
/>They '''burn''' the Lethe immerged in poppy sleep}}
# {{lb|la|figurative}} to be [[inflamed]] with [[love]] or [[lust]]
# {{lb|la|figurative}} to [[annoy]], to [[gall]], to [[vex]]
#: {{syn|la|fatīgō|turbō|perturbō|sollicitō|agitō|concitō|disturbō|irrītō|lacessō|stimulō|percieō|concieō|cieō|ēvertō|peragō|īnfestō|moveō|agō|angō|versō}}
#: {{ant|la|cōnsōlor}}
#* {{Q|la|{{w|Terence|Publius Terentius Afer}}|{{w|Eunuchus|The Eunuch}}|Act 2, Scene 2, line 42|year=~161 BCE|quote='''Uro''' hominem.|trans=I '''gall''' the fellow.}}
# {{lb|la|figurative}} to [[rage]], to [[ravage]]
#* {{Q|la|Titus Livius (Livy)|The History of Rome, Book 10|10|17|quote=haec eos in Etruria iactantes molientesque bellum domi Romanum '''urebat'''.|trans=While they were embroiled and struggling in Etruria the war in Roman houses '''raged'''}}

