Page 5838 valeo: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*h₂welh₁-|id=rule}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*walēō}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*h₂wl̥h₁éh₁yeti}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₂welh₁-||to rule, be strong}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|valeō|eccl=yes}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-valeo.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2+.nopass|valeō}}

# to be [[strong]], to have [[strength]], to have [[influence]], to have [[power]], to be [[powerful]], to [[avail]]
#: {{ant|la|langueō|languēscō|ēlanguēscō|senēscō}}
#* {{Q|la|[[w:Titus Livius|Titus Livius]]|[[w:Ab Urbe Condita Libri|Ab Urbe Condita]]|I, 30|quote= '''valuitque''' {{l|la|apud}} {{l|la|Veientes}} [...] {{l|la|pacta}} {{l|la|cum}} {{l|la|Romulo}} {{l|la|indutiarum}} {{l|la|fides}}|t=The truce of peace agreed upon with [[w:Romulus|Romulus]] '''had influence''' among the [[w:Veii|Veientes]].}}
# to be [[well]], [[healthy]], [[sound]]
#: {{ant|la|iaceō|aegrōtō|cubō}}
# to be [[worth]], to be of [[worth]]
# to be [[effectual]], be [[efficacious]], be of effect, be [[good]] for
#: {{syn|la|prōficiō|prōsum}}
#: {{ant|la|officiō}}
#* {{Q|la|Catullus|Carmina|116|5|thru=6|quote={{...}}hunc videō mihi nunc frūstrā sūmptum esse labōrem,<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Gellī, nec nostrās hīc '''valuisse''' precēs.|trans=I see now that this effort was undertaken by me in vain, Gellius, and that our prayers to this end '''were of''' no '''avail'''.|transyear=1894|transauthor=Leonard C. Smithers}}
# to be in [[force]], in [[effect]] {{gloss|said of laws}}
# to [[mean]], [[signify]] {{gloss|used of words or statements that have a certain ''force'' or ''power'' in meaning}}
# {{lb|la|Ecclesiastical Latin|Medieval Latin}} to [[can]]; to [[prevail]]
#: {{syn|la|polleo|possum|queō|praevaleō|vigeō}}
#: {{ant|la|nequeō}}
# {{lb|la|New Latin|rare}} to [[leave]]; to go away

====Usage notes====
The supine can be either {{m|la||valitūrum}} or {{m|la||valitum}}. Passive use is rarely attested.

