===Etymology===
From {{af|la|vēnum|*dere|t2=put/give}} meaning "give for sale." Compare {{m|la|vēneō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|vēndō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|vēndō|vēndid|vēndit}}

# to [[sell]], [[vend]]
#: {{syn|la|addīcō|dēferō}}
#: {{ant|la|emō|comparō|sūmō|coëmō}}

====Usage notes====
In Classical Latin, the only passive forms in use are the past participle {{m|la|vēnditus}} and the future participle {{m|la|vēndendus}}; the remaining forms were supplied by {{m|la|vēneō}}.

====Conjugation====
The passive forms are post-Classical.
