Page 5878 verifico: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*weh₁-|*dʰeh₁-}}
From {{compound|la|vērus|t1=true|faciō|t2=do, make}}, formed with the latter component as the [[causative]] suffix {{m|la|-ificō}}. First attested in the 5th century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|vērificō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1+|vērificō}}

# {{lb|la|Late Latin|Medieval Latin}} to [[present]] something as [[true]]
#* {{Q|la|Pope Leo I|De haeresi et historia Manichaeorum|55|year=lived ca. 400 - 461|quote=Non mirum ergo si quae exposuit Archelaus in laudatis Actis '''verificari''' potuerint, maxime quia, ut iam vidimus, Marcellus, sive Marcellinus, qui imperiali auctoritate Mesopotamiae provinciae rebus praeerat, utpote catholicus, fidei veritatis propagationisque in desiderio erat|t=It isn't surprising that they have been able to '''present, as true,''' what Archelaus elaborated upon in his much-praised ''Acta''. All the more so since, as noted, Marcellus, also known as Marcellinus, was in power with imperial authority in the province of Mesopotamia, and as a Roman Christian, he desired the truth and propagation of our faith.}}
#* {{Q|la|Boethius|Interpretatio Topicorum Aristotelis|64|year=lived 480 - 525 CE|quote=Non enim erit proprium, quod positum est esse proprium, ut quia de geometra non '''verificatur''' indeceptibilem esse ab oratione (nam decipitur geometer cum pseudographiam facit)|t=Therefore, what has been stated to be proper would not be proper, as, regarding the geometer, it would not '''be presented as true''' that he is not able to be deceived by an oration (as a geometer is deceived once he writes a false presentation)}}
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin}} to [[verify]], [[confirm]] the truth, confirm whether it is true
#* {{Q|la|Agnellus, sive Andreas Ravennatensis|Liber Pontificalis|106|notes=in Patrologia Latina|year=lived ca. 805 - ca. 846|quote=Id enim de Galla Theodosii senioris uxore secunda, quae brevi post nuptias in puerperio decedens, nec sua, nec viri potuit decennalia celebrare, seu tricennalia multiplicare, '''verificari''' haud potest.|t=This event of Galla, Theodosius the Elder's second wife, who allegedly passed away soon after her wedding in childbirth, and so could not do a 10-year celebration or even a 3-year one of hers or her husband's, can not at all '''be verified'''.}}
#* {{Q|la|Roger Bacon|Compendium studii theologiae|58|year=1292|notes=as cited in ''Dictionary of Medieval Latin from British Sources''|quote=Predicatum necessarium potest '''verificari''' de subjecto aliquo ente et de aliquo non ente|t=A ''necessary predicate'' can be '''verified''' (confirmed as true) whether a subject is an entity or a non-entity}}
# {{lb|la|Medieval Latin}} to [[aver]], [[prove]] or [[justify]] a plea (by [[jury]] or by [[record]]s)

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1+|vērificō}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|la|vērificātiō}}
* {{l|la|vērificābilis}}

====Descendants====
{{top2}}
