===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*wors-o-}}, ultimately from {{der|la|ine-pro|*wers-||to drag on the ground}}. 

Compare {{cog|hit|ts=warš|t=pluck, reap}}, {{cog|sq|zvarrë||drag on the ground}}, {{cog|grc|ἔρρω||to move slowly, limp}}, {{cog|non|vǫrr||stroke}}, {{cog|lv|vârsms||heap of corn, grain}}.<ref>“Indogermanisches Etymologisches Wörterbuch”, J. Pokorny, 1959, Bern : Francke </ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|verrō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|verrō|verr|vers}}

# to [[scrape]], [[sweep]] out or up, [[brush]], [[scour]], [[clean]] out
#: {{syn|la|dēverrō|converrō}}
# to [[sweep]] [[along]], [[drive]], [[impel]]
# to [[sweep]] [[away]], [[carry off]], [[take away]]
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|58-59|quote=Nī faciat, maria ac terrās caelumque profundum<br/>quippe ferant rapidī sēcum '''verrant'''que per aurās.|trans=''If [Aeolous] should not do [this], [protecting] seas and lands and the vast sky, undoubtedly the all-consuming [winds] would carry [everything] with them and '''sweep''' [it all] '''away''' through the emptiness.''<br/>(King Aeolus restrains stormwinds which otherwise would destroy the world. See: {{w|Aeolus (son of Hippotes)}}.)}}
# to [[cover]], [[hide]], [[conceal]]
#: {{syn|la|vēlō|dissimulō|occultō|indūcō|operiō|obnūbō|occulō|condō|recondō|obruō|adoperiō|nūbō|tegō|abscondō|abdō|cooperiō|obvolvō|comprimō|prōtegō|premō|opprimō|mergō}}
#: {{ant|la|adaperiō|aperiō|patefaciō}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|verrō|verr|vers}}

====Derived terms====
