===Etymology===
{{w|Pliny the Elder}} derives it from {{compound|la|ver|alt1=vēre|gloss1=in spring|pos1=ablative of time|agō|gloss2=to drive, lead}}, which has the appearance of a folk etymology; in particular, the medial ''-v-'' is unaccounted for. However, no other explanation is available.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|vervagō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|vervagō}}

# {{lb|la|transitive|hapax}} to [[plough]] land for the first time after it has lain [[fallow]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|3|vervagō}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|la|vervactum}}

===References===
* {{R:L&S}}
