Page 5897 veto: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|la|votō}}, {{m|la|votāre}}, from {{inh|it|itc-pro|*wotāō}}, from {{inh|it|ine-pro|*weth₂-||to say}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|vetō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|1|vetō|vetu|vetit}}

# to [[forbid]], [[prevent]], [[prohibit]]
#* {{Q|la|Virgil|Aeneid|1|39|quote=“Quippe '''vetor''' fātīs.”|trans=''“No doubt it '''is forbidden''' by the Fates.”<br/>(Juno seeks to destroy the Trojans despite the will of the Fates.)}}
#: {{syn|la|prohibeō|abdīcō}}
# to [[advise]] not to
#* {{Q|la|Marcus Tullius Cicero|Epistulae ad Atticum|year=1st c. BC|quote=Pragmatici homines omnibus historiis, praeceptis, versibus denique cavere iubent et '''vetant''' credere.|t=''Prudent men in all their histories, teachings and verse besides tell us to beware and '''advise''' us '''not to''' believe.''}}
# to [[oppose]], [[#English|veto]]
#: {{syn|la|oppōnō|adversor|obversor|refrāgor|recūsō|repugnō|restō|resistō|officiō|subsistō|dīvertō|resistō|obstō}}
#* '''1st century AD''', [[w:Seneca the Younger|Seneca Minor]], ''{{w|Troades (Seneca)|Troades}}'', line 334
#*: {{quote|la|Quod nōn '''vetat''' lēx, hoc vetat fierī pudor.
|translation=What law '''forbids''' not, decency '''forbids''' be done.}}

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|1|vetō|vetu|vetit}}

===Interjection===
{{la-interj|vetō}}

# to [[forbid]] it! to [[protest]]!

====Usage notes====
* Used in the Senate by tribunes to oppose objectionable measures.

