Page 5903 video: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*weyd-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*widēō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*weyd-||to know; see}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|videō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|2.p3inf|videō|vīd|vīs}}

# to [[see]], [[perceive]]; [[look]] (at)
#: {{syn|la|intueor|conspicor|tueor|vīsō|spectō|īnspectō|speciō|invīsō}}
#: {{uxi|la|'''Vides'''ne eum venire?|Do you '''see''' him coming?}}
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|In Catilinam|quote=Nihil agis, nihil moliris, nihil cogitas quod non ego non modo audiam sed etiam '''videam''' planeque sentiam.|trans=''You do nothing, you plan nothing, you think of nothing which I not only do not hear, but which I do not '''see''' and know every particular of.''}}
# to [[observe]], [[note]]
#: {{syn|la|observō|servō|cōnspiciō|spectō|cōnspicor|cū̆stōdiō|intueor|animadvertō}}
# to [[understand]], perceive, [[comprehend]]
#: {{syn|la|apprehendō|comprehendō|dēprehendō|accipiō|cognōscō|teneō|apīscor|capiō|complector|concipiō|excipiō|exaudiō}}
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|In Catilinam|quote=O tempora, o mores! Senatus haec intellegit, consul '''videt'''; hic tamen vivit. Vivit?|trans=''Shame on the age and on its principles! The senate is aware of these things; the consul '''sees''' them; and yet this man lives. Lives!''}}
# to look (at), [[consider]], [[reflect]] (upon)
#: {{syn|la|reflectō|ponderō|putō|pendō|perpendō|cōnsīderō|reputō|cōnsulō|cōnsultō|dēlīberō|replicō|dubitō|circumspiciō|trahō|versō}}
# to [[look out]] for, [[see to]], [[care for]], [[provide]], [[make]] [[sure]]
#: {{syn|la|cūrō|accūrō|prōcūrō|cū̆stōdiō|servō|cōnsulō|colō|cōnsultō|caveō|respiciō}}
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Tristia|1|101|quote=tantum nē noceās, dum vīs prōdesse, '''vidētō'''|trans='''''You be sure''' only [to] do no harm, as long as you have the power to be helpful''}}
# {{lb|la|passive}} to be [[regarded]], [[seem]], [[appear]]
#* {{Q|la|Cicero|On Friendship|98|quote=Virtute enim ipsa non tam multi praediti esse quam '''videri''' volunt|trans=For as to virtue itself, many want not so much as to be endowed with it as '''to seem''' so.}}
# {{lb|la|passive|used impersonally}} to seem [[proper]] or [[right]]

====Conjugation====
{{la-conj|2.p3inf|videō|vīd|vīs}}

