Page 5943 volo: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|la|2012|November|14}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|volō|eccl=yes}}
* {{audio|la|la-cls-volo.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*welh₁-}}
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*welō}}, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*welh₁-||to choose, to want}}. Cognate with {{cog|sa|वृणीते||to choose, prefer}}, {{cog|ang|willan||to will, wish, desire}}. More at {{l|en|will}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|la|voleō||Vulgar Latin}}

====Verb====
{{la-verb|irreg|volō}}

# {{senseid|la|wish}} to [[wish]], to [[please]]
#: {{ux|la|Tibi bene ex animō '''volō'''.|t=I '''wish''' you well with all my heart.}}
#: {{ux|la|Hanc rem pūblicam salvam esse '''volumus'''.|t=We '''wish''' this republic to be safe.}}
# {{senseid|la|want}} to [[want]]
#: {{ux|la|Quid '''vīs'''?|t=What do you '''want'''?}}
#: {{ux|la|[[nunc|Nunc]], ([[ego|ego]]) [[edere]] '''[[volō]]'''.|t=Now, I '''want''' to eat.}}
#* {{Q|la|Plautus|Captivi|618|url=http://www.ihaystack.com/authors/m/plautus_titus_maccius/00016564_amphitryo_asinaria_aulularia_bacchides_captivi_amphi/00016564_englishlatin_utf8_p043.htm|quote=Dō tibi operam, Aristophontēs, sī quid est quod mē '''velīs'''.|trans=I’m at your service, Aristophontes, if there’s anything you '''want''' of me.}}
# to [[mean]], to [[intend]]
#: Et dixit ad socerum, "Quid est quod facere '''voluisti'''?
#:: ''And he said to his father-in-law: "What is it that thou '''didst mean''' to do?"'' (KJV Bible, Genesis 29:25)
#: Quibus ad se accersitis rex ait: "Quidnam est hoc quod facere '''voluistis''' ut pueros servaretis?"
#:: ''And the king called for them, and said: "What is it that you '''meant''' to do, that you would save the men children?"'' (KJV Bible, Exodus 1:18)
# to be [[willing]], to [[consent]]
# to be [[going]] to, to [[intend]], to be about to, to be on the point of

=====Usage notes=====
{{m|la||Nōn velle}} is used in place of {{m|la|nōlō|nōlle}} in the second person present indicative active forms and the third person singular present indicative active.

=====Conjugation=====
While it does have third conjugation forms, this verb is irregular. In Romance, it was regularized into a second conjugation verb ''*voleō'' (present infinitive ''*volēre''), apparently based on the present participle ''volēns'' (that is probably inherited, like {{m|la|iēns}} from {{noncog|itc-pro|*jents}}, and also the model for the formation of the perfect ''voluī''), just like most forms of {{m|la|possum}} were regularized to fit a second conjugation stem *''potē-''. Its present infinitive, ''velle'', descends from the athematic infinitive form {{cog|itc-pro|*welō|*wel-zi}} (''*-zi'' being the source of the usual infinitive ending ''-re'' as well). The second person singular present form ''vīs'' is suppletive and belongs to the root {{cog|ine-pro|*weyh₁-|t=to strive after, pursue}}; the original form appears to be preserved as the conjunction ''vel'' (from Proto-Italic ''*wel-s'').
{{la-conj|irreg|volō}}

